{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates","id":1523773,"title":"WIR Pre-made Werewolf Character Templates","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-07T08:22:58-07:00","id":1523773,"title":"WIR Pre-made Werewolf Character Templates","content":"Following up the previous <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387573-wir-pre-made-vampire-character-templates#post1387573\">WIR Pre-made Vampire Character Templates</a> thread, I will now go back and look at the pregenerated characters from the original second edition Werewolf tribebooks.<br /> <br /> Starting with 1994 with <b>Black Furies</b>, written by Phil Brucato (with some additional advice and input from Judith A. McGlaughlin) and artwork by Ron Spencer. Brucato became best known as the long running Mage developer, and Spencer would go on to be one the signature artists for Werewolf. It's interesting to look at his art throughout the book. His style is one he clearly refined and improved upon over the next decade, but you can clearly see what would become his distinctive style in the full page chapter opening splash pages. The template character art is a little rougher around the edges, and I think he may be trying to do something similar to Josh Timbrook's art from the Vampire clanbooks, but I can't say for certain. <br /> <br /> (I actually am lucky enough to own an original copy of one of Spenser's pieces, the full page chapter opener he did for Mage's Dead Magic 2's Norse chapter. The reprinted work you see in the various White Wolf books really do not do justice to the incredible amount of detail work he puts into these things, including the inking which gives the original piece an almost three dimensional quality to it.)<br /> <br /> And something I'd sort of forgotten about before rereading these was that White Wolf got super heavy into the use of quotes, sometimes from films or books, but often from music. Sometimes these work. Other times they are such low hanging fruit or borderline out of place thanks to questionable context (or lack thereof). Thankfully, White Wolf really started to dial this back later in the decade. <br /> <br /> <b>Street Rat</b> (Homid Ragabash)<br /> <br /> So, starting out with the chorus line from &quot;Bad Reputation&quot; by Joan Jett &amp; The Blackhearts. There's that low hanging fruit I mentioned. Anyway, the character is an orphan and apparently a hunchback. She ran away from the orphanage at age 12 because the Priest was ... abusive. (That's as much as a I feel like saying on the subject.) She fell in with a gang of dangerous metal heads, but eventually had her First Change and was found by a member of her tribe. That tribe mate is now her much suffering Mentor who tries to get her to behave to some minor degree. I do like that sort of detail into the personal relationships behind Backgrounds. Roleplaying hints can be summed up as you have a lot of trust issues - especially with anything involving religion - and expect to be betrayed by everyone, but are afraid of being abandoned and alone, so you cover with a massive amount of bravado and bad attitude. I think that's interesting and you could get a lot of roleplaying mileage out of that. Equipment is a switchblade, 9mm handgun, leather jacket, flash powder, piano wire, and &quot;assorted tricks&quot;. <br /> Getting to the character sheet stats, things are a little off. Physicals are secondary, with a 2/4/2 split. Socials are tertiary, but we have them at 3/1/1. So at least one dot is missing. I guess I can go with an Appearance of 1 for a hunchback gutter punk who sleeps on the streets and probably doesn't put much thought into personal hygiene. Although I can't help but wonder if the hunchback thing is an afterthought to somehow justify that low Appearance rating. I'm guessing that the Manipulation is supposed to be a 2. Mentals are primary, with 3/2/5. Personally, I might've gone for 4/2/4, but whatever. Wits has a specialization of Paranoid, which makes sense. <br /> Talents are primary, with what appears to be six extra points spent here, for a total of 16 dots. Intimidation and Streetwise are both at 4, which totally fits this character. Brawl is 3, Alertness and Dodge are 2, and Subterfuge is 1. Skills are secondary, with a 4 in Melee (and a Knife specialization), a 2 in Firearms and Stealth, and 1 in Drive. Knowledges are tertiary with one extra dot, for Enigma and Occult at 2 and Law and Ritual at 1. I feel that dot in Law might've been better spent on something like Investigation, Linguistics, or Medicine, which feel like they'd be more useful when living on the streets. <br /> Backgrounds are 1 dot in Mentor and 2 dots in Allies, which in the character write up may have been meant to be Kinfolk. Then we have a Rage of 4, a Gnosis of 3, and a Willpower of 5. This appears to throw off the freebie point count, with 3 for the rage, 4 (two each) for the Gnosis, and 2 for WP. With the 8 for abilities, that makes 17 total. I think back in the early days, there was a tendency to just dump points into &quot;power stats&quot; like Rage and Gnosis, without giving any thought to how this might impact the character's personality or behavior. (Revised edition was a lot more careful about this.) I don't think this somewhat high level of primal fury is totally out of place with this character, but I think 3 might've been better, at least IMO. The Gnosis on the other hand, seems a little arbitrary. Nothing about this character indicates much of any sense of spirituality or self-reflection. (Given that Hunchback is one of the Metis deformities listed in the 2nd ed core book, I can't help but wonder if this character started out as a Metis and was later changed to a Homid. I'll also mention that the Hunchback Metis deformity also includes a penalty toward Dexterity and Social roles, but the write up doesn't mention that anywhere.)<br /> That artwork is ... interesting. It's maybe one of the roughest and ugliest things I've seen from Spenser. I again mention that it looks like he may be trying to do something similar to Timbrook. I think it works OK for the character though. It's a very rough looking female gutter punk of the early 90s. <br /> Overall, this character is OK. It isn't exactly my first thought for a Black Fury, which is often a good thing. However, I don't think there's really much here that says Black Fury. The write up flat out says that its only a matter of happenstance that she isn't a Bone Gnawer, and that's sort of more what she feels like. And I say that as one of the last people who'd ever really argue that &quot;concept X&quot; can only fit in &quot;tribe Y&quot;. But given how the tribe books only have five templates, one for each auspice, I feel like maybe they should strive to be a little more archetypical. (Honestly, I wish they'd gone with 10 templates like the Vampire books had, so you could do two of each Auspice, for one that's more archetypical and one more boundary breaking. Plus you can have more than a single Lupus and Metis.) Overall, I think it's a perfectly fine character. Just not the best character for this particular place, maybe. <br /> <br /> Anyway, that's part one. Next will be part two, with the Theurge and Philodox characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-07T16:08:27-07:00","id":1523795,"title":"","content":"Loved the vampire version of this thread, excited to see this thread grow!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-07T22:10:06-07:00","id":1523806,"title":"","content":"A street rat Black Fury is a perfectly acceptable concept, but as you say, it'd be better if there was something more distinctly Black Fury about her. It doesn't need to be her pre-Change origins, but something that came out as a result of her tutelage as a cub. Runaway street girls are particularly at risk of sexual abuse, and some comment about her providing protection to other female street kids would have moored her firmly in the Black Fury tradition (as well as explain her Allies listed in the sheet, although the background implies they are kinfolk). A &quot;Big Sister&quot; type person who looks after her &quot;little sisters&quot;.<br /> <br /> It also would have been better to integrate the Ragabash aspect into her background. What exactly does she do that is particularly Ragabash? She has a good selection of Gifts, and it would be nice to know how she would make use of them. Maybe she's acts as a scout and look out, and going back to what I said earlier, maybe her street kid allies help her with being look outs as well.<br /> <br /> Someone with a hunchback also isn't a bad concept. But if you're going with that, then the character needs to do something with it. It's just an odd comment to make, and then never refer to it again. Just as a reason why other kids made fun of her, well there's any other number of physical or mental or emotional reasons for that. She could have been a stutterer, had a lazy eye, was extremely covered in freckles, been extremely shy, or any other number of things that might have isolated her and made her a target. I also find it odd to mention she's a hunchback and then give her a Dexterity of 4, as I simply don't associate spinal disorders with being very dextrous. Maybe it's a slight hunchback? But if so, again why mention it at all?<br /> <br /> I agree with the comment on increasing Rage and Gnosis solely as power states, and neglecting to think what impact that should have on the character. But that was a common problem all throughout 1e/2e and to a degree even in Revised.<br /> <br /> Are you sure Ron Spencer is the artist on the templates? Although he is the only artist listed, I clearly see some artwork done by Dan Smith (recognizable by his signature of SMIF) in that first tribebook. So if WW failed to credit him, they might have failed to credit Joshua Timbrook too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-08T02:28:33-07:00","id":1523811,"title":"","content":"I love templates as a concept, since I was a wee 14 year old anime nerd finding WtA.<br /> <br /> However, I only saw the 1st ed tribebooks later in life so I got no strong attachment to any of them.<br /> <br /> I can, however, say this; A lot of the 1st ed. templates are trying to 'find' themselves still. The lore isn't as developed and ideas bounce around randomly. Also, the Get of Fenris ahroun template made me genuinely burst out laughing when I saw them.<br /> <br /> If I am being honest, only the theurge, galliard and ahroun really read 'Fury' to me. Black Furies are a tribe that needs to balance itself between their Rage, their caring nature and their mysticism. While the Fury ways of mysticism are unique to them, angry!Fury can end up sounding like Fenrir and caring!Fury like a Coggie. To balance this out, I've often made Furies into a tribe that is either radical women defender or a frightening witches throwing curses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-08T17:30:36-07:00","id":1523846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1523806#post1523806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A street rat Black Fury is a perfectly acceptable concept, but as you say, it'd be better if there was something more distinctly Black Fury about her. It doesn't need to be her pre-Change origins, but something that came out as a result of her tutelage as a cub. Runaway street girls are particularly at risk of sexual abuse, and some comment about her providing protection to other female street kids would have moored her firmly in the Black Fury tradition (as well as explain her Allies listed in the sheet, although the background implies they are kinfolk). A &quot;Big Sister&quot; type person who looks after her &quot;little sisters&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very much this. And likewise with the need to better integrate the fact that she's a Ragabash. As I said, there's nothing particularly bad about this character. But I think it needs some fine tuning to better represent both the tribe and the auspice. <br /> <br /> As for the art, I'm honestly not sure. I can't find Spencer's signature anywhere on them, and it really is quite different from even his chapter opening art in this book. And I'm pretty sure there are other pieces in the book that obviously aren't his either. I suspect this may be a case of various people being omitted from the credits for some reason. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-08T17:51:52-07:00","id":1523848,"title":"","content":"Cool idea. Since you're discussing the art, could you share a pic with each? I for instance only have the later Litanies of the Tribes for these, so I've never had the 1st Ed Black Fury book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-08T18:53:27-07:00","id":1523853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1523848#post1523848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool idea. Since you're discussing the art, could you share a pic with each? I for instance only have the later Litanies of the Tribes for these, so I've never had the 1st Ed Black Fury book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, I only have my original 30-year-old copy, and the spine and binding wouldn't survive any attempt to scan anything. I'm kind of surprised STV doesn't have tribe specific art packs (at least that I can see). I'll try to see if I can find anything online.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-10T14:44:31-07:00","id":1523924,"title":"","content":"So earlier today I got to thinking, in response to people\u2019s dissatisfaction to the sample character Black Fury Ragabash and it got me thinking, what would I describe as the archetypal Black Fury ragabash? I\u2019m also curious what other people\u2019s answer to that would be<br /> <br /> Heres my idea: <u>The Living Taboo</u> (Warborn, Ragabash, Black Fury)<br /> <br /> Born from the union of a Black Fury Garou mother and a male Garou, the product of this union is the Living Taboo, the only masc. Garou who Flying-Horse accepts into their tribe. Once it was practically unheard of for the warborn to survive their birth without being slain in hopes of absolving the taint of their birth, but Flying-Horse is the avenger of wrongs done against the primeval order and forswears the slayings - their daughters must see the culmination of their violations and must learn from it.<br /> <br /> The Living Taboo lives at the heart of the contradictions of the Black Fury tribe. The only masculine members allowed in a tribe governed by matriarchs, the Living Taboo is a testament to Furies who violate the ancient laws. Yet the Taboo must live as well. They are the only men allowed in the tribe, being absolved of the crimes of Man by the greater violation of their birth. The Living Taboo is uniquely positioned to be an outsider and to question the way of their tribe. Not necessarily as a masculine perspective, being sterile and raised within Black Fury society may well preclude this, but as a living testament to the greater scope of the Furies\u2019 duties. They are dedicated to not simply avenging the subjugation of the Mother by the Patriarch but to all other violations of the primordial laws - the defilement of sacred places, the turning of blood-kin against blood-kin, incestuous unions, etc. If the Furies are to be the avenger of the most primordial transgressions than the Living Taboo serves as a reminder to them that they must not allow themselves to become myopic in their visions.<br /> <br /> (Note 1: As readers can probably tell, this concept is linked with my perspective on the Black Furies as a tribe that their task is the avenging of violations against primordial laws, not just the Patriarch\u2019s Usurpation but all other violations. As inspiration you might look to something like the arguments of Clytemnestra or the Furies from the Orestaia)<br /> <br /> (Note 2: Another inspiration for this was the greater emphasis placed in first edition, in my opinion, of the nascent schism between the minority of masculine Furies and the rest of the tribe, embodied in the character of Spartacus - and of course his name is Spartacus, oh White Wolf\u2026 - and his insurrections against the leadership of the tribe)<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-10T14:49:35-07:00","id":1523926,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately, I can't find any copies of the art online. I can find a few of the revised book's templates, but none of the originals. <br /> <br /> I've mostly come to the conclusion that these are drawn by Josh Timbrook. The image on the back of the book (what I presume is Mari Cabrah) looks very much like his work, and looking at the other template images, they also seem very much in his style. <br /> <br /> Trying to describe the Street Rat image as best I can. A fairly disheveled and angry young woman, her hair shaved on one side and looking unwashed on the other. Her eyes and mouth seem almost too large for her face. Said eyes have this weird look to them, like she's high on something. Multiple piercings, mostly in the one visible ear, but also nose and under the lower lip. Spiked collar. An upside down cross hanging from her neck. A shirt that barely qualifies as rags, with part of her bra showing. A leather jacket that looks maybe a size too big. Jeans or leggings that are ripped and tattered. Holding a crow bar. And flipping the viewer off. As I said, it's very rough and ugly, even by Timbrook's standards. But it does fit the character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-10T16:26:32-07:00","id":1523928,"title":"","content":"And finally part 2.<br /> <br /> <b>Vagabond</b> (Homid Theurge)<br /> <br /> So this one starts with a quote from Kate Bush's &quot;Hounds of Love&quot;, which isn't a bad song. So this character is an outsider, &quot;with some wild passion no one could explain&quot;, who ran away from home at 15 to live by herself in the woods. And somehow didn't die of starvation or exposure. (I honestly can't help but wonder if Brucato was familiar with the story of Chris McCandless, a young man from suburban Virginia who decided to venture out into the Alaskan wilderness alone only to die there. His journal he left behind became the basis for a 1993 magazine article that was later expanded into a book, Into the Wild, which later became a film. It's a fascinatingly tragic story if anyone is interested.) Anyway, our character was found by a wolf pack whose alpha submitted to her. Later a Black Fury appeared and guided her through her first change. But instead of joining a Sept or Pack, she remains with the Kinfolk wolf pack that found her. <br /> The spirits speak to her, but she can't understand them (yet). She's described as unstable, having no social skills, and her powers of concentration needing work. But (!) she's also described as a a consummate scout, good in a scrap, and her years in the Wyld giving her insight into Gaia's mysteries. Keep that in mind when I get to the stats later. Though human born, she's &quot;more wolf than wolf&quot;, and prefers to be left alone (&quot;A true lone wolf.&quot;) She might join a pack at some point. <br /> Equipment is a survival knife and the clothes on her back. <br /> <br /> The image is of a wolf. That's it. It's a pretty nice image. That's about all I can say about it. <br /> <br /> Attributes have Physicals as primary, with an extra dot for a 3/3/5 spread, and a specialization of &quot;tough&quot; for Stamina. Socials are tertiary, with a spread of 1/1/4, and a specialization of &quot;wild&quot; for Appearance. Mentals are secondary, with 4/1/3, and a specialization of &quot;feral&quot; for Perception. <br /> Boy, that's a lot of 1s. I feel like if someone were writing such a character today, they'd specify that she was autistic or some other form of neuro-divergence. <br /> Abilities are a bit of a mess to be honest. We have 10 talent dots, 11 skill dots, and five knowledge dots. So, presuming talents are secondary with an extra dot from freebies, skills are missing at least two dots, and really missing four dots because two of those dots are raising their skills to 4 and have been bought with freebies as well. Talents are three dots each in Alertness, Athletics, and Primal Urge, and a single dot in Empathy. For skills, we have 4s in Stealth (Woodlands) and Survival (No Gear), 2 in Animal Ken, and 1 in Melee. Knowledges are 3 in Enigmas, and 1 each in Medicine and Occult. <br /> I feel like the Melee was just an afterthought here. And given that the No Gear specialization in Survival would be nullified by using the survival knife, it makes me think the character would be better without it. Especially if you used it to raise Animal Ken to 3 instead. Also, make Talents primary, so you can put a few dots in Brawl and Dodge to make good on the previous claim that she's &quot;pretty good in a scrap&quot;. <br /> Backgrounds put all three dots in Kinfolk, which makes sense given the wolf pack. I'm not sure why a character who has no social aptitude and shuns social interaction would have Persuasion as a gift, but when the only other option is Smell of Man, which feels even less fitting, I guess you go with what's available. Rage is 4, so I guess it is again just being used as a power stat. Gnosis is 2. Remember what I said earlier about years in the Wyld giving her an insight into Gaia's mysteries? Well, her Gnosis is lower than that of the angry gutter rat street punk. With the alterations to abilities I mentioned, you'd have some points to boost Gnosis to at least three. <br /> <br /> So, much like the Street Rat, I find myself thinking that this is a mostly good character (ability issues aside), but I'm not really feeling that it cries out Black Fury or Theurge. Honestly, if Werewolf had a version of Mage's Orphans (like the Ghost Wolves in Forsaken), this would feel like she should be one of those. And I'm not exactly sure how this really evokes Seeker of the Ways. If it was a Galliard, I could easily see it being the idea of Lover of the Ways as being completely absorbed with the Wyld, wolf-dom, and nature. But as a Theurge, it feels a little off. <br /> <br /> Anyway, that's the Black Fury Theurge. Next will be the Philodox. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-10T20:55:20-07:00","id":1523940,"title":"","content":"I'm in broad agreement with your assessment. Again, the core concept is fine, but needs tweaking to really make it feel like a Theurge or Black Fury. Some slight adjustments to character sheet would greatly improve it. Increase Gnosis at expense of Rage, and change Sense Wyrm for Spirit Speech. Emphasize the connection she feels with the wild. Reveal had she strong, primal dreams before she ran away, and that somehow gave her the instincts she needed to survive in the wilderness before her First Change. Or perhaps spend some Freebies in Past Life/Ancestors.<br /> <br /> The misfit outsider concepts fits the 1 in Charisma and Manipulation, but I don't think the 1 in Intelligence works. That's below average and makes her kind of a dunce, not just a social misfit. With her strong physicals, the concept becomes a slow witted beefcake of a woman, which is not what the text implies at all.<br /> <br /> I'd probably make her Talents Primary and Skills Secondary instead of vice versa as you suggested. It would give her some extra dots to put into Dodge and Brawl. I think the dot in Melee and very high Stealth and Survival was because the character had too many points here and needed to be put somewhere, and the concept restricted what made sense.<br /> <br /> Overall, it's a solid concept, but needs some work to elevate it as a Black Fury Theurge instead of generic Garou. It's certainly a concept a first time player can take and justify her involvement in a new chronicle with her friends.<br /> <br /> One thing I do like with both templates is that they lack Pure Breed. The true heritage of these characters are unknown. And to a degree, their involvement with the Black Furies is accidental. They might have been found by any tribe and indoctrinated in their ways instead of the ways of the Black Fury. Quarrels over Lost Cubs between tribes was a prominent theme in the early sourcebooks that was later forgotten in favor of Garou being from known lineages and growing up as a Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 10-11-2023, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-10T23:56:25-07:00","id":1523942,"title":"","content":"The text doesn't say she refused to join a pack or a sept, it says she refused to join a tribe. Whiiich makes her a ronin, not a Black Fury.<br /> <br /> The dot spread looks so utterly broken to me, especially the 4 in appearance. Were they going for a sexy wild woman here? In addition, unless it has changed between editions, she should have 5 dots to put in her backgrounds, not 3.<br /> <br /> I agree with Black Fox's suggestions above, as well.<br /> <br /> This character reads like my first WtA character, before I understood that brawl is for ALL hand-to-hand combat stuff, just not its namesake. I ESPECIALLY side-eye any theurge character who doesn't take Spirit Speech. Unless it is due to VERY STRONG backstory reasons, lacking spirit speech is like the garou saying to the spirits that they refuse to communicate with them on their level.<br /> <br /> Then there is the whole concept being essentially a loner. Which in a template makes little sense, since these are meant for group play. And with templates like these, I often feel having the loner be press-ganged to join a pack kind of defeats the purpose of the whole thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-11T00:21:31-07:00","id":1523943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1523942#post1523942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The text doesn't say she refused to join a pack or a sept, it says she refused to join a tribe. Whiiich makes her a ronin, not a Black Fury.<br /> <br /> The dot spread looks so utterly broken to me, especially the 4 in appearance. Were they going for a sexy wild woman here?</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost undoubtedly. Satyr did give Bastet Appearance bonuses or far lesser penalties in some forms, after all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In addition, unless it has changed between editions, she should have 5 dots to put in her backgrounds, not 3. </div> </div> </div>It has changed! 1e was extremely uneven with giving out Backgrounds. Some characters even had no Background dots and had to buy them with freebies if they wanted any.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-11T00:25:21-07:00","id":1523944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1523943#post1523943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It has changed! 1e was extremely uneven with giving out Backgrounds. Some characters even had no Background dots and had to buy them with freebies if they wanted any.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Wait, WHAT? How??","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-11T00:34:44-07:00","id":1523945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1523944#post1523944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...Wait, WHAT? How??</div> </div> </div> </div>Wildly different starting WP ratings, for one. Like, Little Brother and the Stargzers had some really high WP ratings back in the day, but few and highly restricted Background dots, whereas Fianna and Older Brother had WP of 2 and no restrictions on their 4 dots. Some Fera got it even worse; Rokea are the aforementioned group that, like the old school 1e Sabbat characters, got no initial Background dots. Mokole also had way lower starting WP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-11T11:41:51-07:00","id":1523955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1523944#post1523944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...Wait, WHAT? How??</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1e WtA corebook, the # of Backgrounds each character got was dependent on their Tribe. 2e corebook changed that to the standard 5 points. There were also a lot of restrictions in 1e that were not kept in 2e (the Get of Fenris, for example, could not buy Past Life; Stargazers could not buy Totem; and many others).<br /> <br /> The number of Backgrounds each tribe got in 1e is as follows:<br /> <br /> Black Furies - 3<br /> Bone Gnawers - 3<br /> Children of Gaia - 2<br /> Fianna - 4<br /> Get of Fenris - 4<br /> Glasswalkers - 4<br /> Red Talons - 4<br /> Shadow Lords - 4<br /> Silent Striders - 5<br /> Silver Fangs - 5<br /> Stargazers - 2<br /> Uktena - 4<br /> Wendigo - 2","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-11T12:34:48-07:00","id":1523960,"title":"","content":"I like the Vagabond and I can see her more as a theurge than I saw Street Rat as a Ragabash, although I don\u2019t feel like either were really perfect fits.<br /> <br /> When it comes to the archetypal Black Fury Theurge, my image has always been a sort of Verbena-like cthonic blood witch style character. A re-appropriation of witch aesthetics and motifs as a source of primordial energy which I think would really be in line 90s vibes.<br /> <br /> The ideas I get for BF Theurge is always stuff like a witch in deep woods or caves, harnessing primordial wyld spirits and various Fury-like spirits, and using them both to empower the rest of their tribe but also to unleash curses and karmic punishments upon those who have violated some primeval law or another.<br /> <br /> Also for some reason I think I\u2019ve always associated Theurge and Ahroun as being the most particularly Fury of the potential auspices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-11T12:36:40-07:00","id":1523961,"title":"","content":"Yeah. IIRC, Black Furies and possibly Bone Gnawers were actually released before the 2nd ed, and had the new Renown system in their character sheets, but were still using the old Background points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-11T14:32:08-07:00","id":1523967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1523942#post1523942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The dot spread looks so utterly broken to me, especially the 4 in appearance. Were they going for a sexy wild woman here? </div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly would've given her maybe a 2/1/3 spread in Socials, with her being kind of sheltered and not really &quot;getting&quot; some of the nuances of social interaction, but able to communicate in a straight forward way when she needed to. <br /> <br /> Looking ahead, I note that all the templates here are either Appearance 1 or Appearance 3+, this one being the highest of the bunch. I personally find that a tad weird for a book about a group who are specifically designed to call attention to and oppose a wide range of female related issues in society and history, given that one of said issues is how female characters in media often seem to be portrayed as either &quot;super hot&quot; or &quot;notably unattractive&quot;. While I totally get the idea of werewolves having this hot'n' sexy animal magnetism/primal athleticism thing going on, I also think there's plenty of room for your totally average looking Appearance 2 characters. Going forward with the other books, I'm probably going to pay attention to how the Appearance thing works itself out with male and female characters. <br /> <br /> I'll also mention that this is part of why I long ago switched to using the nWoD/CoD attribute spreads for my classic WoD games. In a case like this where you decide to make a character who is socially stunted, instead of being left having to dump dots into the leftover Appearance stat and ending up with cripplingly shy supermodel, you could instead have a character who can't communicate very well, but is at least very calm under pressure and emotionally solid (which would have gone a ways in helping better justify the origin story of surviving alone in the wilderness, at least IMO). <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-11T15:38:59-07:00","id":1523971,"title":"","content":"<b>Missionary </b>(Metis Philodox)<br /> <br /> So this one, like the previous two, begins with a quote from a song by a female artist. In this case, Tori Amos's <i>Crucify</i>. And it misquotes it. It's &quot;<i>spit</i> in their faces&quot;, not smash. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Our first Metis character. And also the first character who is presented as being part of a Camp, specifically the Order of Our Merciful Mother. Which is apparently presented in their write up in this book as being &quot;many of them Metis&quot;. So to a certain degree, I can't help but wonder if having your only Metis template be a member of said Camp is maybe not the best exercise in creativity. <br /> <br /> The Order has always gotten a bit of a mixed reaction from fans. Personally, I rather liked it, as it recognizes in its way the deep influence the Catholic Church's reverence for the Virgin Mary has had on how Western Civilization would view women. <br /> <br /> Anyway, our character is a Metis, and was apparently raised by a werewolf pack. She's had mystic visions of the Goddess since before her first change, and was exposed to Christianity by a sympathetic preacher. It doesn't say anything about if this preacher was a human, Kinfolk, or Garou. I feel like maybe that would be important, but maybe not. <br /> Her sense of compassion led her to start doing charity work overseas, and she's started to learn more about the human (and I presume not-so-human) sources of much of the misery she works against. While mostly peaceful and calm, she has her limits and will fight if necessary. <br /> <br /> She's described as having human allies as well as being followed by &quot;the Mother's spirit&quot;. I'll go ahead and mention that her Backgrounds are a 3 in Familiar Spirit. I want to say this was from the first edition Players Guide, but I don't have my copy handy to check. She has no dots in Allies. <br /> <br /> Her Metis weakness is Fragile Claws. This is also apparently from the Players Guide. It's also the same deformity as the Black Fury Metis character Iobe Fareye in Rage Across the Amazon. Apparently this character build opted for making her hulkingly big and strong to compensate for this. <br /> <br /> Her equipment is a jeep, medical supplies, and a flak jacket (size XXL!). Flak jackets were pretty much obsolete as body armor by the 80s, although the name sometimes still gets used to refer to more modern body armor. Actual flak jackets are actually meant to protect from shrapnel and aren't usually effective against bullets. I'm not really sure a werewolf would need one. <br /> <br /> The artwork isn't bad. A very tall, athletic, Plane Jane type, in the sort of clothing you'd expect an aid worker in the Third World to wear back then. The jacket looks like the same sort of old Army surplus jacket I used to wear in high school. (And that's not a flak jacket, btw.) Overall, it's a good image. Nothing all that fancy. But nothing about it is bad. <br /> <br /> As with the last one, Physical Attributes are primary, and we have an extra dot purchased with freebies, for a 5/3/3 spread. I don't really have a problem with this. It's an interesting dichotomy, with the character fitting the classic Gentle Giant archetype. Socials are tertiary, with a 3/2/1 spread. Our second with an Appearance of 1. And to be honest, I don't really see it reflected in the art. She looks completely average. I probably would've gone with a straight 2/2/2 myself. That leaves Mentals as secondary, with 3/3/2. Seems perfectly fine. <br /> <br /> Talents are secondary, with an extra dot, for Alertness 2, Brawl 4 (with a specialty in Wrestling), Empathy 2, and Primal Urge 2. Skills are primary, with Drive 3, Firearms 2, Leadership 3, Repair 1, Stealth 2, and Survival 2. Knowledge is tertiary with Linguistics 2 and Medicine 3. Overall, it's a fairly solid spread. I'm not sure Firearms really fit the character. Maybe spend that instead on another dot of Repair and a single dot in Melee?<br /> <br /> Rage is 5. Again, the power stat thing. From a revised standpoint, it feels too high. Gnosis is the natural 3 for Metis. Willpower is a whopping 7.<br /> <br /> Overall, this is - once again - not a bad character. But I'm not sure it's a great one either. I think it represents an importance facet of the tribe, in the idea of the feminine side of human religion, but I'm not entirely sold on this as the ideal Philodox. It's not that she's necessarily bad as a Half-Moon. But I can't help but wonder if it might work better as a Theurge or Ragabash, maybe?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-11T16:17:00-07:00","id":1523973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1523967#post1523967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I honestly would've given her maybe a 2/1/3 spread in Socials, with her being kind of sheltered and not really &quot;getting&quot; some of the nuances of social interaction, but able to communicate in a straight forward way when she needed to.<br /> <br /> Looking ahead, I note that all the templates here are either Appearance 1 or Appearance 3+, this one being the highest of the bunch. I personally find that a tad weird for a book about a group who are specifically designed to call attention to and oppose a wide range of female related issues in society and history, given that one of said issues is how female characters in media often seem to be portrayed as either &quot;super hot&quot; or &quot;notably unattractive&quot;. While I totally get the idea of werewolves having this hot'n' sexy animal magnetism/primal athleticism thing going on, I also think there's plenty of room for your totally average looking Appearance 2 characters. Going forward with the other books, I'm probably going to pay attention to how the Appearance thing works itself out with male and female characters.<br /> <br /> I'll also mention that this is part of why I long ago switched to using the nWoD/CoD attribute spreads for my classic WoD games. In a case like this where you decide to make a character who is socially stunted, instead of being left having to dump dots into the leftover Appearance stat and ending up with cripplingly shy supermodel, you could instead have a character who can't communicate very well, but is at least very calm under pressure and emotionally solid (which would have gone a ways in helping better justify the origin story of surviving alone in the wilderness, at least IMO).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The sample character from the 2e core went in another direction as a kind of social disaster - instead of putting all three dots in Appearance, they went into Charisma.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-11T16:24:36-07:00","id":1523974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1523967#post1523967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I honestly would've given her maybe a 2/1/3 spread in Socials, with her being kind of sheltered and not really &quot;getting&quot; some of the nuances of social interaction, but able to communicate in a straight forward way when she needed to.<br /> <br /> I'll also mention that this is part of why I long ago switched to using the nWoD/CoD attribute spreads for my classic WoD games. In a case like this where you decide to make a character who is socially stunted, instead of being left having to dump dots into the leftover Appearance stat and ending up with cripplingly shy supermodel, you could instead have a character who can't communicate very well, but is at least very calm under pressure and emotionally solid (which would have gone a ways in helping better justify the origin story of surviving alone in the wilderness, at least IMO).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, there's certain limitations with the Storyteller System character creation and having to put a certain number of dots in one area. Sometimes you just have to dump them into a stat that doesn't make sense. It's just a quirk of the system.<br /> <br /> Early Werewolf didn't have Merits and Flaws in the corebook. They were an optional part found in the Players Guide. If you used them and wanted to tone down the Appearance of this concept, you can probably keep Social at 3, put one dot in each of the Attributes, and then select Flaws like Shy, Soft-Hearted, Phobia, Absent-Minded, Naive, Gullible, etc. as appropriate.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-11T17:26:27-07:00","id":1523977,"title":"","content":"I think this is a case of a decent concept in theory, but not a very good execution.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1523971#post1523971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Order has always gotten a bit of a mixed reaction from fans. Personally, I rather liked it, as it recognizes in its way the deep influence the Catholic Church's reverence for the Virgin Mary has had on how Western Civilization would view women.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the idea of the camp of the Order of the Merciful Mother. I can definitely see the appeal of the veneration of Mary in Catholicism, and how that might appeal to certain Black Furies. But this should be a legacy of the European Middle Ages. I can see this camp once having been dominant among Black Furies (in the Latin West at least) as it would have provided a convenient means for Black Furies to fit in. But this camp would have been declining for a very long time, certainly since the Protestant Reformation. For it to still be a thing, it has to be because of a persistent, but very small, group perpetuating it a sub-culture in the tribe. Probably because the Order has reconciled its belief in both Gaia and Abrahamic monotheism, and this belief is strong.<br /> <br /> Making such a group primarily Metis however, seems like a cheap way to give Metis their own thing. (aka &quot;We need to do something for the metis, so let's do that.&quot;) I don't think that makes sense UNLESS we assume the Black Fury tribe as a whole dump many of their metis onto the Order to raise, perhaps because there is some Catholic nun orphanage run by the Order of the Merciful Mother out there that is dedicated to raising them. Otherwise Metis being the bulk of a group based on a human religion is just bizarre. Homids would predominate. So I'm left with the idea that the Black Furies essentially send most of their metis to the order, and this is perhaps why it is tolerated by the Black Furies even now.<br /> <br /> We should probably assume that &quot;Order of the Merciful Mother&quot; is in fact an actual, but obscure, Catholic religious congregation or institute in the fictional World of Darkness that is solely comprised of Black Furies and their kinfolk exclusively. There are some Catholics that heavily promote Mary as the Co-Redemptrix, and this devotion strikes other Christians (and even other Catholics) as a bit heretical. I assume the Order of the Merciful Mother is very strong on such language and really emphasizes Mary as a figure near equal to Jesus. Maybe not quite heretical, but sometimes running close to it.<br /> <br /> So if I was every going to run a character (PC or NPC) as a member of the Order, that is how I would run it. The Christianity of such characters should be legitimate in the modern day, not just a cover. If it was just a cover, it would have been discarded long ago and no longer considered a camp, but at best some odd beliefs of some individual Garou likely in a few specific Black Fury kinfolk families. So there has to be some small villages somewhere in Europe and Latin America that is composed of Black Fury kinfolk that are strongly Catholic with a heavy dose of Marian veneration. And these villages have to be providing the backstory of new Black Fury homids who keep the Order alive while incorporating Metis dumped on them and the extremely rare convert.<br /> <br /> Familiar Spirit is indeed a new Background from the 1e Players Guide. It is basically a Spirit Ally with some aspects of Totem. At three dots, this spirit would be a Jaggling which she could speak to aloud. It can store give extra points of Rage, Gnosis, or Willpower (pick two). It always knows where she is and can she through her eyes as well as peek through the Umbra. For a roleplaying perspective, the ST and player probably need a long talk about what kind of spirit it is that fits this concept, as I don't think there are any canonical spirit that fits. Should it be more like an Enigmatic spirit or Epiphling? Maybe a nature spirit that evokes St Francis of Assisi preaching to the animals and the Wolf of Gubbio? This relationship is going to be very important to the character, but it still needs to be appropriate for this Gaian cosmology of the game.<br /> <br /> Like you, I would not spend Freebies on Rage and instead use it instead to boost some Abilities and Backgrounds needed to shore up the character concept. But otherwise I think it's a solid build mechanically. It's the lack of development of the Order of the Merciful Mother which is bad, especially in how they integrate their Christianity with Gaia beliefs. This really cannot be done in a Template, but required more detail earlier in the Tribebook. As such, this concept would be very hard for an inexperienced player to pull off. The weakest aspect is why this character is a Philodox. How is she a Keeper of the Ways? Is it that she is preserving the ways of this unique Catholic-Gaian syncretic belief and spreading her understanding of it to others (perhaps not in a sense of converting others, but demonstrating the wisdom of the Mother)? Something else?<br /> <br /> The character certainly is not any iconic idea of a Black Fury. But in terms of showing an example of a new camp introduced in the Tribebook, I think its acceptable. A problem however is that the Template description implies this character runs in a pack composed of other Black Furies of this order. Perfectly fine as an NPC concept. But if these templates are considered to be something the ST can hand over to a new player (someone's friend who just showed up and is interested in playing), this doesn't do that. The template should have some wording that sets up this character in some way being open to join a generic pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-11T19:39:15-07:00","id":1523986,"title":"","content":"I definitely like the ideas that Black Fox gave above re: the Order of the Merciful Mother and I think that the Missionary is fine as a concept and probably even worthwhile just for the convo on the Warborn &amp; the Order that she provokes, but I do agree that she doesn\u2019t read to me as the archetype of a Black Fury Philodox either.<br /> <br /> So like I\u2019ve done for the past few, I\u2019ll try to come up with what I would imagine as the stock example of a Black Fury Philodox and invite others to share their thoughts.<br /> <br /> The ideas which come to me is that, as a Philodox, more than any other auspice they\u2019re concerned with the precise ways in which people have violated taboos which justify a response from the Furies. The Philodox are the ones who keep track of all the various bans and taboos and teach them to the rest of the tribe, as well as previously established and acceptable means of response and punishment. (I actually think it might be interesting to have a tension between Philodox who believe in a by-the-book response to violations of taboo and BF Ragabash, Galliard, &amp; Ahroun who I can easily imagine as either trying to out-do one another with brutal and/or ironic punishments or alternatively just dishing out punishments with extreme prejudice). <br /> <br /> I also figure that the Philodox would probably be the main mediators of the tribe with the rest of the Nation and itself. I can easily imagine a lot of Furies in the modern nights getting into the dark-avenger tunnel vision whereas the orthodox BF might have a Greco-Roman style formula of restitution like \u201cbecause you have committed a mild trespass against this river-spirit, you must sacrifice a black goat in the spirit\u2019s honor\u201d rather than gutting them like a fish (although who knows, Garou are still Garou\u2026).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-12T00:06:27-07:00","id":1523991,"title":"","content":"As someone who plays a Black Fury Philodox Garou Born of this camp, this character doesn't really read as a Black Fury to me. Nevermind member of the Order.<br /> <br /> This character reads like a Children of Gaia Theurge and would be GREAT as one.<br /> <br /> As I said before, Black Furies are in constant danger of losing their flavour in both anger and caring side. This character is a prime example of one.<br /> <br /> The way I play my PC is by focusing on the darker aspects of Catholic mysticism and this sense of community, as well as the role of a Crone in Fury society. The philodox part showed through redemptive but harsh judgements. There is actually an interesting conflict between my PC and a Child of Gaia theurge garou born, as the latter is all for the Rite of the Pregnant mUle and my PC finds the rite EXTREMELY insulting as it makes mockery of motherhood.<br /> <br /> Basically, Furies don't have to be progressive in their thinking. Just women-first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-12T16:18:47-07:00","id":1524019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1523977#post1523977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But this camp would have been declining for a very long time, certainly since the Protestant Reformation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Devotion to Mary, Mother of Jesus is still a big part of Catholicism as well as Eastern and Oriental Orthodoxy, and to a lesser extent she's still venerated to a degree in Anglican and Lutheran denominations. As Maryam bint 'Imr\u0101n/Mary, daughter of Imr\u0101n, she has a place of distinction in Islam also. There's also a Kabbalism concept of Sophia as a female expression of God in a personification of Wisdom, and the theory of the Asherah (possibly the Sumerian fertility goddess) as Yahweh's &quot;wife&quot;. Baha'i apparently also uses certain female aspects of God, and the idea of a Heavenly Mother is part of some LDS doctrines.<br /> <br /> I could easily see the Camp having a presence throughout the Mediterranean, especially the more rural parts of Iberia, France, Italy, Greece, and the Balkans, as well as the Black Sea area and the Ukraine, parts of the Middle East, and in Mexico, the American Southwest, and Cuba. Also in places around New York or Chicago that have sizable ethnic populations from some of those areas.<br /> <br /> I think the Order can be an important part of the Tribe, showcasing the idea of Femininity/The Feminine Mystery/Womanhood in its most nurturing, protective, and healing aspects. From that direction, I do like this character. <br /> However, she doesn't really read &quot;Keeper of the Ways&quot;. Maybe if there was a stronger emphasis on her balancing the ideals of righteous judgment and merciful succor. <br /> I also really wish more thought had gone into her as a Metis. I think the idea of one of the &quot;sin-born&quot; finding a place of acceptance and peace through faith in a healing and merciful Goddess is a good one. But I don't feel this write up explores that aspect enough. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 10-12-2023, 07:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-12T18:20:15-07:00","id":1524024,"title":"","content":"<b>Warsinger</b> (Lupus Galliard)<br /> <br /> So, this one starts out with another song quote. But somewhat surprisingly, it's by Jethro Tull. I was honestly expecting another female artist. It would've made an interesting and appropriate theme, if nothing else. There's also a second quote from John Irving's <i>The Hotel New Hampshire. </i>I actually find this mildly annoying. The lay out for a template write up can only include so many words, about 500 IIRC. So, including an extra quote is effectively padding which wastes words that could be better spent on the actual character.<br /> <br /> That said, this is an interesting character. Born as a wolf, after undergoing the first change she decided that being human was much more fun and exciting. Especially human music. She taught herself to play guitar. Being a werewolf is one big party to her.<br /> <br /> It describes her as being &quot;trained as a witch&quot; and Rituals being her life blood. This is something I'll come back to in a bit. She may be part of the Moon-Daughters camp, but it's not exactly clear on that aspect.<br /> <br /> Her equipment, in addition to a trench knife and sawed-off shotgun, includes a &quot;serious collection of guitars, amps, and hard rock CDs.&quot; Now you may be asking yourself, &quot;Self, just how does a wolf-born Garou come to own a bunch of somewhat expensive musical instruments and equipment?&quot; And the answer to that is apparently that she has 2 dots in Resources. There's probably a really weird and potentially interesting backstory behind that. Unfortunately, absolutely nothing in this write up mentions it. I'll also mention that she has 4 dots in Performance with a specialization in &quot;Guitar&quot;. Lupus, of course, have restrictions on certain Skills and Knowledges they can use their basic points on, based on the idea that they'd have no way to learn them before their first change. Performance isn't one of those restricted Skills, but I sort of feel like specializing in &quot;Guitar&quot; is mildly violating the spirit of those restrictions. Likewise, I've always sort of wondered why Lupus didn't also have certain restrictions on some Backgrounds. Like, for example, Resources. So, all in all, this is just sort of a weird aspect of this character.<br /> <br /> The character image is really great. Probably my favorite of the bunch, to be honest. The same sort of early 90s GenX riot grrl archetype as the Street Rat, just as an attractive and hot wild child instead of an ugly and obnoxious gutter punk. She's wearing cut off shorts and a crop top, with tattoos (including one on her arm that's the tribe symbol that apparently turns into a dragon or something near the bottom). And holding a bloody knife. I like it quite a bit.<br /> <br /> Attributes have Physicals as secondary, and once again with an extra dot, for a 3/3/3 spread. Socials are primary, with a 4/3/3 spread. That leaves Mentals as tertiary, with a 1/2/3 spread. So she's meant to be kind of oblivious, I guess? The text doesn't really indicate anything about it.<br /> For Abilities, Talents are primary with an extra dot. Brawl, Expression, and Streetwise are 3 each, Alertness and Intimidation are 2 each, and Primal Urge is 1. (I always kind of wondered why Streetwise wasn't on the list of restricted abilities.) Skills are secondary with an extra dot. Besides that 4 in Performance, she has 2 each in Drive and Survival, and 1 each in Melee and Repair. Drive is one of the restricted skills for Lupus. (You'd think maybe Repair would be as well, but no.) Knowledge is tertiary, with 1 dot each in Enigmas and Occult, and 3 dots in ... Music? It's sort of penciled in at the very bottom of the official list of knowledges. Remember what I said earlier about the character being trained as a witch and loving Rituals. Well, she has no points in the Rituals knowledge. I feel those Music dots are a total waste and should've been spent to raise Rituals and Occult or Enigmas to 2. (Also, the character has a sawed-off shotgun, but no Firearms.)<br /> <br /> Backgrounds are 2 each in Contacts and Resources. Rage is 6, which seems mostly OK for this character. Gnosis is ... 3. Yeah, Lupus get that at 5 minimum. So, I've no idea what's going on here. Either a misprint or a mistake on the writer's part. But if the latter, then the Developer should've caught it during the redlining of the first draft. Willpower is also 6.<br /> <br /> Once again, I don't hate this character. It's actually pretty interesting. But I'm not sure it's the best example of a Black Fury, especially a Black Fury Lupus. Even with the Galliard aspect, I feel like this is stuck in a lot of the very early presentation of &quot;Galliard = Musician/Performer&quot;. Especially the whole rock guitarist thing. If this character had been one of the templates in Ways of the Wolf (a book I'll be getting to very soon), I think it would have fit better. Especially if it had been the Ragabash one.<br /> <br /> I also find it kind of bizarre that we have a Homid character who is &quot;more wolf than wolf&quot; and a Lupus character who wants to be a human. I honestly can't help but wonder if it'd been better if they'd been switched, with the Theurge being a Lupus and this one being a Homid.<br /> <br /> Next (hopefully tomorrow), the Ahroun, and some final thoughts.<br /> <br /> After that, I'm debating if I should do Bone Gnawers or Ways of the Wolf next.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 10-13-2023, 07:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-12T19:38:07-07:00","id":1524028,"title":"","content":"The Warsinger sounds pretty cool. I agree that there\u2019s some weird stuff here (What is this Lupus doing to get money? How are they doing shows with 4 Rage? Is this the best way to represent the Galliard tradition) but on the other hand it\u2019s also fucking rad? A wolf-born Garou who discovers Rock n\u2019Roll and becomes a riot-grrrl style performer? That\u2019s awesome and I like it. Some real peak 90s character writing.<br /> <br /> That said I do agree that I don\u2019t know if it\u2019s the best way to represent the idea of a BF Galliard, although I do think this one works as a cool character a new player could pick up and be \u201coooh yeah I want to do that\u201d. I def think she should be the inspiration for a signature character in the vein of Spooky Tooth or Baby Chorus. Plus it\u2019s definitely got the punk side of the Gothic-Punk motif.<br /> <br /> That said, what would the archetypal Black Fury Galliard look like?<br /> <br /> The two main ideas that come to me are the Mystic-Memory type and the Scab-Picker. The former is kind of taking inspiration from the ideas of muses, divine poets/poet-priests, and some oracle imagery - basically a mystical character whose function is to recall the sacred truths and to reiterate them to the tribe and deepen their understanding of the various taboos and laws which they uphold (and conversely why it is necessary to respond to violations of them). The latter I see as someone who\u2019s more interested in knowing precisely what violations were done and by who. They\u2019re the Galliards who remind the Furies of past trespasses in order to both remind them of why they fight and also to get them revved up in preparation of major action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-12T19:59:35-07:00","id":1524030,"title":"","content":"The Warsinger is actually my favorite template description in the Black Furies Tribebook. The character sheet not so much. Although I do believe it's important to have distinctions between homid and lupus Garou, I don't believe lupus characters must be prevented from embracing their homid form and interest and humanity any more than homid characters must be prevented from embracing their lupus form and the wilderness. I think the description straddles that edge well. There's a certain feralness about her behavior and look as a homid. A lupus Garou who embraces those aspects of the Wyld in her homid form through artistic expression is valid.<br /> <br /> The character sheet undermines that though. It's a case where someone's description of their character and their character build simply doesn't match. Your criticisms are all valid. But to be fair, I know a lot of players whose spoken character concept and character sheet don't really match. It's not an unusual problem.<br /> <br /> The specialization in guitar doesn't make sense for a concept called the war<i>singer</i> and a reference that her howl as a wolf could not be ignored. I normally don't like new characters, usually depicted as being older teen, having abilities that allow specialization. Lost cubs who only change as adults, and thus had time to develop their abilities, are different. But they are fine in certain circumstances. If the specialization was &quot;singing&quot; and not &quot;guitar&quot;, I would be happy.<br /> <br /> I'd remove her 2 dots in Drive and move them to Stealth and possibly Animal Ken. Her three dots in Music is wrong for all the reasons you mentioned. I think as a long term objective for this character to learn more about human music and musical theory is great. In fact, I think a lupus Garou with a beautiful howl becoming interested in her humanity because she's intrigued by human musical culture is a great idea. (Sidenote, while wolves generally have superior hearing to humans there is one big exception. Humans are great at identifying changes of pitch. We're almost unparalleled at that in the animal world. Most animals are terrible at that except bats. So I think it would be a good angle for this lupus to get into her homid form by really liking this one aspect where the human body is obviously superior to lupus form.) But as a brand new character, she shouldn't have three dots. She should just be starting her exploration of human music. As you mentioned, these would be much better put into Rituals with possibly one dot in Law, just to represent some knowledge of the Litany.<br /> <br /> Her backgrounds make no sense at all. Even with an abiding interest in her human half, I don't see how she gets Resources or Contacts. What is that supposed to represent? Being some kind of a busker? Rites would make a better pick once she has actual dots in Rituals. (Rites like Gathering for the Departed and Rite of Wounding would be especially appropriate - rites that can take advantage of her singing voice.) Outside that Backgrounds like Mentor (someone to teach her about human culture) or Fetish (Harmony Flute or one of the other musical fetishes) would be good.<br /> <br /> This is definitely a martial character so 6 Rage is fine. But once again, if an ST is going to take the Curse seriously, that likely prohibits any ability for this character to fit in with human society. That is not a dealbreaker. You can be a lupus Galliard and learn about human music through intermediaries, but it goes against the Backgrounds she has. And if the player wants to spend more time in the human world learning about her homid form and human society, it'd make better sense to keep Rage at 4. It just depends on the type of roleplay experience the player wants. Certainly the Freebies could be better spent on aligning the character sheet better to the description.<br /> <br /> Warfare and music have very strong ties. Soldiers have been singing as they march and go into battle forever. And music has been used a lot to communicate in battle, increase your side's morale, and decrease your opponent's morale. I would have stressed this in any concept called warsinger. Less MTV and more war chants (but there's no issue in her using more modern musical instruments to explore this new world). It would tie it in stronger with the Galliard aspect, and you could even incorporate the section on Howls in the corebook.<br /> <br /> I would vote for Ways of the Wolf next. The early books are very raw and present a society for the Garou that later books slowly (perhaps unintentionally) depart from. So I think doing Ways of the Wolf early is better than doing it later (like after all the tribebooks).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-13T07:59:10-07:00","id":1524042,"title":"","content":"Warsinger is one template that feels Fury ... until you look at the sheet. While I'm of the opinion that lupus characters are already punished enough for their Gnosis 5, there is a difference between having human contact and this.<br /> <br /> It is good to remember that no lupus, not even a Red Talon, starts the game as just a wolf. Rite of Passage and training make sure of that. But War Singer here is going against her own concept.<br /> <br /> But the wildness and the violence? Yeah that IS Fury. Black Furies are still a tribe of violence and bloody rituals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-13T18:32:00-07:00","id":1524056,"title":"","content":"<b>Radical</b> (Homid Ahroun)<br /> <br /> I guess at the end we finally get to the one that seems to hew to the most obvious tribal stereotype. Not that this is necessarily a bad thing. But it is kind of the equivalent to the Anarch Terrorist in the Brujah clanbook. <br /> <br /> This one starts out with a quote from Chairman Mao Tse-tung, perpetual favorite of radical chic intellectuals and head of one of the most murderous regimes of the 20th century. Also, ironically from a Werewolf perspective, a man who ordered his regime to essentially wage war against nature itself as part of the Great Leap Forward, causing massive environmental damage within China. And equally ironic from a Black Fury perspective, a man who kept hundreds if not thousands of women as concubines (read sex slaves), some as young as 12. I honestly consider the man to be human garbage on a number of levels. <br /> <br /> Anyway. <br /> <br /> This character killed her abusive father during her first change. (Only physically abusive, thankfully.) Her brothers apparently followed dad's example, so she grew up having to learn how to fight. Depressing, but certainly fitting for a Black Fury's backstory. <br /> She's a natural born leader, with a lot of inherent charisma and passion for her cause. She's pretty straight forward, what you see is what you get type character, and I think it works pretty well. It's simple, but strong and focused. <br /> It mentions that she has a fairly narrow world view, and specifically mentions that this is why her Perception is so low. I appreciate this little detail. It also mentions that she feels guilt over her family (I presume what happened during her first change, but possibly also other issues.) I like this, as it offers up a good avenue for future character development and growth. <br /> Her equipment is political literature, which makes sense; a camera, which feels a little random, but OK; and a light revolver, which also makes sense, I think. <br /> <br /> The art is of a very angry young woman in Glabro form. (Interestingly, her silhouette is used for the Glabro form stat adjustment block on the expanded character sheet.) It's a very good image, one that fits the character very well and feels very in keeping with the game. <br /> <br /> For Attributes, Physicals are secondary, with a 3/3/2 spread. Socials are primary, with 3/4/3. I kind of feel like maybe the 4 should be in Charisma instead of Manipulation. Mental is tertiary, with 1/3/2. The write up discusses the low Perception, which I think works well as an aspect of this character. <br /> <br /> With Abilities, it appears Talents are secondary with three extra dots. 3 each in Brawl and Expression. 2 each in Alertness and Intimidation. 1 each in Athletics and Subterfuge. Skills are primary, but one skill, Leadership, is at 4 (with a specialization in Speeches), and there's only the thirteen dots. There's also two freebies left unspent, so she seems to be missing a dot here. Etiquette is at 3, which feels slightly random, with Drive, Firearms, and Performance at 2 each. I'm not sure what the best place to put that missing dot. Knowledge is tertiary, with 2 dots in Law and 3 in Politics. I feel like this character might benefit from a dot in Medicine and/or Empathy, given how the write up describes how deep commitment to protecting women and children. <br /> Regarding the Skills, I sort of have this image in my head of her maybe being from an upper class family where everything seemed perfectly fine on the outside, but violent and dysfunctional on the inside. So in between an abusive home life, she was doing all the usually debutant type things like etiquette classes and piano lessons, with plans to go to one of the Ivy's for pre-law. There's nothing in the character write up to indicate any of this. I just think it would be an interesting thing for the character. <br /> <br /> Backgrounds are Allies 3, Contacts 2, and Kinfolk 1. This seems fine. Three of those are bought with freebies. I feel like maybe the Kinfolk is a little unnecessary. <br /> <br /> Rage is 6, Gnosis is 2, and Willpower is 4. That's the second lowest WP of the group. I feel like maybe that dot used in Kinfolk could've been better spent here. <br /> <br /> I rather like this character. Like I said, she's probably the most stereotypical representation of the tribe, but sometimes you need that and I think it works well. She's also a pretty good representation of her auspice, being able to both fight and lead. Overall, I think this is probably the strongest of the bunch. <br /> <br /> So, that's our collection of Black Furies. <br /> <br /> <i>Final Thoughts</i><br /> <br /> Overall, there aren't any bad ones here. However, while there's nothing really bad about any of them, a lot of them aren't all that great either. I think the Ahroun is the strongest of the group, especially when it comes to representing her auspice. The Galliard is a really fun character, but maybe not the best representation of her tribe or auspice. If we'd had 10 templates, with two of each auspice, I think she would've been a great &quot;outside the box&quot; example to contrast with a more archetypical counterpart. Similarly with the Vagabond and Missionary. <br /> <br /> With that in mind, something occurred to me about half way through this. So consider the following thought experiment: Shuffle around the auspices. Make the Street Rat the Ahroun, the the Vagabond the Philodox, the Missionary the Theurge, the Warsinger the Ragabash, and the Radical the Galliard. It's not entirely perfect, but I think if you did this, you would end up with five characters who all feel like they might be stronger representations of their Auspices. <br /> <br /> As far as alternate template ideas, I would mention the idea of a Freebooter Ragabash tomb raider, except that game and character didn't debut until 1996. I am however a little surprised that we don't have a Wiccan style character, especially given that Brucato was the Mage developer at the time. <br /> <br /> Next will be Ways of the Wolf. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-14T08:15:48-07:00","id":1524062,"title":"","content":"Found the art. I am pretty sure the premades are actual Timbrook pieces. There's a couple of other pieces in the book that are clearly not Ron Spencer, even though he's the only credited artist for the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-14T22:52:55-07:00","id":1524084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524056#post1524056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess at the end we finally get to the one that seems to hew to the most obvious tribal stereotype. Not that this is necessarily a bad thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Radical is my least favorite template of this tribebook. To me it goes beyond stereotype into self-parody. Some sort of ultra-feminist is often people's first impression of the Black Furies, and some sort of representation is expected. But the template description and character history is just awful. Not only did her father beat both his wife (and presumably his daughter although this is not stated), but her brothers also beat her. So the character already begins as caricature. Presumably no one becomes a feminist unless some man is beating her. You might as well have the Brujah skinhead experience actual harm as a result of Jews. Feminism shouldn't be about hatred of men. And while some feminists are undoubtedly misandrists in real life, it's cheap and lazy to portray your sole example of it in fiction. I don't think a female victim of abuse is a bad concept for a Black Fury (or indeed other tribes as well), but it should be handled with some amount of acumen. This doesn't.<br /> <br /> Her First Change leading her to kill her family and causing some amount of guilt is a good hook. Though I don't know why two Black Furies would automatically appear alongside her after it was over. How quickly newly changed Garou are found has always been nebulous, but this short interlude implies the Black Furies already knew about the physical abuse and did nothing. This could have been handled much better.<br /> <br /> The concept of a radical feminist, her skills involving Politics, Leadership, Expression, and Performance, and her Backgrounds of Allies and Contacts all imply a strong involvement in the human world. But that is undermined by her six points of Rage. 76% of humanity will be affected by the Curse. What kind of natural born leader can she be outside of the Garou? What exactly is she supposed to be leading? Some sort of feminist collective? A political group? Cult leader? What? Is that even possible given her Rage? This concept would be much stronger for a Philodox with much lower Rage, or her leadership talents oriented with the Garou with backgrounds in Totem, Fetish, or Rites.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, her lower Willpower than Rage creates all sorts of problems according to rules of the Beast Within. Although to be &quot;fair&quot;, the rules for Beast Within are ignored as much as those for the Curse are. But RAW she is losing two dice for all of her Social dice pools.<br /> <br /> Both the template description and character sheet are terrible in my opinion, although there are certainly elements that can be salvaged for a much better character. If I was the editor, I would have had the other templates reworked to various degrees, but I would have scrapped this entirely. On the plus side, I do like Josh Timbrook's character portrait. Perfectly cromulent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-15T00:15:33-07:00","id":1524085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524084#post1524084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Radical is my least favorite template of this tribebook. To me it goes beyond stereotype into self-parody. Some sort of ultra-feminist is often people's first impression of the Black Furies, and some sort of representation is expected. But the template description and character history is just awful. Not only did her father beat both his wife (and presumably his daughter although this is not stated), but her brothers also beat her. So the character already begins as caricature. Presumably no one becomes a feminist unless some man is beating her. You might as well have the Brujah skinhead experience actual harm as a result of Jews. Feminism shouldn't be about hatred of men. And while some feminists are undoubtedly misandrists in real life, it's cheap and lazy to portray your sole example of it in fiction. I don't think a female victim of abuse is a bad concept for a Black Fury (or indeed other tribes as well), but it should be handled with some amount of acumen. This doesn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you may be edging in on a false equivalence there. Also, if a character has to have the &quot;extreme violence&quot; background, the Ahroun makes a good first choice. You'll definitely want to vary it later on, but for the high default Rage character, it's probably fine. You're probably going to end up with some wide swing in likely character histories, anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Her First Change leading her to kill her family and causing some amount of guilt is a good hook. Though I don't know why two Black Furies would automatically appear alongside her after it was over. How quickly newly changed Garou are found has always been nebulous, but this short interlude implies the Black Furies already knew about the physical abuse and did nothing. This could have been handled much better. </div> </div> </div>The text only mentions killing her father during the change. Presumably, everyone else was out at the time, or at least far enough away that she couldn't rush over to them in frenzy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The concept of a radical feminist, her skills involving Politics, Leadership, Expression, and Performance, and her Backgrounds of Allies and Contacts all imply a strong involvement in the human world. But that is undermined by her six points of Rage. 76% of humanity will be affected by the Curse. What kind of natural born leader can she be outside of the Garou? What exactly is she supposed to be leading? Some sort of feminist collective? A political group? Cult leader? What? Is that even possible given her Rage? This concept would be much stronger for a Philodox with much lower Rage, or her leadership talents oriented with the Garou with backgrounds in Totem, Fetish, or Rites. </div> </div> </div>Politics, debates about what to do, and the need for planning are all found in Garou septs. Before the change, she might have led small ad hoc protest groups. Also, if you don't have enough freebies, you don't have enough freebies, and I've seen enough one-note Ahrouns to not complain when someone makes a well-rounded, socially adept one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Furthermore, her lower Willpower than Rage creates all sorts of problems according to rules of the Beast Within. Although to be &quot;fair&quot;, the rules for Beast Within are ignored as much as those for the Curse are. But RAW she is losing two dice for all of her Social dice pools.<br /> <br /> Both the template description and character sheet are terrible in my opinion, although there are certainly elements that can be salvaged for a much better character. If I was the editor, I would have had the other templates reworked to various degrees, but I would have scrapped this entirely. On the plus side, I do like Josh Timbrook's character portrait. Perfectly cromulent. </div> </div> </div>Growing pains. It was one of the first splat books, ever. Not everyone can be Dharma Book: Devil Tigers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-15T02:29:02-07:00","id":1524089,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it is good to remember TB:BFs was the first tribebook et all. A lot of the understanding how a character works was not known then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-15T13:14:38-07:00","id":1524116,"title":"","content":"Radio Free Asia-type screeds aside and however you feel about a particular political valence, Marxist Feminism is a well established tradition and it makes sense that a Black Fury might pick up on it and re: Mao in particular, the Chinese Red Army\u2019s innovations into Protracted People\u2019s War and Guerrilla tactics alone would make him worthy of study for any Garou, particularly an Ahroun. <br /> <br /> I like the Radical, I feel like she\u2019s a pretty solid and archetypal representation of what a Black Fury Ahroun could look like and I def think her backstory would be the type that some people drawn to the Furies would be interested in exploring (in my experience at any rate). I definitely feel there\u2019s places that it could be more developed and expanded upon but also you\u2019ve only got so much space and I think that they did the job pretty well. I think all the Black Fury sample characters have had interesting concepts but I think the Radical is the one most clearly suited to her Auspice &amp; Tribe.<br /> <br /> That said it gets me to thinking, what would the archetypal Black Fury Ahroun be and honestly I don\u2019t think this is far off. Furious Avengers who deeply feel the violations that have been caused and respond by unleashing a cleansing storm of violence. It\u2019s honestly not that far off from the archetypal image of a Garou in general. A few ways that I think a Black Fury Ahroun can stand out from the Full Moon\u2019s of other tribes (other than the aesthetics of the black-white fur, double-headed Minoan axes, and Scythian-style archery) is to have a particular clarity on the notion of the Fury as Terrible Avenger; someone who is supposed to lash out and respond to particular violations. I also imagine that BF Ahrouns could get particularly scary by leaning into the cthonic aesthtics and come off as hellish tormentors and primordial spirits of vengeance. Plus I do also think that a number of BF Furies getting into various human philosophies as ways to better understand the causes for their use of violence would make sense and fits with the RAW tradition of having intra-tribal debates among the Furies which reflect real world debates between schools of feminist thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-15T14:43:50-07:00","id":1524119,"title":"","content":"will you do mage too,eventually?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-15T15:05:24-07:00","id":1524120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524119#post1524119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">will you do mage too,eventually?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Probably shortly after finishing all of these. I'm not exactly sure how long that might take, but if I can get through 5 a week, that would be at least another 13 weeks (twelve more tribebooks plus Ways of the Wolf), plus additional time for things like WoD: Outcasts, Project: Twilight, Kinfolk, and possibly Rites of Passage. Which means Werewolf will take up at least the rest of the year.<br /> <br /> I'm debating about the breedbooks, because they stretched from the latter half of 2nd edition through the early Revised era. (One of the reasons I am unfortunately unlikely to do Changeling is because they go from 1st edition all the way to C20 and I don't think ever finished.) After Mage, I hope to do Vampire the Dark Ages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-17T19:46:19-07:00","id":1524211,"title":"","content":"So, setting the Wayback Machine to 1993, and one of Werewolf's earliest releases, <b>Ways of the Wolf</b>. This was the guide to Lupus/wolf-born, something that was a pretty good and useful idea for a game in which a large chunk of your PCs are from a completely non-human background. (Unfortunately, it would be several years til we got something comparable for Metis.) <br /> <br /> The book was written by Steve Crow, and the art is credited to Bryon Wackwitz and Dan Smith. However, both have very distinctive styles as well as noticeable signatures, both of which the template art lacks. Comparing with some other books, this appears to be Josh Timbrook, once again not being credited. I can imagine that this must have been a continuing annoyance for him. <br /> <br /> Because this is 1st ed, it uses a different Renown system, with scores in the hundreds. I'm rather glad 2nd ed decided to streamline this. Also, none of them have spent their Freebie Points. So I'm going to mention some thoughts about spending them. <br /> <br /> <b>Classic Trickster</b> (Wendigo Ragabash)<br /> <br /> So, no pop culture/media quotes for any of these. I'm almost a little surprised. <br /> <br /> No indication is given of the character's gender, so I'm just going to use &quot;they&quot;. <br /> <br /> Back in 1st ed, the No Moons were pretty heavily presented as tricksters/pranksters. So naturally this leans into that. They originate from the Mexican-American border region, one of the last few survivors of a pack. Between this and the fact that the Wendigo stronghold from Book of Caerns was in Arizona, I find it kind of interesting how much 1st ed material focused on the tribe in the region. (Still sad we never got a Rage Across Alaska book.) <br /> <br /> The character's sire, the other last survivor of their original group, was killed by a hunter's trap that they managed to avoid. You'd think this sort of loss might drive one to their First Change, but ... well, the writing is unclear. It just says that later a pair of Garou found them and guided them through their Rite of Initiation. Because of their &quot;Amerindian origins among the Wendigo tribe&quot; they look upon themselves as the personification of Coyote, and play the role of trickster to the fullest. They are are tolerated by their pack, but not well liked. <br /> <br /> I have mixed feelings about this sort of presentation of No Moons. I get the idea that trickster style characters are often a bit annoying to others, and I think 1st ed Ragabash sometimes ran the risk of veering into FishMalk territory. But looking elsewhere in the book, it seems to really double down on the &quot;Ragabash are considered the trash Auspice by all Lupus&quot; thing. In hindsight, I'm very glad that later material would go more toward the Questioner of the Ways concept and just what that could mean for different characters. <br /> <br /> It's mentioned that the character's Mentor is another Ragabash in their pack. That should probably say Sept, and I'll chalk it up to it being 1st ed and certain aspects of the setting and how things work still being hammered out. Also, the character's Allies are other Ragabash. I'm not entirely wild about that. There's nothing technically wrong with it, I guess. But I feel like it would've been a chance to do something much more interesting, like having some sort of minor trickster spirit as an ally. <br /> <br /> They character isn't a coward, but prefers to pick their fights, using stealth and cunning. It says this is unusual for a Lupus. I dislike this phrasing. Wolves pretty much survive via cunning and teamwork. Lupus characters should, IMO at least, be fairly straight forward and somewhat less complicated than Homids, but not to the point of being thick headed. <br /> <br /> No equipment is listed. <br /> <br /> The image is of a wolf. It looks fine. Although the apparently laughing look on its face might be a little much. <br /> <br /> With Attributes, Physicals are tertiary, with an even 2/2/2 spread. Socials are primary, with 4/4/2. And Mental is secondary, with 3/2/3. Even if it is a little stereotypical for a trickster character, I do appreciate seeing a Lupus with such high Socials. <br /> <br /> For Abilities, Talents are primary. We have a 3 in Dodge, 2 each in Primal Urge and Subterfuge, and 1 each in Alertness, Athletics, Brawl, Empathy, Expression, and Streetwise. Skills are secondary, with a 3 in Stealth, and 2 each in Animal Ken, Performance, and Survival. Knowledge is tertiary, with a 3 in Enigmas, and 1 each in Investigation and Rituals. <br /> This seems like a mostly solid spread of abilities. Obviously, you'd probably want to bump a few of them up with freebies. I'd probably like to have Alertness, Athletics, Brawl and perhaps Investigation up to 2. Maybe take Subterfuge up to 3 to further the trickster thing, and perhaps Dodge and Stealth to 4. <br /> <br /> Backgrounds are 1 each in Mentor and Allies, as detailed in the write up. This was back when Wendigo only got two background points to start. Thankfully that changed with 2nd ed. Personally, I'd go with Mentor 2 or 3 to represent an older Ragabash who has a position among whatever Sept the character's pack is associated with. As for the remaining points, there's a number of possibilities. I already mentioned the idea of some sort of minor trickster spirit having attached itself to the character (a raccoon or raven or or even Will o' the Wisp type thing perhaps). Past Life might also work. The book has an interesting fetish called a Tool Stick that a trickster could get up to all sorts of trouble with (especially if you decided to spend a couple of freebies on a dot in Repair). <br /> <br /> Rage, Gnosis, and Willpower are all the default for Auspice (1), Breed (5), and Tribe (5, it would be 4 in late editions). I might spend a dot or two on WP, but the rest are fine, even if the write up suggests raising Rage (again, this is when it was mainly a power stat and how it might impact role playing wasn't as bit a consideration). <br /> <br /> So, overall, this isn't a bad character. I do like seeing a Wendigo that isn't bitter and angry. But at the same time, it's kind of the lowest of low hanging fruit, and may be considered to lean a little into an ethnic stereotype. It's fine. Not bad; not great. Just OK. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-17T23:11:49-07:00","id":1524214,"title":"","content":"There are a lot of useful things in Ways of the Wolf, and whatever weaknesses this sourcebook has, I consider it one of the essential books for any WtA ST.<br /> <br /> This Ragabash template is very archetypical, but is so generic I lack any real enthusiasm for it. It does its auspice role OK, but the tribe could easily be changed out for any number of tribes. Not bad, but very indistinct. If given to a player, she'll need to derive any real personality for the character herself. That's much different from the PC templates included in Rite of Passage which has very distinct personalities. So it's not just a 1e issue.<br /> <br /> I think the description would have been stronger if they really dived into what a lupus Ragabash would be like versus a homid. The lupus aspect of it seems neglected in my mind. It just needs one strong hook and the template would be much stronger.<br /> <br /> Having another Garou as your Ally seems like a cheat to me. I would have made it a human Wendigo kinfolk of the area willing to teach the lupus Garou about humans and help her out. I don't know why none of these templates put points into Totem. In my experience with my game group, it's a popular Background. As a one dot Mentor, another Wendigo Ragabash is OK. But for more oomph, I might have made it an actual Nuwisha considering how the character views Coyote as a model. Otherwise the character sheet seems good to me.<br /> <br /> Incidentally at the time I don't think there were any wolves in the American Southwest. Across the border in Mexico, there were still some Mexican wolves. But I don't think the US F&amp;WS re-introduced Mexican wolves back into Arizona until several years later. But I could be wrong. Of course, in the WoD, there were still more wild wolves in various places according to the setting lore. So this isn't a mistake, just a conceit of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-18T03:40:13-07:00","id":1524219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524214#post1524214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are a lot of useful things in Ways of the Wolf, and whatever weaknesses this sourcebook has, I consider it one of the essential books for any WtA ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. I rather wish it had gotten a 2nd edition during the revised period. Something that was at least twice as big and went into more detail on all of its subjects (although perhaps splitting some of the general wilderness material into its own book focused on the wilderness as a game setting and how to run that).<br /> <br /> Incidentally, the first edition core book's mention of upcoming books lists this as Ways of the Wilderness, as well as another book, Ways of the City, that was supposed to talk about Homids. I presume there was probably also some sort of idea for a Ways of the Caern or the like that would have covered Metis.<br /> <br /> And yes, I think the biggest weakness of this template is how generic it is. While I think it's important to show Brown Puppies just as much as Pink Lizards, this may be the brownest of brown puppies to have ever browned. I think my own initial thought about a Wendigo Lupus Ragabash would be a character who doesn't exactly get the rest of the tribe's fixation on specific types of humans and their cultures, and keeps encouraging others to more strongly explore the wolf side of themselves and the tribe. At least that would probably be my starting point.<br /> <br /> As far as wolves in the Southwest, I think I have always just taken it as a given that the presence of werewolves means that there are hidden pockets of wolves scattered about in North America and Eurasia, as well as even smaller efforts to introduce controlled kinfolk breeding populations in places like Australia, Argentina, or South Africa (something Rage Across Australia did include). I feel this goes hand in hand (paw in paw?) with some of the things Ways of the Wolf mentions about the dividing line between &quot;civilization&quot; and wilderness being a bit more pronounced than the real world, and said wilderness being a bit deeper and more mysterious and impenetrable (more Gothic, if you will). But that's just me.<br /> <br /> Speaking of wolves in the Southwest, when I started reading this, the first thing to pop in my head was an old Disney film, Lobo, about a wolf in that region. It's a fun film, but you will probably never fully get the theme song out of your head.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-18T12:45:02-07:00","id":1524231,"title":"","content":"I get this idea also that in the early editions of the series there was this idea why the Ragabash would be the de facto Omega/Whipping Wolf of the pack (which may also be part of the Bone Gnawer-Ragabash connection that also gets made) but eventually some combination of learning about how the imperfections of those (in)famous wolf studies, how annoying it could be as a player to be the de facto \u201cyour friends have permission to shit on you now\u201d class, and the aforementioned risks of having a class be defined as Trickster/Prankster (an archetype so fundamental it should be represented but is unavoidably going to flirt with the excesses of FishMalk/Chaotic-Dumb behavior).<br /> <br /> I agree with those above, the Classic Trickster character is fine, but also kinda boring and uninspiring. Yeah there should be characters like this but it doesn\u2019t pop as a sample character. It also suffers from early edition confusion about what the Ragabash is/does.<br /> <br /> The question of how a Lupus Ragabash ought to be compared and contrasted with a Homid Ragabash is interesting though. Off the top of my head, the first classic notion is that the Lupus will simply not get the first premises of human society and will constantly be forcing homids to try to explain themselves (and therefore interrogate things they may accept as givens). I imagine older Lupus Ragabash might actually go so far as to take on ultra-human personas to further highlight the absurdities of human conventions, whether they do that in the most vulgar slapstick fashion or if they\u2019re painfully dry satirists.<br /> <br /> Other archetypes for the Lupus Ragabash might be the Garou who best seek to embody the wolf tactics which honor crazed humans might reject; stealth, stalking, ambush, overwhelming force, etc. and applying those fundamentals of hunting to other facets of Garou life. I do also think there ought to be room for Lupus Ragabash who do adopt the whelp/omega type social status and use their low rage and low standing as a means of giving their fellow Garou implicit permission to relax and concern themselves with unimportant matters (such as what happened to all of their shoelaces and what that has to do with the strange buzzing outside\u2026).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-18T20:18:34-07:00","id":1524254,"title":"","content":"<b>Dark Mystic</b> (Shadow Lord Theurge)<br /> <br /> This one was born to a small wolf pack eking out an existence in the Louisiana bayous. As I mentioned before, I have always just sort of taken it as a given that because of certain Garou efforts, there are small populations of wolves scattered about in hidden out of the way corners of places like the Rockies, the Adirondacks, the Scottish Highlands, and so forth. <br /> Also, I've always sort of had this impression that the North American Silver Fangs have tended to be more dominant along the East Coast, New England, the Midwest, and Great Lakes, as well as eastern Canada, while the Shadow Lords have tended to be more dominant in places like Mexico, the Southeast, the Southwest, and the West Coast. I suspect this template was part of the start of that idea. <br /> <br /> This was back when the Shadow Lords were presented as being fixated on acquiring power. (They were sort of the Werewolf equivalent to the Tremere, with the Silver Fangs as the Ventrue. Because the early WoD material tended to keep hitting a lot of the same notes.) This one is primarily interested in mystical and spiritual power, especially some of the forbidden secrets of the Wyrm so that they can be turned against it. <br /> <br /> This isn't a bad idea for a character. I can't help but wonder if this is where the idea of the Bringers of Light camp got its start. I think it even holds up with the later material where the tribe was more focused on the idea of ruthless pragmatism rather than just power for power's sake. <br /> <br /> The character won't yield to the Wyrm, but it does say that what it considers &quot;yielding&quot; and what its pack mates might consider &quot;yielding&quot; may not always agree. They're an outsider, even within their own pack. They're willing to sacrifice a pack mate &quot;for the greater good&quot;, but only as a last resort. <br /> I feel like this is maybe a smidge stereotypical for a Shadow Lord, but I think it can work well as a starting place, with the player getting to role-play the character's gradual growth and stronger integration into the pack, to the point where they're strongly loyal to them. <br /> <br /> Part of the write up is eaten up by a discussion of why the character has Talents as their primary abilities, as well as about their Backgrounds. The Background discussion doesn't bother me very much, but I feel like the Talents justification is word count that could've been better spent on something else. <br /> <br /> The image is another wolf, this one mostly darker colored and with a much more serious and grim look on its face. I rather like it. <br /> <br /> Physicals are secondary, with a 2/3/3 split. Socials are tertiary, all at 2. I do enjoy seeing a Shadow Lord who isn't socially focused. The write up does mention this, saying they prefer to use strength and cunning to overcome opposition. Mental is primary, with 3/3/4. <br /> <br /> For Abilities, Talents are primary. The write up acts like this is some sort of weird outlier for Theurges, saying that the character needs those abilities to maintain their fighting edge as a Garou and handle the political intricacies of the Shadow Lords. I find that justification unnecessary. Honestly, unless you are using secondary abilities, it's actually impossible for a Lupus to spend 13 points on Knowledge, as they've access to only four of those abilities, which would max out at three prior to spending freebies. I just sort of presume that most Lupus are going to have Talents or Skills as primary. <br /> Anyway, said Talents are 2 each in Brawl, Empathy, Intimidation, Primal Urge, and Subterfuge, and 1 each in Alertness, Athletics, and Expression. I'm maybe mildly surprised by the Empathy. It doesn't seem entirely keeping with the character as presented, but I think it does offer a potential avenue for the character growth arc I mentioned early. <br /> Skills are secondary, with 3 in Leadership, 2 each in Stealth and Survival, and 1 each in Animal Ken and Melee. I'm not sure that this high degree of Leadership fits with the way the character is described as an outsider who lurks on the edge of the pack. I'm also not entirely sure Melee is needed. Maybe raise Animal Ken to 2 and shift a point from Leadership into Stealth?<br /> Knowledge is tertiary, with 3 in Occult and 1 each in Enigmas and Rituals. That seems fine. Obviously, you'd want to raise Enigmas and Rituals a bit with Freebies. <br /> (Alternately, I think you could switch Skills and Knowledge, having those three Knowledges all at 3, and having the Skills be Stealth and Survival at 2 and either Animal Ken or Leadership at 1, and raising those with freebies later.)<br /> <br /> In 1st ed, Shadow Lords got four Background points. These have been allotted 1 each in Fetish, Past Life, Resources, and Rituals (what would thankfully be renamed Rites in 2nd ed so we didn't have a Background and Knowledge of the same name). According the the write up, the Resources are supposed to represent a small power base they've built up among mortals (Minor Quibble: that really should say &quot;humans&quot;, as &quot;mortals&quot; is the sort of term I'd expect to be used in a Vampire book). I'm left asking myself why? Nothing about this character indicates any sort of interest in human society or in acquiring power within it. If anything, this would seem to be a distraction from their primary focus on uncovering mystical power within the Umbra and among the spirits. I feel like this is here only because the character is a Shadow Lord and so is somehow expected to be involved in such things. <br /> The others are explained as &quot;the mystical powers you command as a Theurge.&quot; That's fine, but I feel like you would be better picking one or two to specialize in. The character has no equipment listed (none of them do), so I've no idea what Fetish this character might have. I'd honestly have gone with 2 each in Rituals/Rites and Past Life. Under 2nd ed rules, where you'd have five points, I'd probably put that last one in Rites. Alternately, I might could be sold on the idea of putting it into Contacts, to represent that the character has a single small inroad into the world of human mysticism that they've not been able to fully cultivate as much as they'd like.<br /> <br /> The rest of the stats are all as their defaults. Rage 2, Gnosis 5, and Willpower 3. I'd probably spent some freebies to raise WP to 5. <br /> <br /> So that is our Theurge. I mostly like this character. I think the concept is pretty good, and fits the Auspice and the Tribe, while also feeling like it has a good general Lupus mentality. However, I think it needs some tweaking with the stats, and would benefit from a cleaner write up (and some of the later material about its Tribe). <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-18T23:04:30-07:00","id":1524259,"title":"","content":"I like the Dark Mystic a lot. It's definitely a great Shadow Lord concept. But other than an image of a wolf, I'm not sure how much of a lupus character concept this is. It could easily be a homid of metis breed.<br /> <br /> Some type of flavor text evoking an actual lupus heritage would have been great. Maybe just as an animal being in awe of thunder storms, reacting to them in a more primal, mystical way than how a modern day human would react to weather phenomenon. Once you bring in a shamanistic point of view that is equally valid to a rational scientist, there is a lot to play with in the setting of WtA. Emphasize that pre-rational, pre-scientific point of view for lupus and within the context of the setting make it equally valid to what we as the readers consider as real.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-19T02:43:37-07:00","id":1524262,"title":"","content":"Yes, I think all of these suffer to one degree or another from this being so early in the game's run and no one entirely having a full handle on how to differentiate how Lupus think and view the world. I think the idea of ignoring material/political power in favor of mystical is a good start but needs at least another step or two to really be complete.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-19T05:28:26-07:00","id":1524268,"title":"","content":"Off-topic, but I love the teeny tiny Battle Scars section on the top of the sheet.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Dark Mystic looks good as a concept but has ENTIRELY ill-fitting stats. Even if Talents Primrary is just useful for most garou PCs, rituals 1 and enigmas 1 are pitiful for a theurge. Leadership 3 for a character that is an outcast makes no sense as does Animal Ken. Homids don't have to get Animal Ken to deal with other humans, so why should lupus get Animal Ken to deal with other wolves?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-19T09:12:19-07:00","id":1524279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524268#post1524268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Off-topic, but I love the teeny tiny Battle Scars section on the top of the sheet.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Dark Mystic looks good as a concept but has ENTIRELY ill-fitting stats. Even if Talents Primrary is just useful for most garou PCs, rituals 1 and enigmas 1 are pitiful for a theurge. Leadership 3 for a character that is an outcast makes no sense as does Animal Ken. Homids don't have to get Animal Ken to deal with other humans, so why should lupus get Animal Ken to deal with other wolves?</div> </div> </div> </div>I noticed the Battle Scars thing too. That really was one of the weirder choices of what to put there, as opposed to something like pack name or sept.<br /> <br /> None of these have had Freebie Points spent, so I presume the idea is two spend at least four of them to boost Rituals and Enigmas to 2 each. But like I said, I think it would be more economical to just make Knowledge secondary and have all three abilities at 3, then spend two points to boost one of those to 4. That also solves the Leadership issue, where you could just have those five dots spread between Stealth and Survival, and use freebies to even them out at 3 each. I think if you do that and better focus the Backgrounds, you end up with a character who is very strong in their chosen bailiwick while also useful as a scout and able to hold their own in a fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-19T13:18:56-07:00","id":1524284,"title":"","content":"The Dark Mystic sounds cool, I definitely see them as a solid example of a Shadow Lord Theurge and a good player-facing sample but I agree with others who said that it they don\u2019t quite see how the Dark Mystic needs to be a Lupus in particular with the write up it gets.<br /> <br /> Agreeing further with others I could definitely see a greater focus on a sort of primaeval mysticism that the Lupus are in contact with as worth exploration. After all even Animism is going to be developed by centuries of experience from a human perspective with the human premises of subsistence and survival. A Theurge who began life as a wolf, a creature with radically different premises, should view the mystical realm differently and perhaps with the Gnosis 5 that Lupus get their deserves to be some word-count dedicated to the Primaeval Mysticism that Lupus would be in touch with and how it differs from even the Animism of Human/Homid practices. Perhaps a Lupus Theurge can be differentiated from a Homid because they have an instinctual spiritual sense, they have lived fully as an animal without human mediation, and unlike Homids who must carefully observe relationships and customs the Lupus naturally knows it\u2019s position and relations.<br /> <br /> Of course there also would remain how to distinguish the Lupus Theurge in general and the Lupus Theurge Shadow Lord in particular. I like the suggestion that they feel a natural sensitivity for weather phenomena. Perhaps one could represent this by having LTSL be storm-whisperers or weather-whisperers who get some type of bonus to rolls having to do with comprehending the weather.<br /> <br /> Anyway all that aside I agree with what No One Said about the geographical vibe of the Shadow Lords, it does seem that they tended to get more of a Southern/Hispanic influence that was interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-19T13:37:41-07:00","id":1524285,"title":"","content":"One thing I just noticed is the relatively low Primal Urge (for lupus) in the templates in Ways of the Wolf. All are at 2 except for one template which is at 3. Since Primal Urge is pretty much the primary Ability a wolf needs to survive in the wilderness, 2 seems low to me. It pretty much acts as multiple Abilities as long as you are in wolf form. Each character has 2 or 3 dots in Survival which you only really need if you are in homid form and are trying to survive in that form. But any problem you have would best be solved by shifting into lupus form and using your Primal-Urge. Those points in Survival can then be spent on other things. A strong case can be made that Stealth and Alertness would also be covered. Only if you are in homid or glabro would you need to be using those other skills. I understand STs wouldn't want it to too useful, but wolves don't think rationally. They use their animal instincts, and in animal form this would work best. Without having to put points in Skill to get those, you can make Knowledges your Secondary and get more points in Garou specific knowledges like Enigmas, Rituals, possibly Law to represent the Litany, and the always popular Occult.<br /> <br /> I have a feeling those points put into Alertness, Stealth, and Survival are trying to cover functions that Primal-Urge would better cover those functions for one of the lupus breed. Most likely any dots in Animal Ken as well. You can argue against that in an urban setting heavy campaign where lupus may spend a lot of time in homid form and need to know a more human way of doing things, but this is in Ways of the Wolf and the templates are presumably for use in a wilderness oriented chronicle. Staying in lupus form would be the normal state, and you would only switch to homid in special circumstances.<br /> <br /> I would expect at least a 3 for all lupus and can easily justify lupus characters having a 4 or 5 at character creation. But perhaps that is just my perspective, and other players will disagree.<br /> <br /> I am also surprised we don't see more Kinfolk background where the tribe's human kinfolk are there to assist the lupus in fitting in among human society. That would make more sense than for the Dark Mystic than Resources. But I also notice that many players don't see the utility of the Kinfolk background, and I have always found it very useful for characters especially those who want to do things in the human world, but may be limited because of their Rage and the Curse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-19T14:25:38-07:00","id":1524287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524285#post1524285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I understand STs wouldn't want it to too useful, but wolves don't think rationally. They use their animal instincts, and in animal form this would work best.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since this is a bit of a personal bugbear for me (thanks to years of trying to convince people that playing lupus <i>doesn't </i>require you to have a master's in animal behaviour), while wolves don't think rationally lupus are no longer just wolves. Just like how homids are often rather feral compared to regular humans, lupus are not that bound to instincts anymore.<br /> <br /> This is actually something that gets used later in WtA, as Red Talons revised points out that Red Talons have to intentionally deny any sort of higher reasoning in an effort to try and be closer to wolves. And they still don't succeed because a tribe still needs its culture.<br /> <br /> To me, lupus need survival and stealth because their added reasoning basically overrides instinct at times. While I think any wild born lupus should have AT LEAST 3 in Primal-Urge, they also do things with much more intention than a regular wolf and at times might get lost in what-ifs. Especially for lupus of Shadow Lord persuasion, they'd be much more conscious of their action even to the detriment of their instincts.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-19T15:03:00-07:00","id":1524289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524285#post1524285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. I understand STs wouldn't want it to too useful, but wolves don't think rationally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither do humans. For instance, just wait a moment...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They use their animal instincts, and in animal form this would work best. </div> </div> </div>The human fixation on &quot;animal instincts&quot; doesn't hold up to rationality because instincts that are hard-coded into an animal require a lot of room in a genome - at least one gene per fixed action pattern, maybe more. So you usually only get a very limited number of behaviors that qualify. Simply just tossing every behavior, including learned behavior, into the &quot;animal instincts&quot; basket is a very bad habit of humans who learn it as doctrine from other humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-19T15:05:44-07:00","id":1524290,"title":"","content":"On a certain level, I sometimes wonder if Primal Urge should have been an ability as opposed to, say, an aspect of Gnosis or something. It sometimes feels like the equivalent of Vampire having a Beast ability or the like that was important for hunting, using Vitae to boost stats, and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-19T19:14:51-07:00","id":1524298,"title":"","content":"<b>Human Mediator </b>(Child of Gaia Philodox)<br /> <br /> So, two curious things about this one right off the bat. First is that this is the only one of these shown in human form, and because of that is the only one whose gender (female) is instantly recognizable. Second is that among the premade characters in Rite of Passage, that Philodox is also a female Child of Gaia (a Homid). I'm not exactly why this was a recurring thing. I admit that the Children of Gaia are a tribe that slots very easily into the &quot;balanced mediator&quot; role of the Auspice, but I do find it a little surprising creatively.<br /> <br /> She was taken from her mother at a young age by human &quot;researchers&quot; (no idea why it decided that needed to be in quotation marks), and ended up bonding with them. She was then taken away by another Garou around age two and underwent the First Change and induction into her tribe. She realized the reason she was so comfortable with humans is that she had the seed of humanity within her. (That's almost verbatim.)<br /> Because of her background, she is all in on her tribe's ideals of peaceful coexistence with humans, and seeks to take advantage of her ability to assume human form to approach, interact with, and hopefully educate humans about accepting Garou and healing Gaia.<br /> This was back when the idea of restarting the Impergium was thrown around a lot, and this character holds herself up as an alternative to that, feeling that her life shows that humans and wolves can live together.<br /> As a Half-Moon, she sees herself as an agent of balance, especially in resolving conflicts between Garou and humans (and it doesn't say this, but I presume also between Lupus and Homids as well). Her ideas about peaceful coexistence don't extend to the Wyrm, but she feels that Wyrm influenced humans should be converted and reeducated rather than automatically killed.<br /> <br /> The image is of a young female who looks about like you would expect for a circa 1993 GenX female outdoorsy type from the Pacific Northwest, Midwest, or Northeast to be dressed, complete with flannel shirt and jeans. Perfectly fine, and honestly wouldn't seem out of place if you saw it in an early Vampire or Mage book either.<br /> <br /> For Attributes, Physicals are tertiary, at 2/2/2. Socials are primary, with 4/4/2. I do kind of like the idea of a Child of Gaia with a high Manipulation trait. And, ironically compared with the later Black Furies book, we have a female character with an average appearance. Mental is secondary, with 3/2/3. All in all, I think this is a solid spread for a character like this.<br /> <br /> For Abilities, Talents are actually secondary. She has 2 each in Expression, Primal Urge, and Subterfuge, and 1 each in Brawl, Dodge, and Empathy. I think I might have moved a dot from Primal Urge to Empathy, as I think that might better fit this character's back story and concept. Skills are primary, with 3 each in Animal Ken, Leadership, and Performance, and 2 each in Stealth and Survival. Regarding Animal Ken, my read of the 1st and 2nd ed is that a lot of it is understanding how animals - including prey animals - think, and being able to predict and manipulate their behavior. So I can see wolves and Lupus getting some mileage out of this as a means of being better hunters and in understanding when some sort of potential danger has disturbed the local fauna. I'm not entirely sold on the idea of this character needing three dots in that skill. And like Primal Urge, given this character's back story, I could see a case for Survival only being a 1. I could also see a case for having Skills as secondary and Talents as primary, for a heavier focus on Empathy and Expression. Knowledge is tertiary, with 2 in Investigation and 1 each in Enigmas, Occult, and Rituals. I think maybe I would have dropped Occult and moved that dot into Enigmas or Rituals.<br /> <br /> Backgrounds are 1 each in Allies and Pure Breed. The Ally is supposed to be one of the researchers who raised her, who apparently may not know she's a werewolf. Under 2nd ed rules, I'd probably put another dot or two in Pure Breed. Maybe also one in Fetish, as I could see this character getting some good mileage out of a Harmony Flute.<br /> <br /> And, like the rest, we have the default traits for Rage (3), Gnosis (5), and Willpower (4).<br /> <br /> For freebies, I'd probably bump WP up a dot or two, and focus the rest on Abilities like Empathy, Expression, and Leadership, as well as maybe some Alertness and higher Dodge.<br /> <br /> Overall, I think this is a pretty good character. It's very simple and straightforward, but seems to be a decent representation of her Auspice and Tribe. I think the back story helps explain why this character is a lot different from the rest, including the fact that it's the only one presented in Homid form. I think the stats might benefit from some minor tweaks, but generally speaking, I like it just fine.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-19T19:42:40-07:00","id":1524300,"title":"","content":"I like the Human Mediator a lot, putting aside the mechanics I\u2019ve got no notes. It\u2019s a good way of depicting what a Lupus Philodox could look like and it pops in the context of the book as well. Perhaps being a Child of Gaia is somewhat stereotypical but this is so early in publication that it\u2019s less cliche and more lilebthe source of the cliche. All and all, I like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-19T21:00:17-07:00","id":1524306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524287#post1524287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since this is a bit of a personal bugbear for me (thanks to years of trying to convince people that playing lupus <i>doesn't </i>require you to have a master's in animal behaviour), while wolves don't think rationally lupus are no longer just wolves. Just like how homids are often rather feral compared to regular humans, lupus are not that bound to instincts anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't disagree with this at all. All I was saying is that if you are going to spend most of your time in lupus form, why not utilize the instincts you already possess? There's no problem with them utilizing their rational mind in homid form or even when appropriate in lupus form. At some point even in lupus form, a lupus breed Garou will want to use their Investigation or Science. But if Primal-Urge works as stealth while in lupus, why bother learning Stealth unless it is exclusively used when they are in another form where Primal-Urge won't work? It'll be a rare situation when an ST says a Garou in lupus form can't use Primal-Urge for Survival or Stealth, and need to use those actual skills.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-19T21:09:00-07:00","id":1524308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524298#post1524298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This was back when the idea of restarting the Impergium was thrown around a lot, and this character holds herself up as an alternative to that, feeling that her life shows that humans and wolves can live together.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was an early 1e idea that did not last long past the corebook and a few early supplements. Everyone eventually realized this was an extraordinarily stupid idea. The time when that could have worked had long since passed. Garou just don't have the numbers or power to impose the Impergium anymore against mankind whose population and industry gives it so much power. Wanting to return to the Impergium just made that character seem stupid.<br /> <br /> I do like the idea that certain tribes <i>regret</i> ending the Impergium, and now see it as a mistake. But that's different from wanting to reimpose it in a time where that will just fail disastrously. I think this longing for an earlier time could have been implemented differently. <br /> <br /> I'm sure some group of Red Talons are looking into some kind of major natural disaster that could reset the calendar in a way that would not harm Gaia. Let them consider how they can ignite the Yellowstone super volcano or something similar, or figure out a way to make fossil fuels inaccessible. Garou could conceivably pull off things like that. That's beyond the scale of Garou PCs to interact (to either thwart or support) with so I'm not surprised it's never mentioned. But as some kind of background conspiracy, it could have legs in the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-20T03:48:01-07:00","id":1524315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524308#post1524308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was an early 1e idea that did not last long past the corebook and a few early supplements. Everyone eventually realized this was an extraordinarily stupid idea. The time when that could have worked had long since passed. Garou just don't have the numbers or power to impose the Impergium anymore against mankind whose population and industry gives it so much power. Wanting to return to the Impergium just made that character seem stupid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Restarting the Impegrium being a BAD thing is an unofficial litmus test to see if you understand the setting. The first version of W5 spoke about a second impegrium, much to everyone's amusement.<br /> <br /> With the Impegrium, it is also good to remember that it PREDATES the Litany. The way garou are in any playable time period is different from the way they were during the Impegrium. Red Talons are for it more due to their recent situation than their historical one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-20T09:08:16-07:00","id":1524325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524315#post1524315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Restarting the Impegrium being a BAD thing is an unofficial litmus test to see if you understand the setting. The first version of W5 spoke about a second impegrium, much to everyone's amusement.<br /> <br /> With the Impegrium, it is also good to remember that it PREDATES the Litany. The way garou are in any playable time period is different from the way they were during the Impegrium. Red Talons are for it more due to their recent situation than their historical one.</div> </div> </div> </div>The narrator of the original Red Talons tribebook lamented that the new Impergium was already in place - but it was the humans practicing it on wolves and by extension the Garou. Quite frankly, that's better horror than a pointless double-sided track of &quot;maybe fashy&quot; and &quot;horribly distraught&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-20T11:06:03-07:00","id":1524329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524325#post1524325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The narrator of the original Red Talons tribebook lamented that the new Impergium was already in place - but it was the humans practicing it on wolves and by extension the Garou. Quite frankly, that's better horror than a pointless double-sided track of &quot;maybe fashy&quot; and &quot;horribly distraught&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of the reasons why every time I see people go &quot;Red Talons are only played by edgelords who want to play misanthropes and no ST wants THOSE in the game&quot; I know the person isn't really considering that Talons are desperate and they have good reasons of hating humanity. Aka, zero lupus PCs in those games, I'm sure.<br /> <br /> Mind, the Talons are at fault for refusing to help make the Litany and then bitching about it later. But garou should be able to be wolves without threats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-20T19:14:12-07:00","id":1524344,"title":"","content":"<b>Howler </b>(Fianna Galliard)<br /> <br /> So, 1st ed tended to present the Galliards as essentially Bards. And by that I mean D&amp;D Bards who are primarily focused on musical performances rather than actual Celtic Bards who are keepers of culture, lore, history, and knowledge. And this template certainly keeps with that. To the point where the term &quot;Howler&quot; is presented as some sort of Garou title for said bards. And, obviously, this was often the go-to Auspice for Fianna back in the early days, similarly to how Ahroun were for Get of Fenris.<br /> <br /> Anyway, this character was born to a small wolf pack in the eastern US. (Again, the idea that this must be the result of efforts by the Garou to preserve said breeding packs anywhere they can.) Far more interested in communicating via howls than their pack mates, their sire eventually returned from a long absence to reveal that they were a werewolf and took them off to become one of the Fianna. Now they wander the world, alone or with a pack, and eagerly howl their new discoveries to the Moon. A &quot;happy go lucky&quot; type, they seem to enjoy entering Homid form for the novelty of a new way of communicating.<br /> <br /> And that's about it. There's not a whole lot here. A vast amount of the word count seems to be eaten up with regurgitating basic info about what Fianna and Galliards are rather than who this character is and what they do.<br /> <br /> The image is a wolf in mid howl. It's a fine image. Just sort of unremarkable.<br /> <br /> For Attributes, Physicals are secondary, with 2/3/3. Socials are primary, naturally, with 4/3/3. And Mental is tertiary, with 2/2/2. I don't really have anything to say about this. It's fine. Nothing stands out, really.<br /> <br /> For Abilities, Talents are secondary. We have 2 each in Empathy and Primal Urge, and 1 each in Alertness, Athletics, Brawl, Dodge, and Expression. Skills are primary, with 3 each in Animal Ken, Performance, and Stealth, and 2 each in Leadership and Survival. Knowledge is tertiary, with a 2 in Enigmas and 1 each in Investigation, Occult, and Rituals.<br /> I feel he should have more points in Expression, even before freebies come in to play. I'm not sure if swapping Talents and Skills in regards to primary and secondary would help or not.<br /> <br /> For Backgrounds, we have 1 each in Allies, Kinfolk, Past Life, and Pure Breed. The write up explains the Ally as a fellow Galliard, likely a Homid from either their own tribe or another. I'm not sure why so many Allies in this book are just another Garou of the same Auspice. The Kinfolk are described as being of Irish decent. This book just seems to assume that any Lupus character's Kinfolk must be humans rather than wolves. I think this is one of those things where the earlier material was still trying to find its footing in certain areas. I think this could benefit from some focus. Perhaps a few dots of Kinfolk to represent their former pack. And the rest in either Past Life or Pure Breed.<br /> <br /> The defaults for the remaining starts are Rage 4, Gnosis 5, and Willpower 2. This was back when the Fianna got really hamstrung on WP. Thankfully 2nd edition would raise this to 3. Even then, the amount of Rage over WP is going to make interaction with humans difficult. Obviously, you'd probably want to throw a few freebies into the WP stat.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how I feel about this character. Possibly because, like I said, there's not a lot here. On the one hand, it's not a bad basic start of a concept. A Lupus who is really fascinated with verbal communication, both their own original howling and the new forms opened up via shapeshifting, is a potentially interesting idea. But I think this needs to be fleshed out a lot more. Spend less time repeating basic info from the core book's character creation chapter, and more talking about how they've tried to learn about and communicate with humans.<br /> I'm not sure how well this works as a Lover of the Ways, but like I said, this was back when Galliards seem to focus entirely on the Performance skill and not a lot else. I think if it talked about trying to express the feelings of wolves and a love of nature to humans and Homids, it would help. So, this character isn't terrible. But there doesn't seem to be enough meat on the bones to be good either.<br /> <br /> [I had a weird Mandela Effect with this template. For some weird reason, I have always remembered this as being called &quot;Moon Howler&quot;. But no, just Howler.]<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-20T22:58:34-07:00","id":1524348,"title":"","content":"Yes, the Howler template leaves a lot to be desired. It's like the first draft of a basic character concept before someone spends some time refining it and adding to it. &quot;I like to howl,&quot; just isn't that interesting of a character. It's an inferior version of the War Singer in the Black Furies tribebook - a lupus who likes to sing and discovers the capabilities of the human voice.<br /> <br /> As is, the desire to howl a lot is just a quirk, not a character. You need to do something more with it. The corebooks always have a section on howls, and it would be good to make some kind of reference to them. So besides the character's like of singing/howling, maybe you can do something to make him something of a herald or favored messenger between septs. Some references about the Anthem of War or Wail of Foreboding and the like could elevate the general concept.<br /> <br /> I think the Backgrounds are all wrong. A lupus in North America is likely descended from native wolf stock, not European which means the cub was simply seized when found with little birthright of the Fianna. So Pure Breed, Kinfolk, and Ancestors are mistakes. Even with the conceits of WtA, there just can't be many wolves from Ireland. And if you do want to go down that route, it should be an important part of the background, not an aside. There's no problem of some old Fianna lupus coming to North America and finding its own wolf pack to breed with, and this is that descendant, but if so that should be played up.<br /> <br /> Like the other templates in Ways of the Wolf, this is all very generic. The description and character sheet could be used for any tribe as is. This is probably because in 1e, tribal culture was essentially homid culture. Little thought was given about the totemic aspects of the tribe and how lupus characters - without any human culture - would be a child of Stag, Thunder, Falcon, Rat, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-21T00:35:10-07:00","id":1524350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524348#post1524348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Even with the conceits of WtA, there just can't be many wolves from Ireland.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a very strong suspicion that the idea is that these Kinfolk were intended to be humans. \ud83d\ude11","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-21T01:14:06-07:00","id":1524351,"title":"","content":"Looking at this character, two options come to mind;<br /> <br /> Either they are going through the stereotypes first. Or, even in this early book, they really have run out of ideas for lupus PCs.<br /> <br /> Generally, not a bad concept but not really anything interesting. You can get so much more out of Fianna Galliard than just 'likes to howl.' Or maybe the galliard could have been given to another tribe. Glass Walker or Bone Gnawer, maybe. Or Red Talon to depict a less typical take on them.<br /> <br /> As an off-topic, Ways of the Wolf annoys me so much when it just goes &quot;If you want to know what lupus think of the tribes, look at Red Talons tribebook.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-21T09:14:50-07:00","id":1524354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524351#post1524351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an off-topic, Ways of the Wolf annoys me so much when it just goes &quot;If you want to know what lupus think of the tribes, look at Red Talons tribebook.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. There are several parts of the book that are very, very thin. The section about Lupus and Auspices is a quarter of a single page, for example. (Although this is following the same lead as the 1st ed core book, which crammed the Auspice write ups in to a mere two pages.) Like I said earlier, we really would have benefited from having a much larger 2nd ed of this book during the same period we got 2nd eds of Umbra and Book of the Wyrm, which would have had the advantage of several years of setting development/refinement and not felt the need to include a Red Talons micro-tribebook. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-21T10:15:46-07:00","id":1524359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524354#post1524354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. There are several parts of the book that are very, very thin. The section about Lupus and Auspices is a quarter of a single page, for example. (Although this is following the same lead as the 1st ed core book, which crammed the Auspice write ups in to a mere two pages.) Like I said earlier, we really would have benefited from having a much larger 2nd ed of this book during the same period we got 2nd eds of Umbra and Book of the Wyrm, which would have had the advantage of several years of setting development/refinement and not felt the need to include a Red Talons micro-tribebook.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Quite honestly, my issues with Ways of the Wolf boil down to my experiences trying to play lupus in online games. It was presented as the book to play lupus. When I pointed out that it is outdated since alpha/omega is only in zoos, it got little response.<br /> <br /> I had hoped Changing Ways would pick up the slack but..nope. It made it WORSE.<br /> <br /> To explain this a little better; For literal decades, playing lupus has been basically considered something you needed to get a masters in animal behaviour to do 'right.' If you weren't told to basically play a lupus kin who could shift or any other 'punishments' for the 5 gnosis. Ways of the Wolf was used to justify this and why your lupus PC could NEVER learn to pass for a human if you even got to play one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-21T11:09:50-07:00","id":1524361,"title":"","content":"Yeah. My attitude has always been that Lupus should approach things differently than most Homids do, but not necessarily the same way an actual wolf would. Just as a Homid is going to think differently from a human because of the presence of Rage and Gnosis (and the level of anger and spiritual awareness that comes with them), a sudden exposure to heightened levels of sensory stimulation (especially smells and sounds), and so forth, a Lupus is going to make adjustments to having access to working hands and tool use, an understanding of abstract concepts and logic, alternate means of communication, etc. Actual wolf biology and behavior should be the starting place rather than the end result IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-21T16:44:02-07:00","id":1524375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524350#post1524350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a very strong suspicion that the idea is that these Kinfolk were intended to be humans. \ud83d\ude11</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not talking about the Kinfolk. The dots in Pure Breed and Past Life indicate the character has wolf ancestors of the Fianna. A cub adopted in the tribe wouldn't have those Backgrounds. But if the character is supposed to be a North American wolf, he wouldn't be.<br /> <br /> I don't necessarily view Kinfolk to mean they are related to the character, although I think that would be the most common. When it is only between one and five kinfolk, they could easily be assigned by other tribe members to help that character out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-22T04:08:03-07:00","id":1524383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524359#post1524359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Quite honestly, my issues with Ways of the Wolf boil down to my experiences trying to play lupus in online games. It was presented as the book to play lupus. When I pointed out that it is outdated since alpha/omega is only in zoos, it got little response.<br /> <br /> I had hoped Changing Ways would pick up the slack but..nope. It made it WORSE.<br /> <br /> To explain this a little better; For literal decades, playing lupus has been basically considered something you needed to get a masters in animal behaviour to do 'right.' If you weren't told to basically play a lupus kin who could shift or any other 'punishments' for the 5 gnosis. Ways of the Wolf was used to justify this and why your lupus PC could NEVER learn to pass for a human if you even got to play one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I loved playing Lupus characters as well and always bothered me that besides the expectation that your character needed to show off &quot;animal behavior&quot; was that the character ought to be child-like/naive or cave-man-like/simplistic in how they spoke or acted. Lupus-characters have a different perspective but they have human-level intelligence. I always thought it a bit unfair that it was totally acceptable as an idea that a Homid could figure out and adapt to the wolf-form with its different senses and instincts but Lupus not being overwhelmed or baffled by the human experience was somehow this thing that was hard to imagine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-22T12:04:26-07:00","id":1524393,"title":"","content":"I completely understand why people want to see a difference in the roleplay and backstory of a lupus PC versus a homid. Not only do you want that for the origin alone, but you want to avoid the twinks simply picking the breed to get the extra Gnosis. But that needs to include other concepts than just the equivalent of an alien being materializing on the Earth and learning about human society for the first time. Lupus characters have equal intelligence to humans, and have already gone through training as a cub to get that first rank of Cliath. They should know how things work and can fit into human society when the game begins. There are probably kinfolk families of every tribe except for the Red Talons that foster newly changed lupus cubs and help them adjust. But even the Red Talons likely have worked out a system where they know enough to not stick out like a sore thumb. That's why while you are initially limited in certain Abilities when you assign them, you can spend Freebies on anything.<br /> <br /> If someone does want to play a lupus PC where they are still naive and somewhat ignorant, that can work too. But that's the choice of the player, and they should likely take an appropriate flaw Naive, Gullible, or even Twisted Upbringing. Roleplaying some sort of ignorance can be useful. There should be lots of details or idiosyncracies lupus do not understand. But then again according to the setting, so should many homid Garou because they were pulled out of human society after puberty and spent the last three to five years learning as a cub, and their understanding of human society is less of an adult's and more like those of a pre-teen child. It's not unique to lupus or metis.<br /> <br /> Strangely in D&amp;D, people accept the idea of wolfweres being able to successfully disguise themselves as human beings all the time. So I've felt like if Harkon Lukas in Ravenloft can do it, why not lupus characters? Lupus characters are probably more &quot;fantasy&quot; based than &quot;animal&quot; based because you are combining elements together that do not occur in real life. It's just that you want that fantasy to fit into a setting of gothic horror in a similar world to the real world rather than a high fantasy one. The 1984 movie The Company Wolves has a lot of useful elements in that. I also find it good to steal a lot from books with anthropomized animal characters like Bambi and Watership Down. But that's just to build the foundation, not limit it to them.<br /> <br /> I generally look at the characters perspective and goals as a better indicator if they are &quot;doing&quot; a lupus right. If they are too anthropocentric, the character is probably better as a homid. But if they come from a more wilderness and wolf family centric, it is probably an acceptable lupus. You need to be an outsider to some degree when you are around humans. But being an outsider does not mean you aren't able to blend in, or are confused, or acts stupidly. It could just mean you feel isolated and unnerved. Or it could be you are curious and fascinated. Or resentful and suspicious. Or xenophobic and hostile. Or any other number of things.<br /> <br /> This kind of thing can be hard to describe in a character template which is probably why a lot of these in Ways of the Wolf seem weak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-22T12:19:03-07:00","id":1524394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524298#post1524298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">She was taken from her mother at a young age by human &quot;researchers&quot; (no idea why it decided that needed to be in quotation marks), and ended up bonding with them. She was then taken away by another Garou around age two and underwent the First Change and induction into her tribe. She realized the reason she was so comfortable with humans is that she had the seed of humanity within her. (That's almost verbatim.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this could have been improved if instead of going with kidnapped by humans and later rescued by Garou, it was more about the wolf was orphaned and she was adopted by a kinfolk run wolf rescue program that also performed such research. Having human kinfolk raising the wolf and gaining her trust before she changed would have been a nice twist, and then they could have turned her over to the Garou of their tribe. That way she could still feel the humans as her &quot;family&quot; and possibly even any other wolves at the camp who were later released.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524298#post1524298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Overall, I think this is a pretty good character. It's very simple and straightforward, but seems to be a decent representation of her Auspice and Tribe. I think the back story helps explain why this character is a lot different from the rest, including the fact that it's the only one presented in Homid form. I think the stats might benefit from some minor tweaks, but generally speaking, I like it just fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, but think it would have been better if it had been a different tribe and have her do a slightly different take. This is a character almost any new player of the game could come up with. It's so stereotypical. I think templates should show strong concepts that might not be immediately thought of by players. They are a good way to show the diversity of whatever group you are doing. Tribes that could be still appropriate for the concept, but put some spin on things would be Black Furies, Fianna, Glass Walkers, Silent Striders, or Stargazers IMO.<br /> <br /> But as we've said before, this is so new that people are still figuring out things in the game. I think when published in 1993 these might be the first templates ever. The writers are still trying to learn about their own game. We're talking now with the benefit of thirty years or experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-22T12:50:14-07:00","id":1524395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524393#post1524393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I completely understand why people want to see a difference in the roleplay and backstory of a lupus PC versus a homid. Not only do you want that for the origin alone, but you want to avoid the twinks simply picking the breed to get the extra Gnosis. But that needs to include other concepts than just the equivalent of an alien being materializing on the Earth and learning about human society for the first time. Lupus characters have equal intelligence to humans, and have already gone through training as a cub to get that first rank of Cliath. They should know how things work and can fit into human society when the game begins. There are probably kinfolk families of every tribe except for the Red Talons that foster newly changed lupus cubs and help them adjust. But even the Red Talons likely have worked out a system where they know enough to not stick out like a sore thumb. That's why while you are initially limited in certain Abilities when you assign them, you can spend Freebies on anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, hence why I call these punishments for the 5 gnosis; They are meant to make getting to play lupus and then playing lupus so hard people don't want to bother. That and/or some people don't like if lupus PCs are too 'doggy.'<br /> <br /> Honestly, it is silly when you really just need to point at Wolf's Rain and say 'that, do that.' It was never meant to be so utterly serious.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-22T13:25:55-07:00","id":1524396,"title":"","content":"Mechanically we already have the Ability-restrictions and Gnosis 5 during character-creation to represent a gap and difference compared to a Homid. But after that sky's the limit. And it isn't like you get a ton of hemming and hawing about the idea of Homid-characters getting five dots in Primal Urge or having more than five dots in Gnosis. And making Red Talons representative of Lupus-characters always felt wrong to me. Yeah, they are all about hating humans and being wolves but at the end of the day this is an ideology. It's not something intrinsic to being a Lupus-Garou. And mechanically you already got that: There's no rule against a Lupus-character having five dots in Computers or Drive. <br /> <br /> It's good to emphasize the differences in perspective between a Lupus and a Homid in order to roleplay such characters but personally, I'm always more in favor of giving players room to expand on these concepts rather than constrict them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-22T16:27:31-07:00","id":1524404,"title":"","content":"Rite(s) of Passage is the other 1st ed book that I really wish had gotten a 2nd ed/Revised revamp into a book about the process of going from the First Change to being a fully initiated member of a Tribe (ie, a starting player character) as opposed to an introductory adventure. <br /> <br /> Start with discussion of the First Change and how its circumstances can differ between each Breed, and cover how each one is taught to adapt to their new forms, to the existence of spirits and the Umbra, and the basics of the Litany. This would probably be when Lupus born Garou start to pick up any of Restricted Abilities they would buy with freebie points.<br /> Then once a new cub has done that, go through the process of learning and understanding about their Auspice, what it means, controlling their Rage, and their role in Garou society. And then finally their Tribal rite of passage and proving themselves to the Tribal Totem. <br /> <br /> Include the usual spread of five premade character templates, one for each Auspice, but don't give them a Tribe, leaving that for the player to select. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-22T17:59:55-07:00","id":1524408,"title":"","content":"<b>Wolf Warrior</b> (Red Talon Ahroun)<br /> <br /> And much like the previous entry, this is probably the most stereotypical Tribe for this Auspice (save, perhaps, the Get of Fenris, which is what the Lupus Ahroun character in Rite of Passage is). Not that it's necessarily bad. It just is what it is. <br /> <br /> Anyway, this character was born to a pack of &quot;powerful&quot; wolves. I'm guessing maybe that refers to the pack's size. It was lead by a Garou, and this character and one of its pack mates both underwent the First Change at about the same time. Their rite of passage was to kill a group of human hunters. It's a little vague, but one could make the case that this character may have eaten part of them and enjoyed doing so. This was a thing back in the early days of the game, with the Red Talons frequently presented as being by and large man-eaters. I think the idea of this, at least as a tribal-wide thing, started getting down played later on, especially once you had Camps within the Bone Gnawers and Silent Striders who were specifically singled out as being heavily Wyrm-tainted and corrupt for eating people and eating brains, respectively. <br /> <br /> The character prefers to remain in either wolf or Hispo/near-wolf form, but has moved among humans in homid form. What they've seen hasn't impressed them much nor has it improved their overall opinion of humanity. So, like a lot of the Red Talons at this stage in the game's development, they're wanting to bring back the Impergium, only really being held in check by the potential power of human weapons and the Veil. <br /> <br /> This write up leans heavily into the whole &quot;you must think like a wolf&quot; thing we've been discussing in the thread, relying primarily on instinct. They tolerate non-Lupus Garou but are a pretty staunch Lupus-supremacist. They're also largely devoid of social skills, being designed only as a killing machine. Like most of these, it suffers a bit from how limited the idea of the Auspices were in 1st ed. Ahroun were still pretty much &quot;they fight. And fight. And fight and fight and fight.&quot; The idea of them also having leadership abilities and being &quot;Protectors of the Ways&quot; would really start to develop with the 2nd ed. <br /> <br /> The image is of a wolf, all black save for what look like some ritual scar &quot;tattoos&quot; and a shock of white hair in its mane. It may be meant to be in Hispo form, but I'm not not 100% sure. It's not a bad image, all in all. <br /> <br /> For Attributes, Physicals are, of course, primary, with 4/3/3. Socials, as mentioned in the write up, are tertiary, with 2/2/2. This leaves Mental as secondary, with 4/2/2. Yeah, it's basically a Kill Machine.<br /> <br /> Abilities follow a similar pattern. Talents are primary, with 2 each in Alertness, Athletics, Brawl, Dodge, and Intimidation, and a 3 in Primal Urge. (Naturally, the Red Talon is the one with the highest rating in that talent out of all five.) Skills are secondary, with 3 each in Animal Ken, Stealth, and Survival. Again, this is prior to reorienting the Ahrouns toward leadership roles, but really the only thing making him a Kill Machine as opposed to the KillNinja trope I mentioned frequently in the Vampire thread is the lack of Melee and Firearms. Knowledge is tertiary, as it is for every character in this book (and admittedly, that makes a certain degree of sense with all the restricted abilities), with 2 each in Enigmas and Rituals, and 1 in Occult. I have to confess, this doesn't really feel like the sort of introspective character who would be big on Enigmas. I think maybe Investigation might've been more fitting. At the very least, it might tie in better with the mention that they've tried going out among humans, especially as this character has no social abilities outside of Intimidation. I'd probably spend a few Freebies on a dot in Subterfuge and at least one dot in Leadership if not more. <br /> <br /> Backgrounds are 1 each in Kinfolk and Past Lives, and 2 in Pure Breed. The Pure Breed makes a certain degree of sense, I think, given that the character is from a wolf pack that was lead by a Garou and had another pack mate who also changed. (No mention is made of what happened to the other. I think that might've made for some interesting character hooks and role play potential.) The Kinfolk are also the pack they grew up with. The Past Life represents the spirit of a powerful Ahroun. <br /> These seem sensible. Though if I were making this with the 2nd ed rules of five Background dots, I'd probably go with Kinfolk 3 (a ten member wolf pack) and Pure Breed 2 to start with. <br /> <br /> Rage, Gnosis, and Willpower are the defaults of 5, 5, and 3. It recommends raising WP with freebies, and I'd certainly do that. <br /> <br /> As with most of the characters in this book, this one isn't terrible. It's very basic. An Ahroun designed as a Kill Machine. I wish this had a little more depth to it. At least some sort of hook that pointed toward potential character growth. As it is, I think it's fine as something for a first time player to pick up and use. But it could be better, I think. <br /> <br /> So, that's Ways of the Wolf. Overall, these are mostly OK, but not spectacular. This was very early in the game line, when the nature of the Auspices were still being fleshed out, and when Lupus were still something new and slightly enigmatic even to the writers. <br /> <br /> I think the strongest one is the Human Mediator. I think she's the best representation of her Tribe and Auspice. Curiously, she's also the only one who's gender was actually defined. The rest are pretty nebulous on that front. The rest are all OK, but tend to lean heavily into their most basic Tribal and Auspice stereotypes but not a lot into why the character should be a Lupus as opposed to something else. The slight exception to that is the Wolf Warrior, but that feels like it's more a part of its Tribe than its Breed. <br /> <br /> Next I'm going to look at the premade characters from Rite of Passage, because I think some of them are actually pretty interesting. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-23T02:12:59-07:00","id":1524417,"title":"","content":"The Wolf-Warrior is a stereotype but as a template for a PC it needs a better hook, I think. The way the character is described he has already made up his mind about everything in the world and his interaction with the world is pretty one-dimensional in being this warrior-type. I also think while the character being this straightforward makes it easy to pick up the character and play it, I would imagine that whole shtick of this character would get old pretty quickly.<br /> <br /> Maybe make it about this character having a rivalry with the other Lupus Ahroun that underwent the First Change with him and they're competing for who can rise in the Ranks first. And the Wolf-Warrior struggles with the realization that in order to do that he has to work together with his Pack and other Homids while also having to engage in tactics and strategies he isn't used to. So should he insist on his wolf-supremacist thinking and potentially being a hindrance to the others or should he adapt for the sake of earning more Renown? Something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-23T11:36:02-07:00","id":1524432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524417#post1524417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe make it about this character having a rivalry with the other Lupus Ahroun that underwent the First Change with him and they're competing for who can rise in the Ranks first. And the Wolf-Warrior struggles with the realization that in order to do that he has to work together with his Pack and other Homids while also having to engage in tactics and strategies he isn't used to. So should he insist on his wolf-supremacist thinking and potentially being a hindrance to the others or should he adapt for the sake of earning more Renown? Something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given Ways of the Wolf assumes that lupus thinking=Red Talon thinking, I don't think they realised this. Which is sad, because one of the most interesting parts of being an ahroun is how that Rage 5 removes you from your mortal family. Wolf or humans. So Wolf Warrior would have to look at their family always from afar.<br /> <br /> The art of the template looks so odd compared to the rest of the art. Like the artist had changed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-23T14:21:25-07:00","id":1524436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524432#post1524432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given Ways of the Wolf assumes that lupus thinking=Red Talon thinking, I don't think they realised this. Which is sad, because one of the most interesting parts of being an ahroun is how that Rage 5 removes you from your mortal family. Wolf or humans. So Wolf Warrior would have to look at their family always from afar.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, Rage would also add another wrinkle to the character.<br /> <br /> One way where I also think Ways of the Wolf fails is that it doesn't take the Lupus-PC-question into consideration from a player/ST-perspective. It's all about setting and player-character-perspectives but there's very little on how to look at this from the perspective of players and STs playing a game. Especially with a character like the Wolf-Warrior who's a Red Talon that's this wolf-supremacist fanatic, you need an ST who's on board with this. And it probably would go over better with an ST if there were more to the character than them being a wolf-supremacist. But also the ST needs to accommodate such a character by weaving things like wolves in the wild, animal-rights or humans being shitty into the story. Because without that having this Red Talon character complain about humans and the human world every couple of minutes would just make them seem whiny and/or comical.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-23T15:07:44-07:00","id":1524439,"title":"","content":"A Red Talon tribal template is pretty much guaranteed in a lupus and wilderness focused sourcebook, but it should have been a non-obvious auspice. Showcasing what a Red Talon Ragabash or Theurge would have shown the diversity of the tribe more. But I wonder how much the creators really conceived of the Red Talons as a tribe that could be played by PCs in a mixed pack as opposed to one of the designated bad guys of the setting. Multiple things about the template seem like a bad stereotype. Not only does this character come off bad, even the humans mentioned in it are stereotypes. Very few hunters would ever attempt to hunt while drunk because of firearms safety issues. No one wants to risk killing a friend. And hunting wolves (while drunk) makes even less sense unless we make substantial changes from the real world.<br /> <br /> The character's simple mindset is too simple. As written this is a character as a bully, wanting to establish some kind of lupus supremacist ideology in a group where they are a small minority. Some acknowledgement of the obvious flaws of such an approach, and being in favor of a more intelligent approach could have transformed this into a stronger character that would be more fun to play.<br /> <br /> Most of the traits are broadly acceptable, but not increasing Willpower to equal Rage is a huge mistake. It puts the character in position of failing lots of Rage rolls and succumbing to the Thrall of the Wyrm. That would not be fun for any player. But it is something overlooked by brand new players because they are still mastering the rules set. A template should already be set up in a way so the PC can succeed. As is, this character is going to fail and blow up in the player's face. Bad design choice.<br /> <br /> Like all the other templates, the basic concept though generic is OK, but the details are weak. I think it's obvious that at this point in time, White Wolf really didn't know what to do with the lupus breed and wrote about them in a very perfunctory way.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, I think the example &quot;Lupus of Note&quot; written earlier in the sourcebook do a much better job of showing some diversity in the characters. If they had considered other such characters, but what they would have been like in their youth, that might have created more interesting templates.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-23T15:51:14-07:00","id":1524442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524439#post1524439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Red Talon tribal template is pretty much guaranteed in a lupus and wilderness focused sourcebook, but it should have been a non-obvious auspice. Showcasing what a Red Talon Ragabash or Theurge would have shown the diversity of the tribe more. But I wonder how much the creators really conceived of the Red Talons as a tribe that could be played by PCs in a mixed pack as opposed to one of the designated bad guys of the setting. Multiple things about the template seem like a bad stereotype. Not only does this character come off bad, even the humans mentioned in it are stereotypes. Very few hunters would ever attempt to hunt while drunk because of firearms safety issues. No one wants to risk killing a friend. And hunting wolves (while drunk) makes even less sense unless we make substantial changes from the real world.<br /> <br /> The character's simple mindset is too simple. As written this is a character as a bully, wanting to establish some kind of lupus supremacist ideology in a group where they are a small minority. Some acknowledgement of the obvious flaws of such an approach, and being in favor of a more intelligent approach could have transformed this into a stronger character that would be more fun to play.<br /> <br /> Most of the traits are broadly acceptable, but not increasing Willpower to equal Rage is a huge mistake. It puts the character in position of failing lots of Rage rolls and succumbing to the Thrall of the Wyrm. That would not be fun for any player. But it is something overlooked by brand new players because they are still mastering the rules set. A template should already be set up in a way so the PC can succeed. As is, this character is going to fail and blow up in the player's face. Bad design choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>You need Rage 6+ to do this unless you get Mars Midsky. Also, back when Ways of the Wolf was published, Thrall of the Wyrm didn't exist as such - every frenzy technically carried the possibility that you would potentially eat someone if you botched a Wits roll, like the present Homid TotW, but it was just part of a frenzy and getting a bunch of extra successes didn't affect it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-23T18:51:19-07:00","id":1524457,"title":"","content":"I think you could have done something interesting with a Red Tallon Galliard. Perhaps a character who is somewhat hellbent on getting Homids and Metis to better understand the Lupus perspective and experience, and how their thinning numbers and the loss of wolves and other animal species is a big part of the world hurtling towards the Apocalypse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-24T08:35:05-07:00","id":1524476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524439#post1524439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But I wonder how much the creators really conceived of the Red Talons as a tribe that could be played by PCs in a mixed pack as opposed to one of the designated bad guys of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say they were pretty clearly meant as playable to serve as the counterpoint to Glass Walkers. The issue with the Talons is how little changes they had since 1st ed and how poorly they were presented to the players. I will forever remember how TV Tropes had a whole rant about them and how playing them was either supporting zoophilia or being an edgelord.<br /> <br /> The massive issue with the Talons, as wolf warrior shows, is that they are geared to dislike every other PC in the pack. And the only time that changed was when Werewolf: The Dark Ages came out and presented the Talons more as visionaries and prophets than RARR KILL HUMAN.<br /> <br /> This is just my personal opinion, but I feel what made Talons such a hard sell for most was that they were lupus (and garou born) only. Because, for all the Talons get called edgy, plenty of other WoD factions of edge get played just fine. Tzimisce,Thallain,Nagaraja, Rokea,etc. are things people are interested in. The way Talons are set up makes them hard to integrate and plan for a game, because most of the time they are the odd garou out in every scene. There is no human connection there for players to grab onto.<br /> <br /> What makes this sad, is that the Talon lore IS good and in good hands they can be amazing to play. But the problem is that it requires the ST running the game to plan for a lot of BS.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-24T09:00:35-07:00","id":1524477,"title":"","content":"I'm reminded of my longstanding theory that, in spite of being introduced in the Vampire <i>Players</i> Guide, the four Independent Clans were likely first conceived as antagonist factions rather than something people would play in a mixed group. I sometimes wonder if Werewolf had started with just seven Tribes and added the rest later, just which ones would have been the core seven and which would have been the &quot;problem children&quot; that came later. (Red Talons, Get of Fenris, and Wendigo seem likely candidates for the latter. I could see a case for Bone Gnawers and Shadow Lords as well.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-24T09:20:48-07:00","id":1524479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524477#post1524477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (Red Talons, Get of Fenris, and Wendigo seem likely candidates for the latter. I could see a case for Bone Gnawers and Shadow Lords as well.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Despite what the current climate might let you believe, Fenrir are one of the most 'basic' tribes in WtA. For the 'problem children', I'd see Red Talons,Shadow Lords, Silent Striders and Gale Stalkers as the ones added later. Tribes that require more 'effort' from the ST to include.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-24T11:40:58-07:00","id":1524482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524476#post1524476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd say they were pretty clearly meant as playable to serve as the counterpoint to Glass Walkers. The issue with the Talons is how little changes they had since 1st ed and how poorly they were presented to the players. I will forever remember how TV Tropes had a whole rant about them and how playing them was either supporting zoophilia or being an edgelord.<br /> <br /> The massive issue with the Talons, as wolf warrior shows, is that they are geared to dislike every other PC in the pack. And the only time that changed was when Werewolf: The Dark Ages came out and presented the Talons more as visionaries and prophets than RARR KILL HUMAN.<br /> <br /> This is just my personal opinion, but I feel what made Talons such a hard sell for most was that they were lupus (and garou born) only. Because, for all the Talons get called edgy, plenty of other WoD factions of edge get played just fine. Tzimisce,Thallain,Nagaraja, Rokea,etc. are things people are interested in. The way Talons are set up makes them hard to integrate and plan for a game, because most of the time they are the odd garou out in every scene. There is no human connection there for players to grab onto.<br /> <br /> What makes this sad, is that the Talon lore IS good and in good hands they can be amazing to play. But the problem is that it requires the ST running the game to plan for a lot of BS.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the seed of what makes Red Talons potentially annoying is when you just reduce it to how it's phrased under &quot;Concept&quot; for the Wolf-Warrior-template: &quot;You were born as a wolf, and still think like wolf. Your thought processes are somewhat more sophisticated, but you prefer to rely on instinct. Like most Red Talons, you believe the humans should be completely destroyed.\u200b&quot; &quot;Thinking like a wolf&quot; shouldn't mean you have to roleplay animal-like behavior all the time and &quot;humanity should be destroyed&quot; shouldn't mean being a 24/7 psychopath hellbent on killing humans. Rather the former should be about how Red Talons see themselves as advocates for the wolves' perspective. The problems don't just stop as far as wolves are concerned when you simply destroy a Pentex facility, there are plenty of non-Wyrm-tainted humans being a threat to wolves living in peace and quiet as well. So they will make a case that from the wolves' perspective merely destroying a Pentex-facility doesn't entirely solve the problem whereas Homids might be inclined to think that that's enough. And with the latter, it shouldn't be about portraying some bloodhungry sociopath and more about expressing the frustration of how many setbacks the Red Talons' cause has suffered over the last couple of centuries, if not millennia.<br /> <br /> The Dark Ages thing of them being so tied to making prophecies is interesting because I think you can use that to make them a bit of a Cassandra-figure. Sure, they don't see the whole picture with how fixated they're on wolves and calling for a Second Impergium isn't exactly a solution either but the dismal fate of the wolves around the world should've been seen as a warning-sign that things aren't exactly going in the right direction for Gaia and the war against the Wyrm. And then here we are in the present modern day where the situation just has gotten worse and worse. It's in that context you get these angry Red Talons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-24T11:44:00-07:00","id":1524483,"title":"","content":"One thing Werewolf lacked was the many canonical examples of characters in regional sourcebooks that Vampire had. Chicago By Night not only gave us characters we expected from each clan, but characters that defied expectations. Tremere had Nicolai and DuSable, but also Garwood Marshall. Ventrue had Lodin and Ballard, but also Bobby Weatherbottom and Lorraine. Toreador had the expected artistes and poseurs, but also Sir Henry Johnson who was an English naval captain. And so on. The introductory sourcebook CbN 1e had over 70 characters for 7 clans, meaning on average there were around 10 NPCs per clan. In contrast, Rage Across New York had around 26 for 13 tribes, meaning 2 characters per tribe. So even a small clan like Tremere had four examples in CbN 1e, while the Red Talons had one example only in Rage Across New York.<br /> <br /> The lack of seeing many different interpretations of a tribe early on easily lent itself to tribes seeing much less diverse than they could be. I think the &quot;problem&quot; tribes who have seen less like a problem if we saw more examples of them, and how they could fit into the game.<br /> <br /> I imagine WtA writers likely assumed any Red Talon PCs would come from the &quot;Anti-Extinction Faction&quot; which the Players Guide tells us is the main camp of the tribe. But we're not given examples of it so it's easy to forget. And I think the writers themselves would forget that as well and this camp would be reduced in stature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-26T12:55:16-07:00","id":1524545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524479#post1524479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Despite what the current climate might let you believe, Fenrir are one of the most 'basic' tribes in WtA. </div> </div> </div> </div>I quite agree. But at the same time, first edition material about the Get tended to be ... aggravating is one word for it.<br /> Rite of Passage, in the (ridiculously brief) section about each Tribe's Rite of Passage, it says the Get cull those they feel aren't worthy, either killing them out right or banishing them to be Ronin for the rest of their lives. (Both options are strategically dumb; the game drives home how the Garou are a dying species, so killing a new Cub is extremely self destructive, and even if they aren't &quot;the right fit&quot; for the Get, you can easily turn them over to another tribe - Children of Gaia, for example - rather than Ronin who might more easily fall to the Wyrm.) It then goes on to describe their Rite as something akin to a lynch mob. The only other tribe that comes close to such a negative description in the section is the Shadow Lords; even the Red Talon Rite comes across as more reasonable in comparison. <br /> Like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> mentioned, the early Rage Across books didn't offer a lot of sample characters for the tribes, and with Rage Across New York, we got only the local Get leader, the female Get he secretly had a child with who is currently in hiding, and their Metis offspring ... who is the leader of a gang of Get skinheads in NYC (who make up, IIRC, a quarter of the state's Get population). <br /> And then there's that really terrible story in the Drums Around the Fire fiction collection which said that female Get aren't allowed to be Ahroun. Ethan Skemp said that even at the start of the Revised edition era, he was still hearing about groups that took that as in-game cannon. <br /> So I think there was clearly some sort of tendency among various Werewolf writers at the time to write the Get with the presumption that they were going to be antagonists to the PCs rather than something they thought people might want to actually play. <br /> <br /> Personally, I have always really enjoyed them, especially once the game started to get some of the early kinks worked out, and presented them as a tribe focused on the idea of Strength and just what that means. And the revised edition had one of the cooler tribal signature characters with Karin Jarlsdottir. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-26T14:27:13-07:00","id":1524549,"title":"","content":"Now on to <i>Rite of Passage</i>. Released in 1992, this was the first Werewolf sourcebook for 1st ed, with only the Storytellers' Screen coming out between it and the core book. This was written by Sam Chupp, William Hale, and Rob Hatch. The template art is by Josh Timbrook.<br /> The book is about 90% introductory chronicle and about 10% sourcebook. These five characters were created with the chronicle in mind and apparently used to play test it. Unlike the premade templates in Ways of the Wolf or the tribe books, these are named characters with more fully fleshed out personality and backstory. The word count for each seems to be a lot larger than that of Ways of the Wolf or Black Furies. And unlike Ways of the Wolf, they've had their freebie points spent. Also, in contrast to every other book that came after, these go from Ahroun to Ragabash rather than vice versa. <br /> <br /> <b>Snarls-At-Fleas / Lone Wolf </b>(Lupus Ahroun Get of Fenris)<br /> <br /> I'll note to start that this character appears to be male, but nothing in the write up says anything definitive about gender, and because the image is in Crinos form (which tends to down play sex characteristics), this could just as easily be interpreted as a female character. <br /> <br /> Their upbringing is a fairly typical Lupus affair. A pleasant life as a wolf interrupted by humans. But the writing here is top notch, with a lot of emotional detail that I really enjoy. Piece by piece, the pack is forced back by encroaching humans, and one by one members of the pack fall. And bit by bit, the Rage grows, until finally they start to Change. The description of the character growing from a wolf's mindset into something more is really good, and something I think anyone wanting to play a Lupus character would benefit from reading. Learning how to think and plan and lure human hunters into traps and ambushes eventually leads to erupting into the full Change and Crinos form. But once the hunters were dead, the surviving pack members didn't want them anymore. They were as much a monster to the pack as they were do the humans, and wandered alone until being found by other Garou and becoming a Get of Fenris. But no matter how much they loose themselves in the fury of battle, they still long for a return to the simple life among the pines with the pack of their youth. <br /> <br /> <i>This</i> is what I feel the Red Talon in Ways of the Wolf should have been. This sad and tragic longing for a lost innocence that one can never return to, and a clear motivation to protect and defend that pack that played into the First Change. I actually can't help but wonder if the presence of this character here prevented them having such a thing in Ways of the Wolf. It would be sadly ironic if that were so. <br /> <br /> The image is of a Garou in Crinos form. There appear to be some ritual scars on the right shoulder, and they have a klaive. It's a nice image. Nothing about it really stands out, but it's a very solid depiction of a werewolf in Crinos. <br /> <br /> Lone Wolf is the concept listed on the character sheet. I tend to dislike this term for non-Ronin Garou. In nature, a lone wolf tends to be a soon-to-be-dead wolf. But in the context of this character, forever isolated from the pack they wish to return to, and because of that perhaps a little stand offish to these new pack mates (non of whom are Lupus if you use the pre-generated characters here), I think it fits. And I confess, I'm head-cannoning the last part, but I feel it makes sense given what's written, and would give this character a good personal arc through the chronicle. <br /> <br /> With Attributes, Physical is primary, with an extra dot from freebies, for a 4/3/4 spread. That seems perfectly fine. This character is obviously meant to be the muscle for this pack. Socials are tertiary, with 3/1/2, which makes sense. This feels like a straight-forward type who can be a strong personality when they want to. Mental is secondary, with 3/2/3. As we saw in the write up, they're fairly clever when they want to be. And I appreciate having a character of this particular mix of Breed, Auspice, and Tribe who is presented as not being some sort of thick headed lout. <br /> <br /> For Abilities, Talents are primary, again with an extra dot from freebies. Brawl is at 4, with 3 each in Intimidation and Primal Urge, and 2 each in Athletics and Dodge. <br /> Skills are secondary, with 3 each in Animal Ken and Survival, a 2 in Stealth, and 1 in Leadership. <br /> Knowledge is tertiary, with 2 each in Investigation and Rituals, and 1 in Occult. <br /> <br /> Backgrounds, of which Get get four in 1st ed, are Contacts 2, Fetish 1 (Klaive), and Pack Totem 1. <br /> It's nice to see some effort give to Pack Totem. However, I'm kind of at a loss as to who these Contacts might be. Other Get of Fenris? In 1st ed, Get couldn't have Allies; in 2nd ed, this was changed to Contacts. (They couldn't have Past Life either, which was just bizarre.) <br /> As for the Klaive, the first edition core book does not appear to have any descriptions for Klaives. They're aren't among the example Fetishes, and the weapons chart just says that knives include Klaives. All you really get is the word's definition in the lexicon, and that's about it. However, second edition made these a level 4 Fetish, and even the step down from that, the Fang Dagger, is level 3. However, it seems like two freebie points haven't been spent. I'm guessing maybe they were meant to be spent on the Fetish background?<br /> <br /> Rage has been raised from 5 to 7. Gnosis is 5. Willpower has been boosted from 3 to 7. <br /> <br /> Stat wise, this is mostly pretty solid. However, using 2nd ed rules, I'd probably change the backgrounds to Fetish 3 (Fang Dagger), and Pack Totem 2 (because I feel like this is the sort of character who wants a place to belong, even if they're going to be tsundere about it). I would probably drop Rage to 5, that way I'd still have four freebies, so as to buy a point in Alertness and two dots in Pure Breed. <br /> <br /> Stat quibbles aside, I really like this character a lot. It's a great back story with a lot of emotional depth and some great potential for role play and growth as part of a new pack. An excellent start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-26T18:19:06-07:00","id":1524560,"title":"","content":"In 1e, the definition of a klaive was more like how it ended up in Forsaken (a loose, general term for a fetish weapon). The level 5 Silver Sword was supposed to be an example of an impressive one. In 2e, it became codified into the klaive and grand klaive. And then ended up defining the magic swords of the Exalted...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-27T01:19:57-07:00","id":1524576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524545#post1524545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I quite agree. But at the same time, first edition material about the Get tended to be ... aggravating is one word for it.<br /> Rite of Passage, in the (ridiculously brief) section about each Tribe's Rite of Passage, it says the Get cull those they feel aren't worthy, either killing them out right or banishing them to be Ronin for the rest of their lives. (Both options are strategically dumb; the game drives home how the Garou are a dying species, so killing a new Cub is extremely self destructive, and even if they aren't &quot;the right fit&quot; for the Get, you can easily turn them over to another tribe - Children of Gaia, for example - rather than Ronin who might more easily fall to the Wyrm.) It then goes on to describe their Rite as something akin to a lynch mob. The only other tribe that comes close to such a negative description in the section is the Shadow Lords; even the Red Talon Rite comes across as more reasonable in comparison.</div> </div> </div> </div>In later books, the cubs usually join other tribes, but the way Fenrir RoP are hasn't changed. The thing is that getting to join the tribe is extremely hard and you have to basically prove you have the willpower to get back up again and again but also that you can hold control over your Rage to deal with mockery and beatings without frenzying.<br /> <br /> To me, that fits the tribe. Especially as it is same for <b>everyone</b>. You can have purebreed 5 and Ancestor/Past Life 5 and you still get tested to your limits. So those who become rited usually are the ones that embody the tribe's spirit the best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-27T01:52:33-07:00","id":1524577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524545#post1524545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rite of Passage, in the (ridiculously brief) section about each Tribe's Rite of Passage, it says the Get cull those they feel aren't worthy, either killing them out right or banishing them to be Ronin for the rest of their lives.</div> </div> </div> </div>I try to incorporate a lot of overlooked or forgotten 1e and early 2e lore in my version of the chronicle, but I agree that is dumb for the reasons you mentioned. I ended up incorporating a variant of it though - the Get of Fenris include a lot of real danger in their Rite of Passage so that while it is rare, it is not unheard of for a cub to die during their rite of passage. It's not intentional, and it is limited to those NPCs who have very low Attributes (actual 1s in their Physical or Mental traits). In other words, not characters built using the standard character creations rules but reflecting the left hand side of the bell curve. They want it to be a real test to see if the cubs are worthy and ready.<br /> <br /> As we've discussed earlier, these are extremely early products and their tribal descriptions are still in the form of wanting to easily distinguish one tribe from another. So they are using very broad stereotypes that sometimes fall into self-parody. So adjust accordingly if you are using these sourcebooks today.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-27T02:03:12-07:00","id":1524578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524549#post1524549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>This</i> is what I feel the Red Talon in Ways of the Wolf should have been.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a very similar concept done better. So I like it.<br /> <br /> I should note that in first edition, &quot;klaive&quot; did not have the specific meaning it has now. It was more like any Garou weapon, not a specific kind of fetish.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524549#post1524549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stat quibbles aside, I really like this character a lot. It's a great back story with a lot of emotional depth and some great potential for role play and growth as part of a new pack. An excellent start.</div> </div> </div> </div>However, as a starting character in Rite of Passage, meaning it is intended for the Sept of the Green in Central Park, there needed to be a better explanation as to why this character starts at that sept. Maybe that can be put (along with rationales for the other templates) on its own page so it does not clutter up the template so the template can be used for any chronicle. Did Arn Guth Stormbright send it to Central Park to search for his son in the city? Did Spotlight offer to look after the lupus as some kind of favor to the Adirondack sept, thus leaving it up to the PC if they want to stay afterwards? Otherwise it is hard to see why this is a good template for use in this location. A good ST can come up for good reasons to explain it, but as an introductory adventure for a brand new game and setting, it would behoove the sourcebook to already provide some advice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-27T02:10:33-07:00","id":1524579,"title":"","content":"There's an interesting bit at the start of Chapter One: &quot;If the players wish to create their own characters, you need to be concerned with the choices they make. There should be one of each auspice represented if at all possible. You should not allow more than one lupus character, nor should you allow more than one Red Talon or Get of Fenris. However, the metropolitan nature of the Sept of the Green allows virtually any other combination of tribes, auspices and breeds among your pack of pups.&quot; Makes me wonder why they didn't course-correct in how lupus, Red Talons and Get of Fenris are portrayed if the developers already felt the need to add this kind of advice. <br /> <br /> This also informs how the sample-characters are assembled, I assume and so with Snarls-At-Fleas you already got that one limitation out of the way with only one lupus character and one Red Talon/Get of Fenris character being allowed. Giving the Ahroun-auspice to either a Red Talon or Get of Fenris is once again a bit on-the-nose but the writing is really good. The high Rage is mentioned, it has good writing for a lupus-origin-story and you get what the character's core-theme is. Still think it would've been nice to at least bring back Roleplaying-Tips as a section. Especially because I think what should be avoided is that the lone-wolf-concept comes across as too stand-offish in interactions with the other player-characters. The lone-wolf-status should be more of a starting-point than an idea to be strictly adhered to in the roleplaying of this character.<br /> <br /> Stat-wise it's mostly okay. The Backgrounds, though... Both the Klaive and the dots in Contacts: From the writing, it isn't really clear where that's supposed to come from or what role in the character's background it's supposed to play. Raising Rage to 7 is certainly a choice. But other than that a good character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-27T19:31:11-07:00","id":1524610,"title":"","content":"<b>Dirge aka Janet Crowley / Loyal Soldier </b>(Homid Shadow Lord Galliard)<br /> <br /> So this one is a little shorter than the previous, looking like it clocks in at about the same word count as most of the tribe book template entries. <br /> <br /> Janet is from a fairly miserable home environment, but one that was sadly kind of common for some GenX kids of a certain socio-economic background. Her mom ran off at some point, leaving her with an alcoholic and neglectful father. Janet developed &quot;antisocial tendencies&quot; and &quot;behavioral disorder&quot;, getting into fights, cutting class, shoplifting, and becoming a general juvenile delinquent. Finally she got picked up by the police. <br /> I do enjoy this description of her internal anger, the desire to fight back against anyone who got in her face, and smash their faces in. Even in 1st ed, we got descriptions about Homids being maladjusted or not fitting in while growing up, and I believe later in the line, Ethan Skemp would mention at times the idea that the Rage boiling up inside them would lead to various personal issues. However, a number of Homid character write ups would seem to gloss over or ignore this at times. So I'm happy to see a character where it's right there up front. <br /> <br /> She was taken from the police by another detective who gave off an aura of menace that cowed her natural rebelliousness. He told her she was one of the Shadow Lords, and that they were here family. It turns out that a family is what she's wanted all this time, so she's extremely loyal to her new tribe, more than to anything else in her life. <br /> Again, I like this take, especially given her Tribe. There isn't even any mention of her being used by her new &quot;family&quot; or the like. I think this is an interesting direction for a Shadow Lord. While it plays in with the way they are written in the 1st ed, 2nd ed started focusing more on the idea of dominance before shifting more toward a sort of ruthless pragmatism. <br /> <br /> There's a rather offhand (gratuitous, really) remark about her playing bass guitar in a band. There's nothing wrong with the idea. I do with it had perhaps been mentioned earlier when talking about her various forms of teenage rebellion. But as it is, it feels like it was just sort of thrown in as &quot;oh, yeah, she's a Galliard, so she does something with music&quot; kind of thing. <br /> <br /> The image is pretty cool. It's similar to a number of Timbrook's early Vampire illustrations, and wouldn't feel out of place in the Brujah, Gangrel or Malkavian clan books. Your sort of typical early 90s GenX grunge riot grrl with some Goth overtones. Jeans, leather jacket, and cigarette. <br /> <br /> For Attributes, Physicals are primary, with a 3/4/3 split. Socials are secondary, with an additional dot from freebies, with a 4/3/2 split. Mental is tertiary, all of them at 2. This seems to work fine. <br /> <br /> For Abilities, both Talents and Skills have 13 dots each, so I've no idea which is primary and which is secondary with an extra four dots from freebies. I guess it doesn't really matter. <br /> Talents are a 3 in Brawl, 2 each in Dodge, Empathy, Expression, and Intimidation, and 1 each in Streetwise and Subterfuge. <br /> Empathy feels like a strange fit for this character. It's possible that there are some aspects of her personality that aren't being discussed in the write up that one could try to infer from the presence of that abilities. But as written, I feel like maybe those two dots might've been better used to raise Streetwise and Subterfuge to 2 each. <br /> For Skills, we have 3 each in Leadership and Performance, 2 each in Firearms and Stealth, and 1 each in Animal Ken, Drive, and Survival. <br /> Animal Ken strikes me the same way as Empathy. I think Melee might make more sense, given the juvenile delinquent background. I might even go as far as to move a point from Firearms into Melee as well. I have no problem with the Leadership skill, even through the write up doesn't exactly offer anything about it. However, I could see her being the leader of a small gang of some sort prior to her change, which I think would make for potential interesting character hooks later one. Survival also feels like a little bit of an outlier. However, she's the only Homid character of the bunch to have that skill. I sort of see it as something she was forced to learn after her first change, just so she didn't embarrass her Tribe when around others. But that's just me head-cannoning again. <br /> Knowledge is tertiary, with 2 in Rituals, and 1 each in Law, Occult, and Politics. These all seem fine. <br /> <br /> For Backgrounds, she has 1 each in Past Lives, Pure Breed, Resources, and Pack Totem. I'd be tempted to drop Past Lives in favor for a dot in Contacts to represent people she used to hang out with. I'm presuming resources have to do with this band she plays with. However, if you went with the gang thing I mentioned earlier, it could just as easily be them paying her some sort of regular tribute. Under 2nd ed rules, she'd have one more Background dot, and I could see it going to raise any of the ones already chosen. <br /> <br /> Rage is 4, Gnosis is 3, and Willpower is 3. This means she's spent more than 15 freebie points (5 for Attributes, 8 for Abilities, and now 4 for Gnosis). I'd fix this by leaving Gnosis at 1 and spending the remaining two freebies to raise her WP to 5. I might even be tempted to strip a dot from Abilities to increase it to 6 or 7. <br /> <br /> I like this character. I think she has a good backstory that offers a number of avenues for personalized development and expansion. She has the kind of background I enjoy seeing in Homid characters, and what I feel is a non-stereotypical expression of her Tribe. I also think the idea of her wanting a family and now being super-loyal to this new one that has adopted her can make an interesting expression of the Lover of the Ways archetype and be a reason for her to be all in on tribal rites and traditions. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-27T22:55:23-07:00","id":1524616,"title":"","content":"Empathy is required to understand others' motivations, Leadership is required to organize others and play a role in an organization, especially if you have ambitions of taking charge... and well, we're talking a first edition Shadow Lord. They were dangerously close to being Starscream before later course corrections.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-27T23:55:17-07:00","id":1524622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524616#post1524616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They were dangerously close to being Starscream before later course corrections.</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn, now I want to see the Margrave crowning himself while a bunch of sycophants play trumpets. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-28T00:05:19-07:00","id":1524623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524610#post1524610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do enjoy this description of her internal anger, the desire to fight back against anyone who got in her face, and smash their faces in. Even in 1st ed, we got descriptions about Homids being maladjusted or not fitting in while growing up, and I believe later in the line, Ethan Skemp would mention at times the idea that the Rage boiling up inside them would lead to various personal issues. However, a number of Homid character write ups would seem to gloss over or ignore this at times. So I'm happy to see a character where it's right there up front.</div> </div> </div> </div>I honestly wish they had either doubled down on this or just removed it. Because even as far as Revised, you had garou doing human jobs just fine and then it made players want to have their Ahroun with a special forces training or be a former police officer.<br /> <br /> It really looks disjointed when the rules say one thing and then have the <b>official</b> sourcebooks say another, because the writer found it too hard to write someone who could not exist in the human world. Forsaken did a good job in removing the initial horror effect, so I'm baffled W5 just plain old added it back with interest.<br /> <br /> Personally, as much as I enjoy this aspect of being garou, having read book after book that ignores Rage in favour of the narrative/NPC jobs I'd just remove the Curse. Because it is clearly something most sourcebook or novel writers and therefore players can't deal with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-28T02:05:06-07:00","id":1524625,"title":"","content":"Just personally, I don't have a huge problem with it with Ragabash, Theurge, and to some extent Philodox characters (especially if they bulk up their WP a bit). But with Galliard and Ahroun, I think any chance of continuing the facade of a normal human life goes out the window. And even with the lower Rage Auspices, I think a human career is just a starting point, and by the time they hit Rank 3, circumstances have likely necessitated focusing more on Garou society than any &quot;day job&quot;. And I plan to look at those templates that try to keep a job from that perspective. For example, when I got to Get of Fenris, I had planned to talk about how the vigilante cop character was likely about to go off the rails or already is. I think you can get a lot of role play mileage out of that kind of thing. But a lot of it should be the tragedy and frustration of realizing you can never be the pre-change you again, no matter how hard you try. IMO at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-28T03:08:06-07:00","id":1524627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524610#post1524610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> She was taken from the police by another detective who gave off an aura of menace that cowed her natural rebelliousness. He told her she was one of the Shadow Lords, and that they were here family. It turns out that a family is what she's wanted all this time, so she's extremely loyal to her new tribe, more than to anything else in her life.<br /> Again, I like this take, especially given her Tribe. There isn't even any mention of her being used by her new &quot;family&quot; or the like. I think this is an interesting direction for a Shadow Lord. While it plays in with the way they are written in the 1st ed, 2nd ed started focusing more on the idea of dominance before shifting more toward a sort of ruthless pragmatism.</div> </div> </div> </div>About that bit... Is it just me or could there be an implication here that this &quot;detective&quot;-figure is actually her real father? And so when this figure says her whole life has been a mistake and she's now where she belongs, with her family, he's being very literal actually...? The character having Pure Breed 1 would add to that interpretation as well.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-28T05:42:33-07:00","id":1524631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524625#post1524625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just personally, I don't have a huge problem with it with Ragabash, Theurge, and to some extent Philodox characters (especially if they bulk up their WP a bit). But with Galliard and Ahroun, I think any chance of continuing the facade of a normal human life goes out the window. And even with the lower Rage Auspices, I think a human career is just a starting point, and by the time they hit Rank 3, circumstances have likely necessitated focusing more on Garou society than any &quot;day job&quot;. And I plan to look at those templates that try to keep a job from that perspective. For example, when I got to Get of Fenris, I had planned to talk about how the vigilante cop character was likely about to go off the rails or already is. I think you can get a lot of role play mileage out of that kind of thing. But a lot of it should be the tragedy and frustration of realizing you can never be the pre-change you again, no matter how hard you try. IMO at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with all of this. But the problem is not the people who want to play this out, it is how the books actually treated it. And most often, it was ignored in various ways. Plus it then set this really bad contrast between what the sourcebooks give examples of and what the actual rules are. I have had discussions with people where they have stated that the sourcebooks have garou with jobs, so why not have ones in game.<br /> <br /> And this isn't a small thing you can ignore, it is basically if a vampire clanbook ignored the clan weakness.<br /> <br /> So I am looking at this from the perspective of practicality. If years upon years of official book writers chose to ignore the Curse in favour of their own story, then the Curse is something that gets in the way of a good story for most. I don't agree, but I have been around long enough to know some REALLY hate the idea of garou being moochers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-28T05:44:50-07:00","id":1524632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524579#post1524579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's an interesting bit at the start of Chapter One: &quot;If the players wish to create their own characters, you need to be concerned with the choices they make. There should be one of each auspice represented if at all possible. You should not allow more than one lupus character, nor should you allow more than one Red Talon or Get of Fenris.</div> </div> </div> </div>A bit spoilery, but I find this EXTREMELY funny, consider what the theurge character is. A lupus PC is far less disruptive than the Whisperer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-28T06:10:58-07:00","id":1524635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524632#post1524632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A bit spoilery, but I find this EXTREMELY funny, consider what the theurge character is. A lupus PC is far less disruptive than the Whisperer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, there will be a lot to say about that particular character when we get to him. And what makes it even funnier is that the template-section starts by proudly proclaiming: &quot;These characters have been playtested with the game and work well in it.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-28T09:39:05-07:00","id":1524641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524627#post1524627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About that bit... Is it just me or could there be an implication here that this &quot;detective&quot;-figure is actually her real father? And so when this figure says her whole life has been a mistake and she's now where she belongs, with her family, he's being very literal actually...? The character having Pure Breed 1 would add to that interpretation as well.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oooh, you're right. I didn't even think of that, but it would make a really great twist down the line if you ran this character for a long time. \ud83d\ude00","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-28T10:13:27-07:00","id":1524642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524610#post1524610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do enjoy this description of her internal anger, the desire to fight back against anyone who got in her face, and smash their faces in. Even in 1st ed, we got descriptions about Homids being maladjusted or not fitting in while growing up, and I believe later in the line, Ethan Skemp would mention at times the idea that the Rage boiling up inside them would lead to various personal issues. However, a number of Homid character write ups would seem to gloss over or ignore this at times. So I'm happy to see a character where it's right there up front.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's good to see it mentioned, but it gets sand bagged by later comment of her playing bass in a band which is not really possible with the amount of Rage. But the Curse often gets overlooked by everyone. I can see an argument that it shouldn't affect her audience assuming the stage is set back some from the crowd, but it should be impacting her bandmates. They could be extremely high willpower, but I think a more elegant solution would be to make the Kinfolk and thus she should have some dots in Kinfolk. At the very least, it should be addressed in some fashion.<br /> <br /> It's important to me as ST in using the Curse as a narrative tool so I keep it in the setting and reference it a lot. Having it ruin personal relationships is not the same as the character not able to walk among people when needed. But I do add some House Rules so players can ignore it when they absolutely have to have a face to face conversation or scene with humans. One thing I allow is for character to spend a point of temporary Willpower to &quot;bury the wolf&quot; for a scene.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524610#post1524610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a rather offhand (gratuitous, really) remark about her playing bass guitar in a band. There's nothing wrong with the idea. I do with it had perhaps been mentioned earlier when talking about her various forms of teenage rebellion. But as it is, it feels like it was just sort of thrown in as &quot;oh, yeah, she's a Galliard, so she does something with music&quot; kind of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. That seems really paint by numbers and does not build on anything established earlier. No mention of her sneaking off to see her favorite punk or metal band, or that she retreated into a world of music to make up for her social isolation. In absence of that, I would have gone with a different &quot;Lover of the Ways&quot; approach and gotten her big into the culture and traditions of the Shadow Lords. Maybe build on her point in Past Life in that respect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524610#post1524610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Backgrounds, she has 1 each in Past Lives, Pure Breed, Resources, and Pack Totem</div> </div> </div> </div>Templates usually ignore the Totem background, but I think all these templates have 1 dot of it. It's the only time templates acknowledge players will want to build up their pack totem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524610#post1524610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this character. I think she has a good backstory that offers a number of avenues for personalized development and expansion. She has the kind of background I enjoy seeing in Homid characters, and what I feel is a non-stereotypical expression of her Tribe. I also think the idea of her wanting a family and now being super-loyal to this new one that has adopted her can make an interesting expression of the Lover of the Ways archetype and be a reason for her to be all in on tribal rites and traditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a solid character. Appropriate for the Shadow Lords, but the template could have been used for almost any tribe. I guess that's fine. Not every character needs to shriek &quot;I am obviously from this tribe!&quot; and it makes sense for some starting characters. But for a character that has finally found her &quot;home&quot; and &quot;family&quot;, there should be a bit more flavor text explaining how she fits.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-28T10:18:59-07:00","id":1524644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524627#post1524627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About that bit... Is it just me or could there be an implication here that this &quot;detective&quot;-figure is actually her real father? And so when this figure says her whole life has been a mistake and she's now where she belongs, with her family, he's being very literal actually...? The character having Pure Breed 1 would add to that interpretation as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is more likely the absent mom (&quot;Mom was God knows where&quot;) is the Garou parent, and she left the father sometime after Janet was born to do Garou things. His wife leaving him is what probably drove him to drink. The real question for the ST is whether the mom should still be alive, or if she died on quest and that is why she never came back.<br /> <br /> The cop is probably just a Shadow Lord kinfolk who can recognize the signs.<br /> <br /> This character is easier to integrate into Rage Across New York than others because she is obviously urban based. But there still needs some work tying things together. We know there are Shadow Lords inside the city. The 2e corebook's description of the Sept of the Green has Zachary Ellsion, but he's not mentioned in 1e. But RANY does have Carleson Ruah in the city. But more intriguing is the leader of the Shadow Lords living in the wilderness, Sylvan-Ivanovich-Sylvan. She's middle-aged, has Pure Breed 1, and has black hair like Janet Crowley. As ST, I'd be very tempted to make this NPC Janet's mother. She would know she is Janet's mother, but I would let the PC figure it out herself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 10-28-2023, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-28T10:47:25-07:00","id":1524647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524642#post1524642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Templates usually ignore the Totem background, but I think all these templates have 1 dot of it. It's the only time templates acknowledge players will want to build up their pack totem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's strange that they didn't add a section about what Totem the Pack has. Either pick one that already exists or make a new one. But since they already bothered to give each sample character one dot in Totem this should've been part of the template-package in my opinion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524644#post1524644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is more likely the absent mom (&quot;Mom was God knows where&quot;) is the Garou parent, and she left the father sometime after Janet was born to do Garou things. His wife leaving him is what probably drove him to drink. The real question for the ST is whether the mom should still be alive, or if she died on quest and that is why she never came back.<br /> <br /> The cop is probably just a Shadow Lord kinfolk who can recognize the signs.<br /> <br /> This character is easier to integrate into Rage Across New York than others because she is obviously urban based. But there still needs some work tying things together. We know there are Shadow Lords inside the city. The 2e corebook's description of the Sept of the Green has Zachary Ellsion, but he's not mentioned in 1e. But RANY does have Carleson Ruah in the city. But more intriguing is the leader of the Shadow Lords living in the wilderness, Sylvan-Ivanovich-Sylvan. She's middle-aged, has Pure Breed 1, and has black hair like Janet Crowley. As ST, I'd be very tempted to make this NPC Janet's mother. She would know she is Janet's mother, but I would let the PC figure it out herself.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> Yeah, that's also an option. Especially if you can tie it to later lore like you mentioned.<br /> <br /> Did the detective-character read like a Kinfolk to you? I don't know... &quot;burning green eyes&quot;, &quot;<i>knock-you-through-the-wall</i> stare&quot; sound more like indicators of him being a Garou to me. Of course, if you take the Curse seriously, the detective being a Garou is certainly suspect in terms of worldbuilding but the issue with the depiction of the Curse has already been mentioned previously.<br /> <br /> Personally, I like the idea of her real father being a Garou and her mother being Kinfolk more because that makes the whole thing a messier affair. Who knows what happened that led to this state of affairs... And you give the father-figure a bit of an arc as he's trying to fix things and this starts with him getting her out of jail. That makes the story more personable, I think, rather than some Kinflok just getting her out, inducting her into the Shadow Lords and then (shock!) one of the leading figures turns out to be her real mother.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's a solid character. Appropriate for the Shadow Lords, but the template could have been used for almost any tribe. I guess that's fine. Not every character needs to shriek &quot;I am obviously from this tribe!&quot; and it makes sense for some starting characters. But for a character that has finally found her &quot;home&quot; and &quot;family&quot;, there should be a bit more flavor text explaining how she fits. </div> </div> </div>Agree. To me, the whole thing ends too early, like there should be one or two more paragraphs to round out the text as a prelude. I mean, the text doesn't even cover her First Change. If you were to remove all context from this bit of writing, it's never addressed that she's supposed to be a werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-28T11:23:19-07:00","id":1524651,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I noticed that this write up seems to be maybe a paragraph shorter than the previous one. So I think a few extra lines could have boosted this from solid to really good.<br /> <br /> With the band thing, I think you could do something interesting with her having been in one, but no longer being able to because of her Rage and her new responsibilities, and being regretful about it. Also the idea of her being asked to join a new band made up of members of other nearby packs who just want an outlet to play music again, especially if you wanted ways to tie the pack into a wider Garou community.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-29T17:55:29-07:00","id":1524721,"title":"","content":"<b>Linda Davis</b> <b>/ Peace Activist </b>(Homid Philodox Child of Gaia)<br /> <br /> As I previously mentioned, the first two Philodox ever were both female Children of Gaia. I've no idea how that happened. I mean, that tribe's basic concept/hook does mesh pretty well with the Philodox's role of peace keeper/mediator. Though I can't help but be curious what would've happened if they'd gone with, say, a Stargazer or Silver Fang in this role.<br /> <br /> So, Linda is essentially your archetypical 1st ed Child of Gaia. A gentle child who always wondered why people couldn't just be nicer to each other. A Greenpeace volunteer from age 14, and president of her college chapter of Amnesty International. (It doesn't say anything about her socioeconomic background, but I'm guessing maybe upper middle class.)<br /> Her First Change occurred at a protest she'd help organize against an unsafe chemical plant. I fight broke out between plant security and a group of militant environmentalists called the Green Knights. (This group popped up in some of the 1st ed Werewolf material, and then just kind of vanished, similarly to the Red Circle Wyrm cult.) Guns were involved, and Linda's boyfriend was killed shielding her from gunfire. So she turned into a werewolf and killed one of the security guards.<br /> Needless to say, the Delirium made the mass panic worse, but some of the Green Knights were presumably Kinfolk as they were able to talk her down and give her an inkling of what had happened. Afterwords, none of her friends wanted to be around her anymore so she called a number given to her and was introduced to her Tribe.<br /> (It doesn't specify if this rejection by her former friends was a result of the Curse, a misremembering of what happened at the protest, or both. I like to think both.)<br /> Now she continues her crusade to save the planet, while also working to restrain the violent impulses of the Garou, including her own.<br /> <br /> The image is a young woman of college age (20, maybe?) with not quite shoulder length hair, wearing a flower print dress with a pair of necklaces. One is a peace sign. The other is a little harder to make out, but appears to be a Pan-African symbol. Looking at the character's face, I think she's meant to be either African-American or mixed race. In all honesty, I could easily see her growing up on The Cosby Show.<br /> <br /> For Attributes, Physicals are tertiary, all at 2. Socials are secondary, with a 3/2/3 split. That leaves Mental as primary, with one extra dot from freebies, at 4/3/4. While I might could make an argument for one of those 4s being in Intelligence rather than Perception or Wits, I think this is fine as it is.<br /> <br /> For Abilities, Talents are secondary with an extra dot from freebies. She has 3 each in Empathy and Expression, and 1 each in Alertness, Athletics, Brawl, and Dodge. I mildly question the presence of Brawl. While I can see it being something she's been forced to learn since her first change, it feels maybe a little off.<br /> Skills are tertiary, with 2 in Etiquette, and 1 each in Animal Ken, Drive, and Performance. Given her background, and how it specifically says she was the leader of her college chapter of AI and that she helped organize the protest, I feel she should have Leadership. I'd probably move that dot in Performance, and possibly even the one in Animal Ken for a rating of 2.<br /> Knowledge is primary with two extra dots from freebies. She has 3 each in Law, Politics, and Rituals, a 2 in Medicine, and 1 each in Enigmas, Investigation, Linguistics, and Science. I'm guessing maybe a pre-Law/Political Science major? But a solid spread of abilities.<br /> <br /> Her Backgrounds points - the measly two that Children of Gaia got in 1st ed plus one more from freebies - are 1 each in Past Life, Resources, and Pack Totem. With 2nd ed's five points, I'd probably make that 2 each in the first and leave Pack Totem at 1.<br /> <br /> Her Rage is the base 3. Gnosis is 4, so that's six freebie points. Willpower is 6, thanks to another two freebies.<br /> <br /> So, for those with a sharp eye, that's 5 freebies for Attributes, 6 for Abilities, 1 for Backgrounds, 6 for Gnosis, and 2 for WP, for a grand total of 20 freebie points. Damn. It's been a while since I've seen a character sheet this out of wack points wise.<br /> My solution to this is to drop either the dot in Brawl or one of her Knowledge dots and at least two of the Gnosis dots. That leaves you with a single freebie point, which I would probably spend on another level of Pack Totem (or maybe Resources if you want to stick with 1st ed rules).<br /> <br /> The stat problems aside, I think this is a pretty good character. While the write up is about as long as the one for Snarls-At-Fleas (and yes, both are longer than Janet's), I think it spends at least half of that extra word count on talking about the Green Knights instead of about Linda herself. While I think the description of the protest and what happened do a lot to define her character and what is probably a major trauma associated with her Change, I would've liked to see a little more of the aftermath and how it impacted her. But that aside, I think she works well, with a strong hook for wanting to be a mediator and try to reign in the worst aspects of the rest of her pack. I also like the idea of a Child of Gaia character who has experienced first hand brutal violence in the face of peaceful activism, triggering her own Rage, but still trying to remain committed to her ideals. I think there's a lot to work with here for any player who wants to run this character long term. So I chalk this up as a win.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 10-29-2023, 10:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-29T19:05:54-07:00","id":1524722,"title":"","content":"I think that the sample Uzmati in Gurahl and the Revised Shadow Lord Ahroun probably take the cake in spending other entries' freebie points.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","