Past Life, Resources, and Pack Totem. With 2nd ed's five points, I'd probably make that 2 each in the first and leave Pack Totem at 1.<br /> <br /> Her Rage is the base 3. Gnosis is 4, so that's six freebie points. Willpower is 6, thanks to another two freebies.<br /> <br /> So, for those with a sharp eye, that's 5 freebies for Attributes, 6 for Abilities, 1 for Backgrounds, 6 for Gnosis, and 2 for WP, for a grand total of 20 freebie points. Damn. It's been a while since I've seen a character sheet this out of wack points wise.<br /> My solution to this is to drop either the dot in Brawl or one of her Knowledge dots and at least two of the Gnosis dots. That leaves you with a single freebie point, which I would probably spend on another level of Pack Totem (or maybe Resources if you want to stick with 1st ed rules).<br /> <br /> The stat problems aside, I think this is a pretty good character. While the write up is about as long as the one for Snarls-At-Fleas (and yes, both are longer than Janet's), I think it spends at least half of that extra word count on talking about the Green Knights instead of about Linda herself. While I think the description of the protest and what happened do a lot to define her character and what is probably a major trauma associated with her Change, I would've liked to see a little more of the aftermath and how it impacted her. But that aside, I think she works well, with a strong hook for wanting to be a mediator and try to reign in the worst aspects of the rest of her pack. I also like the idea of a Child of Gaia character who has experienced firsthand brutal violence in the face of peaceful activism, triggering her own Rage, but still trying to remain committed to her ideals. I think there's a lot to work with here for any player who wants to run this character long term. So I chalk this up as a win.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-29T20:31:22-07:00","id":1524731,"title":"","content":"Once again a Children of Gaia Philodox with an obvious focus on peace and mediation. But the writing is still solid. And the backstory is more solid here than it was for the Galliard. The backstory links nicely with a character-motivation for how to roleplay the character. But rather than restraint, I think the disconnect between having such an emphasized background in activism (both in terms of the environment and human rights) should clash very hard with the warrior-culture of the Garou. The writing even hints at the fact that pre-First-Change her beliefs weren't aligned with the aggressive/violent tactics of the Green Knights. Of course, the war against the Wyrm paints a different picture of what the conflict is like in contrast to the sort of tactics a mundane activist-group would consider and how the actual opposition is characterized.<br /> <br /> Stat-wise it's weird that the character's connection to this Green Knight group isn't represented. And then there's of course the whole Freebie-issue... But it's also noticeable how all the Homid-characters have Resources 1 (with the Ragabash having Resources 2). Also, that focus on Mental Attributes and Knowledge-Abilities is a bit surprising. From the backstory, I would expect this character to put far more dots into the social realm of things. She's supposed to be an activist, not a deep scholar on a subject. Like, where do these three dots on Law come from? The next character is much worse than this but the spread of dots goes way too hard into a specialized direction, I feel like. The dots should be spread around a bit more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-29T22:08:57-07:00","id":1524737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524727#post1524727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Her First Change occurred at a protest she'd help organize against an unsafe chemical plant. I fight broke out between plant security and a group of militant environmentalists called the Green Knights. (This group popped up in some of the 1st ed Werewolf material, and then just kind of vanished, similarly to the Red Circle Wyrm cult.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the Green Knights as some kind of radical environmentalist group that would make Greenpeace seem moderate was mentioned in very early 1e material, but then quickly forgotten. Like several other things, it may have been something Bill Bridges was passionate about, but Ethan Skemp was not interested in. The idea of radical left wing direct action / monkeywrenching as an earlier element that was not so much dropped, but ignored.<br /> <br /> In my own chronicles, I continue to use the Green Knights as a criminal group of monkey wrenchers (who are often, but not always referred to as terrorists) whenever I need such a group. I don't really have a &quot;plan&quot; for them, I just use them whenever such a group would be convenient.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qG0fVqJBCKM\" data-code=\"qG0fVqJBCKM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/qG0fVqJBCKM/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T08:09:05-07:00","id":1524756,"title":"","content":"The biggest problem I have with Linda is not anything about her character per se. It is that the tribe never quite got away from her type of character.<br /> <br /> Even the Revised nightmare of a tribebook for the tribe still followed the same upper-middle-class mentality. Children of Gaia at their worst don't read like a millennia-old tribe of peacekeepers, they read like a tribe created in the 60s by a bunch of trustfund kids. Only the historical games, especially the Dark Ages, really dig into the fact that these werewolves come from the Middle East.<br /> <br /> For Brawl 1, remember that she NEEDS that dot to claw and bite and her tribe wouldn't have let her perform her RoP without knowing to fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T09:29:07-07:00","id":1524757,"title":"","content":"I think her character is ill-served by this being this standard Philodox Children of Gaia peace-actvist. The way it's conceptualized it just ends up being this straight line. First, environment/human-rights-activist, violent First Change, Children of Gaia Philodox that wants to restrain the violent nature of other Garou. It's a bit cookie-cutter in how things seamlessly move from plot-point to plot-point while essentially repeating the same idea over and over again.<br /> <br /> In this case, personally what I would think would be more interesting is to make her the Theurge. And her struggle is about how environmental damage has become so much more tangible and personal to her as she's dealing with spirits which really makes her wonder if sometimes Rage is the right answer to a problem. Meanwhile, one part of her still wants to cling to her convictions as a human-rights-activist and she thinks Garou go too far in persecuting their war against the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T12:39:59-07:00","id":1524763,"title":"","content":"The Green Knights are one of those early period gems that I love and that I\u2019d love to take some time to flesh our more one day. While the name is already pretty clear cut on the face of it (Green for the environment and Knights because they\u2019re warriors/guardians) the name also feels evocative of the Arthurian mythos in particular the famous Green Knight of Gawain &amp; the Green Knight. To those unfamiliar with the story the Green Knight is revealed to be one of the fair folk and so the story has the usual elements of mysterious helpers, eccentric games, and fairy tale logic. It\u2019s that element of the name which makes me wonder if there was ever any idea that the Green Knights might be a possible cross-over mechanism for Garou and Verbena Mages or Changelings on the environmental militancy tip.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T13:14:36-07:00","id":1524767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524727#post1524727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, for those with a sharp eye, that's 5 freebies for Attributes, 6 for Abilities, 1 for Backgrounds, 6 for Gnosis, and 2 for WP, for a grand total of 20 freebie points. Damn. It's been a while since I've seen a character sheet this out of wack points wise.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>The high level of Gnosis is probably intended so she can make use of her Mother's Touch Gift many times. You must expend Gnosis to activate that Gift. Given how early this sourcebook is in the development of the game, the author could have been thinking &quot;I need a healer for the other PCs&quot; when statting her out.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T13:54:37-07:00","id":1524768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524024#post1524024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Warsinger</b> (Lupus Galliard)<br /> <br /> So, this one starts out with another song quote. But somewhat surprisingly, it's by Jethro Tull. I was honestly expecting another female artist. It would've made an interesting and appropriate theme, if nothing else. There's also a second quote from John Irving's <i>The Hotel New Hampshire. </i>I actually find this mildly annoying. The lay out for a template write up can only include so many words, about 500 IIRC. So, including an extra quote is effectively padding which wastes words that could be better spent on the actual character.<br /> <br /> That said, this is an interesting character. Born as a wolf, after undergoing the first change she decided that being human was much more fun and exciting. Especially human music. She taught herself to play guitar. Being a werewolf is one big party to her.<br /> <br /> It describes her as being &quot;trained as a witch&quot; and Rituals being her life blood. This is something I'll come back to in a bit. She may be part of the Moon-Daughters camp, but it's not exactly clear on that aspect.<br /> <br /> Her equipment, in addition to a trench knife and sawed-off shotgun, includes a &quot;serious collection of guitars, amps, and hard rock CDs.&quot; Now you may be asking yourself, &quot;Self, just how does a wolf-born Garou come to own a bunch of somewhat expensive musical instruments and equipment?&quot; And the answer to that is apparently that she has 2 dots in Resources. There's probably a really weird and potentially interesting backstory behind that. Unfortunately, absolutely nothing in this write up mentions it. I'll also mention that she has 4 dots in Performance with a specialization in &quot;Guitar&quot;. Lupus, of course, have restrictions on certain Skills and Knowledges they can use their basic points on, based on the idea that they'd have no way to learn them before their first change. Performance isn't one of those restricted Skills, but I sort of feel like specializing in &quot;Guitar&quot; is mildly violating the spirit of those restrictions. Likewise, I've always sort of wondered why Lupus didn't also have certain restrictions on some Backgrounds. Like, for example, Resources. So, all in all, this is just sort of a weird aspect of this character.<br /> <br /> The character image is really great. Probably my favorite of the bunch, to be honest. The same sort of early 90s GenX riot grrl archetype as the Street Rat, just as an attractive and hot wild child instead of an ugly and obnoxious gutter punk. She's wearing cut off shorts and a crop top, with tattoos (including one on her arm that's the tribe symbol that apparently turns into a dragon or something near the bottom). And holding a bloody knife. I like it quite a bit.<br /> <br /> Attributes have Physicals as secondary, and once again with an extra dot, for a 3/3/3 spread. Socials are primary, with a 4/3/3 spread. That leaves Mentals as tertiary, with a 1/2/3 spread. So she's meant to be kind of oblivious, I guess? The text doesn't really indicate anything about it.<br /> For Abilities, Talents are primary with an extra dot. Brawl, Expression, and Streetwise are 3 each, Alertness and Intimidation are 2 each, and Primal Urge is 1. (I always kind of wondered why Streetwise wasn't on the list of restricted abilities.) Skills are secondary with an extra dot. Besides that 4 in Performance, she has 2 each in Drive and Survival, and 1 each in Melee and Repair. Drive is one of the restricted skills for Lupus. (You'd think maybe Repair would be as well, but no.) Knowledge is tertiary, with 1 dot each in Enigmas and Occult, and 3 dots in ... Music? It's sort of penciled in at the very bottom of the official list of knowledges. Remember what I said earlier about the character being trained as a witch and loving Rituals. Well, she has no points in the Rituals knowledge. I feel those Music dots are a total waste and should've been spent to raise Rituals and Occult or Enigmas to 2. (Also, the character has a sawed-off shotgun, but no Firearms.)<br /> <br /> Backgrounds are 2 each in Contacts and Resources. Rage is 6, which seems mostly OK for this character. Gnosis is ... 3. Yeah, Lupus get that at 5 minimum. So, I've no idea what's going on here. Either a misprint or a mistake on the writer's part. But if the latter, then the Developer should've caught it during the redlining of the first draft. Willpower is also 6.<br /> <br /> Once again, I don't hate this character. It's actually pretty interesting. But I'm not sure it's the best example of a Black Fury, especially a Black Fury Lupus. Even with the Galliard aspect, I feel like this is stuck in a lot of the very early presentation of &quot;Galliard = Musician/Performer&quot;. Especially the whole rock guitarist thing. If this character had been one of the templates in Ways of the Wolf (a book I'll be getting to very soon), I think it would have fit better. Especially if it had been the Ragabash one.<br /> <br /> I also find it kind of bizarre that we have a Homid character who is &quot;more wolf than wolf&quot; and a Lupus character who wants to be a human. I honestly can't help but wonder if it'd been better if they'd been switched, with the Theurge being a Lupus and this one being a Homid.<br /> <br /> Next (hopefully tomorrow), the Ahroun, and some final thoughts.<br /> <br /> After that, I'm debating if I should do Bone Gnawers or Ways of the Wolf next.</div> </div> </div> </div>A few interesting facts about this template<br /> 1. Sawed-off shotgun with no firearms skill? You don't have to actually use it, the intimidation factor is good enough<br /> 2. Resources for lupus? That's no problem for me either. I believe that, as a neophyte, she could fanatically learn to play guitar so she could play on the streets and earn some money. If the rest of her sept could afford to buy her some guitars, amps and CDs they would get a fanatically devoted member. Or maybe she found some of them in the thrash can.<br /> <br /> I actually used this template during my games. She was a member of a heavy metal band (Spooky Tooth like), composed also of Janet Crowley (the founder, Gaillard Shadow Lord bassist from Rite of Passage), Gaillard template from Glass Walkers tribebook on vocals and lead guitar and Chris Wlodkowsky, Get of Fenris kinfolk drummer mentioned in Kinfolk: Unsung Heroes. Me and my players even wrote some lyrics, created a name and we almost created a real band based on this. One of the best moments during our games was when this template wanted to get something for Chris birthday and she bought him an Iron Maiden CD, but the original Maiden's one, from 1969.<br /> <br /> And another fun fact: in the cutscenes for the cancelled Heart of Gaia video game is a Black Fury called Warsinger that looks very similar to this template.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T14:34:42-07:00","id":1524770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524644#post1524644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is more likely the absent mom (&quot;Mom was God knows where&quot;) is the Garou parent, and she left the father sometime after Janet was born to do Garou things. His wife leaving him is what probably drove him to drink. The real question for the ST is whether the mom should still be alive, or if she died on quest and that is why she never came back.<br /> <br /> The cop is probably just a Shadow Lord kinfolk who can recognize the signs.<br /> <br /> This character is easier to integrate into Rage Across New York than others because she is obviously urban based. But there still needs some work tying things together. We know there are Shadow Lords inside the city. The 2e corebook's description of the Sept of the Green has Zachary Ellsion, but he's not mentioned in 1e. But RANY does have Carleson Ruah in the city. But more intriguing is the leader of the Shadow Lords living in the wilderness, Sylvan-Ivanovich-Sylvan. She's middle-aged, has Pure Breed 1, and has black hair like Janet Crowley. As ST, I'd be very tempted to make this NPC Janet's mother. She would know she is Janet's mother, but I would let the PC figure it out herself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I once run a game using those characters. It didn't go well but that's another story. In Poland some W:tA sourcebooks was published in mid 90-s:<br /> 2nd edition core rulebook <br /> Player's guide<br /> Storyteller's guide<br /> Rite of Passage poorly converted for 2nd edition <br /> Under a Blood Red Moon poorly translated and converted for 2nd edition <br /> When will you rage<br /> Some adventures and materials from White Wolf magazine (Malafaxus trilogy, Night of Rage and Road to Heaven).<br /> I ran all of them as a campaign, to make myself familiar with the world. Later, in early 2000's access to the rest World of Darkness materials and used one of the Nosferatu template as Janet's mother. She was killed during war in Chicago but Janet didn't know that untill she found a photo among the stuff one of the fallen NPCs had. The same her father had. That was then she found out about her mother and it was one of most emotional moment during that campaign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-01T17:53:18-07:00","id":1524892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524763#post1524763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It\u2019s that element of the name which makes me wonder if there was ever any idea that the Green Knights might be a possible cross-over mechanism for Garou and Verbena Mages or Changelings on the environmental militancy tip.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is that one Eco Terrorist template in the original Verbena book. I think I ended up making them a sub-faction of the Moonseekers IRRC.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-01T17:58:30-07:00","id":1524893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524767#post1524767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The high level of Gnosis is probably intended so she can make use of her Mother's Touch Gift many times. You must expend Gnosis to activate that Gift. Given how early this sourcebook is in the development of the game, the author could have been thinking &quot;I need a healer for the other PCs&quot; when statting her out.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I kind of get the impression that some of the planning behind these characters was the &quot;I need a Fighter, a back-up Fighter, a Cleric, a Wizard, and a Rogue&quot; sort of 2nd ed AD&amp;D approach. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-01T18:47:49-07:00","id":1524895,"title":"","content":"<b>Whisperer / Tormented Soul</b> (Metis Theurge Uktena)<br /> <br /> And ... damn, I'm not really sure where to start with this one. <br /> <br /> Obviously this is when they were still trying to figure out some of the finer points about this Breed. They're born misformed and cursed. In this case, the character, apparently male, I presume, is completely hairless. And also either a paranoid schizophrenic or under constant assault by spirits of the Wyrm. Maybe both. <br /> <br /> Apparently he's had voices whispering in his head offering power and pleasure, apparently in the form of being able to violate others, since before his First Change. Apparently these voices also sometimes offered up the hidden secrets of others (which honestly would've been a more interesting angle to pursue her IMO). And now he's been tossed into this new ad hoc pack, apparently as much a way to make him someone else's problem as anything else, and he fully expects them to betray him and it's kind of implied that he plans to turn on them first, and most likely run off to join the Black Spiral Dancers. <br /> <br /> First edition Uktena leaned really heavy into the whole &quot;they practice black magic&quot; angle, with parts of their write up reading more like what you would expect from the Shadow Lords at times. And this character leans so hard into that aspect that it pretty much falls over on its face. <br /> <br /> The image is of a hairless werewolf in Crinos form, arms crossed and a scowl on his face. He's wearing a slightly ragged tunic, with a few adornments to indicate &quot;Native American&quot; or something along those lines. It's not a terrible image. Just not a very good one either. <br /> <br /> For Attributes, Physicals are secondary, with a 2/2/4 split. This seems to fit somewhat with the brief mention of his abusive upbringing. Socials are tertiary, with all points dumped into Manipulation giving him a 1/4/1 spread. Mental is primary, with 2/4/4. That's a lot of fours. I don't think this is bad, but I do worry about a character who is really powerful in his fortes and almost crippled in Social situations.<br /> One thing I noticed with Vampire's Nosferatu characters was that it was really easy to take advantage of their clan weakness and only spread your Social dots among two traits instead of three, often resulting in characters who were at least slightly stronger than average in Charisma or Manipulation if not outright powerhouses in them with a 4/5/0 split if you went primary. I kind of feel like this was trying to repeat that tactic using the Metis deformity rule as an excuse to not spend any points on Appearance (or Charisma, since he's an unstable introvert). I suspect that if I ever get to a Metis character who has more than 2 dots in Appearance, I'm going to get ridiculously excited over it. <br /> <br /> For Abilities, Talents are secondary, with 3 each in Dodge and Subterfuge, and 1 each in Brawl, Intimidation, and Primal Urge. Skills are tertiary with an extra dot, with 3 in Survival, 2 in Stealth, and 1 in Melee. Knowledge is primary with an extra dot from freebies, for a 4 in Occult, 3 each in Enigmas and Rituals, and 2 each in Investigation and Science. <br /> Generally, these are all OK. But I can't help but feel like he has these abilities just because that's what a Theurge would be expected to have as opposed to because they are part of a thought out background and character development. <br /> <br /> Uktena get 4 Background points in 1st ed, and this has one extra from Freebies. He has 2 each in Rites and Fetish (a Spirit Tracer), and 1 in Pack Totem. I'd almost question why a character like this would have the Pack Totem background, but I know it's because all of them have one dot in it so the players can build the Pack Totem. (I sometimes wonder if they shouldn't have just given every PC a free dot in that background.) As for the others, they make sense, but still have that &quot;this is what a Theurge should have&quot; feel to them.<br /> <br /> Rage is the base 2 for Theurge. Gnosis is 6. Willpower is 6.<br /> <br /> So ... There just isn't a lot here besides &quot;he's crazy and/or corrupted and isn't going to play well with others&quot;. That in and of itself isn't a deal breaker for me, but I'd have to really trust the person playing that kind of character before I'd allow it in a game I was trying to run. I don't think it's a good concept for a scenario like this where everyone is likely to be new to the game, and possibly even new to roleplaying. <br /> <br /> I think if you toned it down a notch or three and fleshed out his personality and background some, you might have something worthwhile here. At least give him a hobby or some sort of hook you can use to build on the idea of him not betraying the rest of the PCs and becoming an NPC villain. But as it is, this feels more like a first draft of a concept rather than a fully realized character. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-01T21:38:57-07:00","id":1524899,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <b>Story/Character: </b>Yeah, okay. This is just bad in terms of a starting character. For one, this is the ONLY Indigenous character of the lot. Second, this is also the only Garou Born template. This means that this character being a voice-hearing future-BSD really isn't sitting well with me.<br /> <br /> On a personal note, I don't really get the hints that this character was often going to be killed. They were spared as a cub and nothing in the backstory says they are particularly rebellious. Garou aren't really the type to keep a garou born cub around if they don't want to. They do abuse them, but generally don't try to kill them for nothing.<br /> <br /> Now, being a Garou Born, some grumpiness is expected. But the way Whisperer is set up, this PC does not play well with others and is almost always antagonistic towards them. And that is not something you want from a template. Nevermind that playing out a character like this takes a lot of skill and a lot of trust from the ST.<br /> <br /> The voices are a problem on their own, as they mean this PC needs even more ST attention than your typical theurge.<br /> <br /> Then there is the fact that the BSD bad guy from this book ALSO heard voices that pushed her to dance.<br /> <br /> This character requires a lot of skill to play in a group and even then they are a ticking timebomb. This is an EXTREMELY poor choice as a starting Garou Born AND a Ghost Council member. Especially as the text ends with a pretty big hint that this PC will dance the spiral since BSDs are the only ones that understand them.<br /> <br /> Which, given this character is the second ever garou born template, has some unfortunate implications. Joining the BSDs should be something a character is driven to during the course of the chronicle. Not part of the character's concept in a book showing example PCs.<br /> <br /> Characters like this are what I call disruptive characters. Characters whose issues take up attention and time from other characters and who spend way too much time going solo.<br /> <br /> <b>Stats:</b><br /> <br /> In Attributes, I feel Perception and Wits should be shifted, as the backstory states this character is a bit TOO perceptive at times.<br /> <br /> The socials need some care as well, as this character is very much NOT a Manipulation 4 character. Not only does it imply that they are good at using others which is not what the text says, they are at 4 dice for any rites. Nevermind anything related to spirits. The image also is not app 1. Yes, they are hairless but not in an ugly way.<br /> <br /> Talents looks extremely clumsy. For one, no Alertness for a character constantly hearing stuff? The theme of a skilled manipulator continues with Subterfuge 3, which again doesn't match the backstory. Dodge 3 only makes sense if you assume this character has had to dodge a LOT of things, which then runs counter to the 7 dice in lying. Primal-Urge should be higher on a nature raised PC as should Brawl. Intimidation would make more sense for a character that isn't the punching bag.<br /> <br /> Skills has a random melee, but otherwise is solid.<br /> <br /> Knowledges looks good until we come to 2 dots in science. Where did those come from? What science would this isolated kid know? Unless it refers to the knowledge of poisons. As if this PC didn't need more obvious &quot;This guy is EVIL&quot; hints.<br /> <br /> Backgrounds have randomly a two dot fetish that is not mentioned in the backstory. Given that this character barely survived until now, having a fetish makes no sense.<br /> <br /> All in all, extremely volatile and hard to play with very little pay-off. The fact that the book says more than one lupus PC would be an issue, when THIS character is in the mix is hilariously tone deaf.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-02T01:12:46-07:00","id":1524900,"title":"","content":"Honestly, for the past twenty years, my first thought for a character of that particular Tribe and Breed has often been a Galliard I refer to as &quot;Middle Brother's Memory&quot;, a member of the Ghost Dance camp who, having no ties to any human tribe/nation is instead fixated on learning and uncovering everything they can about the lost North American Tribe and putting it to use.<br /> I'm not exactly sure what the best idea for a Theurge would be, but I am pretty sure &quot;BSD in the making&quot; isn't it. Some sort of necromancer who hears ghosts, maybe? A computer hacker who found a much needed social outlet via early BBS/message boards? (That might be more suitable for a Glass Walker, especially this early in the game.) Someone who takes extreme risks to dig up hidden and forbidden lore because they secretly consider their life less important than Homid or Lupus Garou?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edi