ach in Dodge and Subterfuge, and 1 each in Brawl, Intimidation, and Primal Urge. Skills are tertiary with an extra dot, with 3 in Survival, 2 in Stealth, and 1 in Melee. Knowledge is primary with an extra dot from freebies, for a 4 in Occult, 3 each in Enigmas and Rituals, and 2 each in Investigation and Science.<br /> Generally, these are all OK. But I can't help but feel like he has these abilities just because that's what a Theurge would be expected to have as opposed to because they are part of a thought out background and character development.<br /> <br /> Uktena get 4 Background points in 1st ed, and this has one extra from Freebies. He has 2 each in Rites and Fetish (a Spirit Tracer), and 1 in Pack Totem. I'd almost question why a character like this would have the Pack Totem background, but I know it's because all of them have one dot in it so the players can build the Pack Totem. (I sometimes wonder if they shouldn't have just given every PC a free dot in that background.) As for the others, they make sense, but still have that &quot;this is what a Theurge should have&quot; feel to them.<br /> <br /> Rage is the base 2 for Theurge. Gnosis is 6. Willpower is 6.<br /> <br /> So ... There just isn't a lot here besides &quot;he's crazy and/or corrupted and isn't going to play well with others&quot;. That in and of itself isn't a deal breaker for me, but I'd have to really trust the person playing that kind of character before I'd allow it in a game I was trying to run. I don't think it's a good concept for a scenario like this where everyone is likely to be new to the game, and possibly even new to roleplaying.<br /> <br /> I think if you toned it down a notch or three and fleshed out his personality and background some, you might have something worthwhile here. At least give him a hobby or some sort of hook you can use to build on the idea of him not betraying the rest of the PCs and becoming an NPC villain. But as it is, this feels more like a first draft of a concept rather than a fully realized character.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't agree with you, I believe that, with a good player, it could be very deep and emotional character.<br /> <br /> As for attributes I think that it's one of the best spreads for a Theurge. I believe that many abused will have high stamina (to withstand the beatings), high manipulation (to avoid the beatings) and high wits and inteligence (to invent the ways to avoid the beatings). Mechanically one of the most important stats for Theurge are manipulation and wits.<br /> <br /> As for skills I think that they reflect both the abuse and the upbringing in the sept (hence high occult). Totem as a background? There's a suggestion that, after meating with Billy, a Bear totem can choose this pack. And they all have 5 Totem Background points to purchase it. As for this Uktena it can reflect some kind of spirit messenger from one of the more aggressive totems to abus... ehem, harden this character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-02T02:45:07-07:00","id":1524903,"title":"","content":"I think this one is just bad. With this template the character starts out with these beats:<ul><li>fully embracing the idea of Metis as social outcasts disliked by everyone</li> <li>character hears voices (sometimes ghosts but the character also comes off as a paranoid schizophrenic)</li> <li>character believes the other PCs are plotting against him</li> <li>he has some sympathy for the BSD and if things get worse will join them</li> </ul>What makes this so bad is to make this character playable, the only thing you're doing is essentially running away from all of that. Because of the way things stand in this template, this character joining the BSD at some point is the reasonable conclusion to this template's story. He's being mistreated, he hears voices, he's paranoid to the point that he thinks of the other PCs as enemies and what some of the voices urge him to do is to join the BSD. The real challenge here is to conceive of a scenario where this character wouldn't be this obstacle to other players and end up joining the antagonists. Even in the best of times, you would need both a player and an ST working together to turn this character into something playable.<br /> <br /> Stat-wise it's a <i>very narrow</i> selection of how the dots have been distributed. Already, having a distribution like Cha 1, Man 4, App 1 conjures a very extreme character. Then Occult 4 is also interesting because... how did he acquire that? But also with how his upbringing was described, how did he acquire Science 2? And with the Backgrounds, it's also a mystery where the Fetish has come from.<br /> <br /> As for alternative depictions... If we stay with this one character being a Metis, you could go with Bone Gnawers, I think, and while he has been mistreated early on and ultimately rejected by his old Tribe, the Bone Gnawers have taken him in and now he wants to prove himself to be worthy of that mercy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-02T04:39:15-07:00","id":1524906,"title":"","content":"As someone who has done quite a few garou born characters over the...decades I've been playing, here are my fixes to Whisperer;<br /> <br /> -Either voices or hairlessness, two deformities are a chore to keep track of and since this is a STARTING character, you need to offer some leeway.<br /> <br /> -Make the character's existence something important, say a rescued BSD pup or an omen brought to life. Give a sense WHY this character would be tolerated in their sept.<br /> <br /> -Whisperer is in a new environment that is not as hostile as their old home, plus with a pack that looks up to them for what they know about the spirits. Even if they were prepared to be grumpy and hate them, this new situation should make Whisperer pause and ponder.<br /> <br /> -Make joining the BSDs something that Whisperer sees as an INSULT, they are GAIAN and they will not fall! Doesn't mean they can't, just that it is not their first option.<br /> <br /> -Make socials 3/2/2. Nothing in the deformity description in the 1st ed book says it is a forced app 1. Just that you have penalties to your appearance.<br /> <br /> -Remove fetish or give it a backstory reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-02T05:04:33-07:00","id":1524907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524906#post1524906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Make the character's existence something important, say a rescued BSD pup or an omen brought to life. Give a sense WHY this character would be tolerated in their sept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually that brings up another issue with the template I forgot to mention. There's the suggestion that the reason why he was kept around is that in these whispers that he hears sometimes he would get useful info. But that &quot;ability&quot; is nowhere to be seen on the character-sheet. Also, this isn't an ability inherent to either being a Metis, a Theurge or being part of the Older Brother Tribe. So the only way this could work is if you get ST-approval first - which isn't something you should find on a character-template for an introductory adventure. And of course, how this whole &quot;whisper&quot;-thing works represents extra work for the ST.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-02T05:12:17-07:00","id":1524908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524907#post1524907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually that brings up another issue with the template I forgot to mention. There's the suggestion that the reason why he was kept around is that in these whispers that he hears sometimes he would get useful info. But that &quot;ability&quot; is nowhere to be seen on the character-sheet. Also, this isn't an ability inherent to either being a Metis, a Theurge or being part of the Older Brother Tribe. So the only way this could work is if you get ST-approval first - which isn't something you should find on a character-template for an introductory adventure. And of course, how this whole &quot;whisper&quot;-thing works represents extra work for the ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, neither is the hairless deformity seen. But yeah, we are not given any stats/mechanics for the voices. With modern tools, you could have it be a Numina of a Bane, I guess.<br /> <br /> I still want to point this out; Lupus were seen as disruptive to the story. But Whisperer was fine, somehow? The reason they are in here is, I think, because all of these characters were PCs during a playtest of this story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-02T08:04:47-07:00","id":1524917,"title":"","content":"It occurred to me that one possible fix would be to replace the two dots in Fetish with Mentor, representing an older member of the Tribe who has looked after and guided him. This would provide the character both an extra motivation for wanting to pass the Rite and for not wanting to bring shame upon their mentor by, you know, falling to the Wyrm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-02T08:19:33-07:00","id":1524919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524917#post1524917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It occurred to me that one possible fix would be to replace the two dots in Fetish with Mentor, representing an older member of the Tribe who has looked after and guided him. This would provide the character both an extra motivation for wanting to pass the Rite and for not wanting to bring shame upon their mentor by, you know, falling to the Wyrm.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh, tha'd be good.<br /> <br /> I do honestly wonder why they chose this angstball mcTraitorson. Were they trying for an edgy &quot;But look, the BAD guys treat the garou born better!&quot; thing? Looking the book over, there seems to be no thought put into the fact that Whisperer might just join the main bad guy.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-02T08:41:25-07:00","id":1524923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524908#post1524908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, neither is the hairless deformity seen. But yeah, we are not given any stats/mechanics for the voices. With modern tools, you could have it be a Numina of a Bane, I guess.<br /> <br /> I still want to point this out; Lupus were seen as disruptive to the story. But Whisperer was fine, somehow? The reason they are in here is, I think, because all of these characters were PCs during a playtest of this story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah and if you take this template to say that both the whispers and the hairlessness are the result of Metis-deformities, then it's striking how the template is defined by these. It's all about the flaws he was born with and sketching out an arc of seemingly depressing inevitability that takes him to possibly joining up with the BSD. He was born with those deformities, he was treated badly and in the way it's portrayed, his detractors are right: He is a liability. But it's like we're talking about original sin here, the character's biggest issue is stuff he was born with and then it's all downhill from there pretty much in how it's described. I don't know but the more I think about it the less I like the whole concept.<br /> <br /> And then it really is a weird thing to say that Lupus are the disruptive Breed. In a human-dominated world the wolf-born are at a disadvantage, sure, but it doesn't come even close to the level of disruption you get with such a depressing and pessimistic portrayal of Metis.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-02T09:17:03-07:00","id":1524925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524923#post1524923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah and if you take this template to say that both the whispers and the hairlessness are the result of Metis-deformities, then it's striking how the template is defined by these. It's all about the flaws he was born with and sketching out an arc of seemingly depressing inevitability that takes him to possibly joining up with the BSD. He was born with those deformities, he was treated badly and in the way it's portrayed, his detractors are right: He is a liability. But it's like we're talking about original sin here, the character's biggest issue is stuff he was born with and then it's all downhill from there pretty much in how it's described. I don't know but the more I think about it the less I like the whole concept.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I did some random RPG digging a year back and ran into Ravenloft's Caliban. They read veeeeery much like a proto-type to the garou born. I believe White Wolf had a hand in Ravenloft, which is why I'm mentioning it.<br /> <br /> I guess the point of the character is that if you mistreat people, they will turn on you. But in media, it is so common for this to be a &quot;Character is different---&gt;Character gets treated like shit---&gt;Character turns evil' pipeline, where the lesson of compassion is instead made into a &quot;SEE, the disabled person WAS evil!&quot; one. And I think your note of the original sin hits the nail on the head, that's what this is meant to evoke.<br /> <br /> Now that I think about it, there were two reactions to Whisperer later in WtA books. The First Ronin is said to be hairless AND the Older Brother 1st ed tribebook's comic stars a Older Brother Theurge Garou Born with no fur.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-02T09:40:19-07:00","id":1524927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524925#post1524925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did some random RPG digging a year back and ran into Ravenloft's Caliban. They read veeeeery much like a proto-type to the garou born. I believe White Wolf had a hand in Ravenloft, which is why I'm mentioning it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The WWGS/Arthaus 3rd ed of Ravenloft came out just after the turn of the millennium. The Caliban were an effort to adapt the 3rd ed D&amp;D Half-Orcs to a setting that had no Orcs. Instead they drew on the trope from classic Gothic fiction of people born misformed and twisted, often as the result of some sort of family curse or other event they had no control over. The Metis, being the result of spiritual incest, also draw on this trope, especially the very Gothic idea of the sins of the parents being visited upon the child. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-02T13:59:17-07:00","id":1524932,"title":"","content":"I think there are two separate concepts combined into one character. There's nothing bad about that. Mixing different ideas can lead to stronger, more interesting characters. But sometimes multiple ideas can work against each other, diluting each concept instead of making a stronger one.<br /> <br /> The hairlessness is the metis concept as is any social outcast as a result. By itself, fairly standard metis. Hairless is even one of the ten examples of malformities given in the 1e corebook. This aspect for this character is very harsh and negative, but other early 1e metis characters don't have it so bad and are portrayed more noble and compassionate and are even looked out for by certain other Garou.<br /> <br /> Then there is the spirit whisperer concept that I don't think is based on the character's breed. It's because of their tribe. 1e WtA emphasized the Uktena as being dark and mysterious. Their members were unfriendly to other tribes, being sullen and introverted. They dealt with malevolent spirits of the Deep Umbra, and jealously guarded their sacred sites. It's part of 1e Werewolf being much less epic heroic fantasy and more dark fantasy gothic horror oriented with many Garou having darker edges to them. Later editions would deemphasize that, and the Uktena being a tribe that included other peoples was more emphasized and the tribe portrayed more positively.<br /> <br /> I will also say that while the 1e corebook obviously mentions the homid ethnic heritage of these Garou tribes, that I think it is really the upcoming tribebooks that heavily concentrated on the human ethnic groups as a means to develop each tribe. That came at the expense of a more broader view of the tribe as cultic devotees to their tribal totems. The first approaching emphasized the side of their human kinfolk and homids. The latter would emphasize more about the Garou as not really being human, not even the homids raised in human culture.<br /> <br /> In this template's case, the writer wanted to combine the two concepts for a tormented soul concept. On one level, I think this is totally fine. Lots of players could enjoy playing this concept. It's totally valid. Could this concept be disruptive or prove too difficult or not fun for some players? Of course. I don't think having such a concept here is wrong though. I think the writers are showing the diversity of concepts that are possible by mixing tribes, auspices, and breeds. My only real complaint is that so many of these templates use the obvious stereotypical combinations (a Get of Fenris Ahroun, a Children of Gaia Philodox, an Uktena theurge). Players will already naturally combine those aspects and come up with obvious character concepts for them. More unusual combinations would be better to showcasing options.<br /> <br /> I've never actually known anyone who actually played any template in any game. It was mostly people reviewing concepts before creating their own character. The only time I ever saw someone play a template is when someone's friend unexpectedly showed up to play so the ST quickly grabbed a book and told them to run a character based on this (with the assumption the player could either continue to play a more personalized version next time, or create their own PC with this one becoming an NPC). So I don't think a possibly disruptive template could doom the game. I doubt any gaming group ever used these templates, certainly not all of them, for a PC pack.<br /> <br /> I will repeat that my earlier post that as characters meant for the Sept of the Green / Rage Across New York setting, there is insufficient local knowledge to allow the ST to actually explain the setting. The ST would need to do some work to integrate the character with the actual setting. Not a dealbreaker, but there really should be a one page note for the ST with advice on how to do so. In RANY only the Sept of the White Water (at Niagara Falls) has Uktena. It's a mixed sept with Fianna (because of that tribe's aid in regaining this caern from the Wyrm) but still ruled by Uktena. As written there is no connection between the Sept of the White Water and the Sept of the Green. That can be justified because in the sourcebook's lore because Frederick Law Olmstead was a Fianna kinfolk, and he was involved in both the creation of Central Park and making Niagara a state park. So there's an obvious connection for the ST to build on. But I think that should be spelled out. In general, there should have been explicit information about the other nearby caerns sending at least some of their cubs to the Sept of the Green for their Rite of Passage. These templates just aren't concepts for a Central Park caern. That's the only way to justify the diversity of these templates and whatever concepts the players will create and putting all of them at the Sept of the Green.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-02T16:13:35-07:00","id":1524939,"title":"","content":"One of my favorite oddities from the 1st ed is the mention of how Uktena organize their young packs like street gangs. That and that abandoned warehouses and tenement basements are among the places they prefer to have their Caerns. I suspect this was meant to be part of how their human culture was meant to draw from African American and various immigrant populations who tended to cluster in the poorer parts of urban areas that had a lot of gang activity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-02T17:32:36-07:00","id":1524945,"title":"","content":"<b>Curtis Worrell / Lay About</b> (Homid Glass Walker Ragabash)<br /> <br /> So, Curtis is apparently a fairly normal young man, I presume from NYC or the surrounding area (Jersey, Conn., Long Island, etc.). In his own way, he's as much a delinquent as Janet Crowley was. Skipping school, stealing stuff from the local convenience store (I presume shoplifting rather than armed robbery), hacking into his school's computer system, and even the odd drug dealing. <br /> In the 10th grade, his computer started talking to him. Then a car. And other things. I really do like this detail. Once again, it's one of those reasons I wish we'd got a second edition of this book that went into a lot more detail about how Homids grow up and the weird stuff that often happens as the First Change nears and they eventually enter a whole new world. <br /> Some heavies in suits and shades rolled up on him on the sidewalk one day. He tried to run, but streets kept dead-ending or being blocked with trash. They caught him and tossed him in the back of a limo with a talking dog. <br /> While I do appreciate these interesting details about the First Change, I do somewhat lament that we aren't learning more about Curtis as a character. But at the very least, it does help understand the idea of a guy who still feels a little bit like he's in over his head and isn't happy about it. <br /> <br /> At least he likes the easy access to money and influence that comes from being one of the Glass Walkers, as well as the physical power of being a werewolf. But he fully lives up to the Tribe's stereotype of being totally urban oriented and hating the wilderness. He's participating with this pack Rite mainly out of fear of his elders, but will want to bail as soon as the going gets tough. <br /> <br /> There seemed to be a constant theme in 1st ed about Ragabash being cowardly, perhaps almost more so than being irksome troublemakers. If I had to guess, I'd presume that this is somehow based on them having the lowest starting Rage. Again, this was back when Rage was still kind of just a power stat rather than something that had an impact on your personality. But between this guy and the Ragabash template in Ways of the Wolf, it's really kind of noticeable. And, at least personally, mildly annoying. So I'm really glad it's something the game moved away from by the time the Tribebooks started coming out. <br /> <br /> The image is of a young man in slacks and a suit jacket. There's absolutely nothing remarkable about it, and you could just as easily use it as an image for a Vampire template. Not that there's anything wrong with this. I think it fits the character. <br /> <br /> I will mention that I'm not really a fan of the concept of &quot;Lay About&quot;. It's similar to how I didn't really care for those Vampire templates who had any concept involving the term &quot;wannabe&quot;. It kind of feels like the character is being set up to be thought of as a bit of a loser. I would really prefer something like &quot;Young Hustler&quot;, which would kind of refocus him into someone who is out to get ahead rather than just sort of coast. <br /> <br /> For Attributes, Physicals are tertiary with one additional dot from freebies, for 2/3/2. Socials are primary, with 3/4/3. Mental is secondary with 2/2/4. I feel like maybe his Intelligence should be a little higher, but other than that, these are fine. <br /> <br /> With Abilities, Talents are primary with one extra dot from freebies. Expression, Streetwise, and Subterfuge are 3 each, a 2 in Athletics, and 1 each in Brawl, Dodge, and Empathy. <br /> Skills are secondary with one extra dot (again), with 3 each in Stealth and Firearms, a 2 in Drive, and 1 each in Etiquette and Repair. <br /> That leaves Knowledge as tertiary, which is perhaps a little unusual for a Homid Glass Walker. A 2 in Computer, and 1 each in Linguistics, Politics, and Science. <br /> These aren't bad, but I feel like they could use a little tweaking. I'd probably move that one dot in Linguistics to Computers, to better reflect what the write up says about his hacking. I'm not really sure about the Firearms. I can't help but feel like this is one of those &quot;well, he's the Glass Walker, so he's the one who uses a gun&quot; kind of thought processes. His write up doesn't really imply the kind of kid who'd routinely carry a gun, so maybe drop that a level and either use the freebies for something else or bump Repair to 2. Maybe also take one of the Athletics dots and move it to Alertness. <br /> <br /> Glass Walkers got 4 Background dots in 1st ed, and he has an extra from freebies. 2 are in Resources, and 1 each in Pack Totem, Contacts, and Fetish (Harmony Flute). I'm not sure why he needs a Harmony Flute. If it's needed for the story, it feels like Linda would be a more suitable candidate to have such a thing. The rest are fine. If doing this with 2nd ed Rules, I'd probably go with Resources and Contacts at 2 and Pack Totem at 1. <br /> <br /> Rage and Gnosis are both at 2, with Willpower at 4. I've not idea why he and Janet have such low WP compared to the other three characters. He also seems to be missing a freebie point. I'd spend it on WP. I think that dot in Gnosis could be better spent on another Ability dot. Perhaps Dodge or Alertness. <br /> <br /> Overall, this isn't a bad character. I think there's enough to work with here, but it could benefit from a little fine tuning and some moving away from the idea of Ragabash as cowardly. <br /> <br /> So, that was the group from Rite of Passage. Overall, they were fairly solid, with the exception of Whisperer (who suffers from both a lack of character depth and a bad case of not playing well with others). This was the first sourcebook released for the game, so they all lean pretty heavily into their Tribal and Auspice stereotypes. I don't think this is necessarily bad for something this early in the game, especially for new players who might be looking for the easiest character hooks to play. But I think all of these would benefit from some fine tuning based on how the game evolved over the years. <br /> <br /> Next, I'll be doing Bone Gnawers. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-02T18:17:51-07:00","id":1524949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524932#post1524932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there are two separate concepts combined into one character. There's nothing bad about that. Mixing different ideas can lead to stronger, more interesting characters. But sometimes multiple ideas can work against each other, diluting each concept instead of making a stronger one.<br /> <br /> The hairlessness is the metis concept as is any social outcast as a result. By itself, fairly standard metis. Hairless is even one of the ten examples of malformities given in the 1e corebook. This aspect for this character is very harsh and negative, but other early 1e metis characters don't have it so bad and are portrayed more noble and compassionate and are even looked out for by certain other Garou.<br /> <br /> Then there is the spirit whisperer concept that I don't think is based on the character's breed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to disagree with this, it is very much based on the character's breed. The template itself says so, the BSDs are the only ones that understand and almost in every description of BSDs it is said they are mostly garou born and that many garou born from Gaian tribes join them due to mistreatment.<br /> <br /> Hence, a garou born wanting to join the Dancers to have SOME compassion is very much a cliche.<br /> <br /> Reading the 1st ed description is actually kind of... weird. I'm so used to the idea that all is negative for the garou born that the idea that 1) they are seen as noble and proud 2)that other garou born taking care of them makes their training EASIER than those of homid/lupus persuasion 3) that elders feel responsible for them and it is not stated in a negative light.<br /> <br /> Even the 20th ed Rage Across the World 20th ed describes the den parent as someone forced to babysit garou born cubs.<br /> <br /> This is like how Black Furies went from pretty chill spiritualists into the raging feminists in 2nd edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-03T03:19:49-07:00","id":1524966,"title":"","content":"The Layabout is a perfectly fine character, I think. The overall feel I get from it is that it very much thinks of Ragabash-as-a-rogue. It's this shifty character who's mainly in it for himself and wants to avoid trouble as much as possible. It doesn't really explain, though, where the Fetish and the three dots in Firearms come from.<br /> <br /> As for the group as a whole. I think the Galliard and the Ragabash look like they would work well together. The Children of Gaia Philodox in her aim to restrain violent acts would be in conflict with the Ahroun most of the time, one would assume. But I could also see that going down a path where the lupus Ahroun gets away from being this &quot;lone warrior&quot;-type as he gets closer to his Packmates. The only standout that I think doesn't work is the Whisperer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-03T08:21:47-07:00","id":1524976,"title":"","content":"Honestly, Curtis here shows what Whisperer should have been. He has hooks to use to make him get along, he wants to get out if shit gets hard but in a very vague sense because he is a dumb kid. It all reads like a very solid character for a first timer to play. In fact the common character that is recommended for first time players IS a homid GW Ragabash because that is the closest to a human a garou gets.<br /> <br /> To close this book out, I'll write a short scene to play with the dynamics of the only non-homids in the pack.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Finding the hairless wolf was too easy, their scent was not hidden even though they hid themselves in sight. Scratches shook his pelt, so many excessive human thoughts for such a simple thing.<br /> <br /> &quot;Whispers, hey, why're you here?&quot; Scratches began, ears perked, tongue lolling and tail wagging. They were supposed to be packmates, right? It was odd for a packmate to hide. The hairless war-shaped wolf turned to look at him, their ears tilted back and their tail between their legs. But they were baring their teeth. Huh?<br /> &quot;What do you want? I already made sure the area was safe,&quot; they muttered, Scratches sat on his haunches and tilted his head.<br /> &quot;Why're you sitting here all alone? It's not safe to be alone,&quot; he tried again, his entire body giving as many calming signals as it could. Whisperer snarled at him and despite himself, Scratches answered it with his own. Whisperer backed away a bit, hunching low. It looked odd in war-form.<br /> &quot;What do YOU care, I did my job. There is no need for me there,&quot; the hairless wolf hissed. Scratches sighed and shook his pelt once more. Damnit, why couldn't they see he was not going to attack them!?<br /> &quot;You are pack, you belong there,&quot; Scratches muttered and loped to Whisperer. The hairless wolf still looked scared, so scratches grabbed their scruff and began to drag them to the firepit. Whisperer froze and let themselves be dragged, shaking.<br /> &quot;Acting like a freshly weaned pup,&quot; Scratches muttered. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-03T12:03:24-07:00","id":1524981,"title":"","content":"I think Curtis Worrell is a decent start of a character, but once again the character sheet doesn't seem too match the actual description of the character. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> already mentioned the issues. Streetwise, Subterfuge, Firearms, and Stealth all seem too high at 3. Easily justified if the description made mention he built up these skills during his life as a cub though. But is this just a delinquent kid, or is he now more of a street criminal? Mention of &quot;that Lockheed stunt&quot; implies a much higher ability in Computer though. But an emphasis on hacking doesn't mesh with the more street criminal aspects of the character. That just seems to happen because of a general sense of &quot;Glass Walkers should have this stuff&quot;. I find the high ability of Expression and a fetish of a Harmony Flute to just be bizarre. The one obviously is for the other, but they don't make sense. 1e corebook was very limited in the types of fetishes and talens given, and none really work for this character. Better to just select another background and other abilities.<br /> <br /> This is all very &quot;generic Glass Walker&quot;. He wears a suit like a businessman. He has an ability set best used by criminals. He has resources for no explainable reason. He has computer skills. It is very unfocused. Building on the most likely portrayal of the character, I'd be more explicit that he's progressing from delinquent kid to minor hood and that his old high school friends are now minor local criminals and he is trying to make use of them. That would solve almost all the problems.<br /> <br /> Being an urban based character, he can easily slot into the Sept of the Green with little explanation.<br /> <br /> One thing that some of these templates assume is that Garou begin developing certain Gifts as part of the First Change or early life. Spirit Speech comes obviously to Whisper like Control Simple Machines comes to Curtis. There's no sense that Gifts just don't happen, but require teaching or blessing by a spirit. They just develop those abilities. I don't think that is a problem per se, but it would be better if the game somehow acknowledged that unusual things do happen to Garou undergoing their First Change that are not normally part of the rules. Similarly, 1e WtA often made use of metis cubs spontaneously changing to a homid or lupus form soon after birth to better protect them and seemingly &quot;locking&quot; them in that form for the duration of their cub. I don't think that is a bad idea either. It gives more options to STs and PCs, but I'd prefer such things to be made explicit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-03T12:14:05-07:00","id":1524982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524949#post1524949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading the 1st ed description is actually kind of... weird. I'm so used to the idea that all is negative for the garou born that the idea that 1) they are seen as noble and proud 2)that other garou born taking care of them makes their training EASIER than those of homid/lupus persuasion 3) that elders feel responsible for them and it is not stated in a negative light.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, they are trying to eat their cake and have it too. I get it. They want to encourage diversity in how an individual metis is treated. No problem with that. But it seems very inconsistent in its portrayal. Later editions would probably add more language that much depends on tribal and caern and individual Garou in terms of how they treat Garou but always with some kind of stigma.<br /> <br /> But I find 1e WtA corebook to appear to be the least professional 1e corebook. Lots of white spaces and some very cheap looking art. Even 1e Vampire looks better. And future 1e corebooks look far more professional. You can tell that when this came out, White Wolf did not have a lot of money to spend on production values or to spend more time in adding more useful details and specifics to some of their concepts. At this time, they probably needed materials out so they could earn more revenue and keep the office lights on. I think soon afterward their games would take off.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-03T12:37:03-07:00","id":1524984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524982#post1524982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, they are trying to eat their cake and have it too. I get it. They want to encourage diversity in how an individual metis is treated. No problem with that. But it seems very inconsistent in its portrayal. Later editions would probably add more language that much depends on tribal and caern and individual Garou in terms of how they treat Garou but always with some kind of stigma.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in all honesty it was refreshing to read that, since later editions went for the 'nearly always abused' route. Having the text say that for all their suffering, garou born are still proud and noble is such a positive message. Because later books never really described how the garou born act, just how they suffer.<br /> <br /> Sometimes, you just want to read stories of bullied and disabled people who still managed to keep their positivity.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-04T11:34:51-07:00","id":1525025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1524984#post1524984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, in all honesty it was refreshing to read that, since later editions went for the 'nearly always abused' route. Having the text say that for all their suffering, garou born are still proud and noble is such a positive message. Because later books never really described how the garou born act, just how they suffer.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a big difference between having a stigma versus being abused. A lot of people, including the writers of sourcebooks, confused misery with horror. Everything was presented as some kind of dystopian vision of the world instead of the setting being our world through a mirror darkly with a secret history of the supernatural. So instead of a setting of gothic horror, or whatever &quot;savage horror&quot; was meant to be, there was a lot of misery porn. I think metis being constantly abused was an aspect of that.<br /> <br /> Now I don't mind some depictions of abuse. It makes sense. But there is a big difference between &quot;there is a lot of social stigma and some abuse does happen&quot; versus &quot;all metis are always and constantly abused&quot;. Not only does it unnecessarily limit how STs and PCs can portray those characters, it can lead into your earlier point of metis not really having any reason to enjoy being Garou or proud of their people and falling into a cycle where concerns that metis are of the Wyrm become a self-fulfilling prophecy. As an individual character, that is fine. But you want to see other aspects as well. Thankfully, I think we'll see some of those in the upcoming tribebook templates. I recall a few that were much more positive and upbeat, acknowledging the stigma but presenting more optimistic characters.<br /> <br /> What is a bit surprising was that the 1e corebook would go out of its way to mention potential good aspects of the metis breed is that the 1e portrayal of the setting included a lot more negative aspects of the Garou. Every tribe had an outright Wyrmish camp, and often had another camp that while not outright Wyrmish should be controversial. The Silver Fangs were obviously failing as providing leadership to the Garou Nation and there were many conspiracies against them. There was a strong generational conflict. In other words, lots of internal enemies when Bill Bridges was the Developer. Those would be downplayed, ignored, or even outright eliminated after Ethan Skemp took over. So in a way, it's a bit surprising if this was the sole element that became worse. That might have been because it's such a prominent and unique aspect of WtA's take on werewolves so writers kept coming back to it.<br /> <br /> Now I never paid much attention to the portrayal of metis throughout the editions. For all the archaeology I do comparing edition differences, this was never something I was interested in. So I don't remember a constant portrayal of metis being always abused compared to earlier depictions, but I'll take your word for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-04T13:59:23-07:00","id":1525031,"title":"","content":"I'd say that the Crinos-born really got the shaft when W:tA added in Thrall of the Wyrm frenzies and gave the Garou-Garou born... that one. The one that makes them stop fighting and commit sexual assault and possibly necrophilia. Things were better back when any frenzy could just result in cannibalism, I think, and there was no mention of Wyrm frenzies. That just leads to forced symmetry and a lot of appended angst and brood (because Vampire said that we all had to). Kind of like Tribe Weaknesses, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-04T14:55:04-07:00","id":1525033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525031#post1525031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say that the Crinos-born really got the shaft when W:tA added in Thrall of the Wyrm frenzies and gave the Garou-Garou born... that one. The one that makes them stop fighting and commit sexual assault and possibly necrophilia. Things were better back when any frenzy could just result in cannibalism, I think, and there was no mention of Wyrm frenzies. That just leads to forced symmetry and a lot of appended angst and brood (because Vampire said that we all had to). Kind of like Tribe Weaknesses, really.</div> </div> </div> </div>(And they gave lupus one that is honestly a nothing thrall.)<br /> <br /> Often, the garou-born sections of any WtA book focus on how people either dislike or justify the abuse the garou-born face and that is as far as it goes. Rarely are there mentions of the perspectives the garou-born give and the thing the 1st core noted, that they'd have a much easier time learning garou culture BECAUSE other garou-born teach them.<br /> <br /> In fact, if I actually think back on it, most garou-born templates and example character writing assume that the character was the ONLY garou-born at their sept and members of other breeds raised them. Ironically, only Children of Gaia revised actually notes this adoption system existing at all. Given it is said garou-born are more common than lupus, this actually doesn't track. So the focus truly is on the abuse to the point where the existence of other garou-born is ignored for the sake of drama.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-04T17:04:56-07:00","id":1525045,"title":"","content":"The really wonky thing about their Thrall of the Wyrm manifestation is that when in Crinos form, the genitals are supposed to recede into the body to protect them during combat. So, how is that supposed to work? Are they supposed to assume Near Wolf form and look like a dog trying to hump someone's leg? That just takes something that is already kind of cringe and tasteless and turns it into bad farce. But pointless violent groping and grinding in Crinos is equally absurd IMO. And suddenly shifting into Homid or Glabro as part of a Frenzy makes no sense either. <br /> <br /> Honestly, I think if you needed the Thrall of the Wyrm aspect of Rage Frenzy, then just across the board eating whatever you are going berserk against, be it human, Garou, fomori, etc., would have been perfectly fine for all three Breeds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-04T18:24:14-07:00","id":1525050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525045#post1525045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The really wonky thing about their Thrall of the Wyrm manifestation is that when in Crinos form, the genitals are supposed to recede into the body to protect them during combat. So, how is that supposed to work? Are they supposed to assume Near Wolf form and look like a dog trying to hump someone's leg? That just takes something that is already kind of cringe and tasteless and turns it into bad farce. But pointless violent groping and grinding in Crinos is equally absurd IMO. And suddenly shifting into Homid or Glabro as part of a Frenzy makes no sense either.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I think if you needed the Thrall of the Wyrm aspect of Rage Frenzy, then just across the board eating whatever you are going berserk against, be it human, Garou, fomori, etc., would have been perfectly fine for all three Breeds.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure the intention was whipping it out with a botched Wits roll or the breakage of pelvises, depending on the case. This was established between 1e and 2e, so the the concept of &quot;protective pouch&quot; might not have been a fully realized explanation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-05T03:25:23-08:00","id":1525062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525050#post1525050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure the intention was whipping it out with a botched Wits roll or the breakage of pelvises, depending on the case. This was established between 1e and 2e, so the the concept of &quot;protective pouch&quot; might not have been a fully realized explanation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hate to be gross, but cub garou-born and form-locked garou-born still need to pee. So the parts are functional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-05T04:04:28-08:00","id":1525064,"title":"","content":"My experience with this pack (because nothing points out that templates are from one pack except those from RoP).<br /> <br /> As for fetishes I assumed that Whisperer's Spirit Tracer was a gift from Uktena sept for the Sept of the Green to accept him but Mother Larissa decided that cubs shouldn't pay for sept membership so she let him keep it. Curtis Harmony Flute was in form of a referee whistle to better accent his Glass Walker heritage.<br /> <br /> First me and my friend run this story for a group of new players whose only experience was Talisman board game. We didn't modify those templates but expanding their background (such as the name of Janet's band). After being cast out they didn't believe that Sept of the Green was responsible for murdering Wendigo cubs so they choose to stay close to the Winter Wolf sept. Later, because of the encounter with the tainted bear and a bane that haunted the waiter's son, they were sure that something is wrong. After a few days, when Azaera found out that they weren't killed by members of the sept, she send a lone BSD Gaillard (played by my friend, then First Officer and one of the best STs that I met; because of that none of the players expected treachery) who told the PCs that something is indeed wrong and that he and his buddies wants to correct it. None of the characters has Sense Wyrm gift so they believe him (after all the dialogue was run so well that Linda couldn't use Truth of Gaia gift) and ended in the mine. Of course the showed some concerns about it but as the BSD said &quot;who could expect defenders of Gaia in a place like that&quot;. Ultimately they all ended among Dancers.<br /> <br /> The second time I run this characters it was for a group of experienced players, who played CP2020 and Vampire mostly. They also modified the characters bio (some of them to the extremes; one of the players assumed that, as Curtis has an earring in his right ear, he surely is homosexual which later led to a situation when, during the moot, Curtis was accused of mating with a female garou he shouted in front of an entire sept and a large pack of Fenris visitors &quot;but I'm gay&quot;; this was one of the best roleplayed scene in my life). After being cast out they assumed that it will be a Bone Gnawer style Rite of Passage (you know, far away from home, without any resources, and you have to return). With Billy's help they survived the snowstorm and returned to NY. Later a Silent Strider send for them returned with the news of Accolon's death and Azarea's treasure. After that they had a new Rite of Passage and went on. But the pack basically splited: Snarl at Fleas went to the Sentinel Sept in the wild, Janet founded a new band with other garou and a kinfolk, Linda returned to college, Whisperer made his home in Central Park and Curtis tried to live as far from garou affairs as he could. It was also because the players were older than the first time, they had normal life, work and families. Of course sometimes, when Gaia called, they reformed the pack, but basically from then on it was mostly Janet who run the show.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-07T00:31:11-08:00","id":1525157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525062#post1525062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hate to be gross, but cub garou-born and form-locked garou-born still need to pee. So the parts are functional.</div> </div> </div> </div>A question asked by one female PCs to another after seeing crinos for the first time (with pure fascination in her eyes):<br /> &quot;Is he getting bigger EVERYWHERE?&quot;<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-07T05:48:41-08:00","id":1525160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525157#post1525157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A question asked by one female PCs to another after seeing crinos for the first time (with pure fascination in her eyes):<br /> &quot;Is he getting bigger EVERYWHERE?&quot;<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that was the fastest way to teach cubs the First Law XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-07T16:40:39-08:00","id":1525182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525160#post1525160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, that was the fastest way to teach cubs the First Law XD</div> </div> </div> </div>She was a kinfolk, but I've got your point <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-07T19:12:23-08:00","id":1525187,"title":"","content":"And so, back to 1994, right about the same time the 2nd ed core book was being released. <b>Bone Gnawers</b> was written by Sam Chupp, and once again Joshua Timbrook is doing the art for the templates. <br /> <br /> <b>Ragabash Rat Fink </b>(Homid Ragabash)<br /> <br /> ::Sigh:: So, this begins what will be a recurring thing, both in this book and later Tribebooks. Namely, just calling a template's concept by it's Auspice and/or Camp. Or in this case, both of those and nothing else. For some reason, it's the Ragabash who keep getting this in the future Tribebooks. <br /> Just personally, I find this rather annoying, mainly from a creative standpoint. Besides being a bit lazy, it doesn't really say much about the character in question. It's just what you picked from column A and column B on the takeout menu. Nothing at all about how those particular character traits manifest themselves nor how the character might view themselves. A good concept name is, along with the image, the first thing that draws you to a template. This should have been called &quot;The Invisible Man&quot; or &quot;Trash Collector&quot;. <br /> <br /> Anyway ....<br /> <br /> So this guy has always been a very nosy individual. And even a little bit of a creep, not above blackmail. It's not specified, but he's apparently from a small town or the suburbs. After his First Change, he was taken to the city. It doesn't say anything about how or why he's a Bone Gnawer. Just that he was put to work, somewhat unwillingly, as a janitor for a Pentex company. (This was back when the entire Garou Nation apparently knew about Pentex.) And now they're trying to kill his family. That or brainwash them. <br /> I'm a bit confused about how that's supposed to work. Surely he didn't sign up using his real name and SSN. His Equipment even lists multiple fake IDs. So how would they know who his family even is? And if they're being attacked right now, as this write up seems to indicate, why wouldn't he try to drop everything and return home?<br /> <br /> Once you get past that, the write up is a fairly solid concept. He works as a janitor, and in the process collects assorted keys, phone numbers, floppy discs, print outs, and other detritus. He's effectively invisible, both in the sense of &quot;the help&quot; being totally ignored by those in power, and literally with the Blur of the Milky Eye gift. <br /> <br /> Equipment is a disposable camera and a well used pocket tape recorder (I really do miss the 90s sometimes), as well as the previously mentioned fake IDs. <br /> <br /> The image is of a somewhat scrawny and disheveled young man with glasses wearing janitor coveralls, with a broom/mop and trash can. It looks fine and represents what is described. <br /> <br /> For Attributes, Physicals are tertiary. And are 1/4/1. <br /> <br /> Damn it. <br /> <br /> Socials are secondary, with 3/4/1.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Mental is primary, with 5/3/2.<br /> <br /> This just feels all kinds of broken. I mean, I get the idea of a character being physically unimpressive, but having a pair of ones feels excessive. (Also, I've done custodial work in my lifetime; it requires a certain degree of stamina.) 1/3/2 would seem more reasonable. <br /> With Socials, there's nothing about him that feels like it would indicate above average Charisma. And if you're wanting to blend into the background, being completely average and unremarkable seems better than being notably unattractive (&quot;tend to attract the hostility of others&quot; as the core book puts it). 2/4/2 would probably work fine here. <br /> With Mental, if you want to keep that 5 in Perception, I think having Intelligence 2 and Wits 3 would be more suitable. <br /> <br /> For Abilities, Talents are primary with one extra dot from freebies. 4 in Subterfuge, 3 each in Alertness and Streetwise, 2 in Dodge, and 1 each in Empathy and Primal Urge.<br /> Skills are tertiary with four extra dots from freebies. 4 in Stealth, 2 each in Firearms and Repair, and 1 in Drive. <br /> Knowledge is secondary with two extra dots from freebies. 4 in Investigation, 3 in Computer, and 1 each in Linguistics, Medicine, Politics, and Science. <br /> <br /> Overall, these seem fine. It's a decent spread of abilities that fit what he does, as well as giving him some combat effectiveness. <br /> <br /> Backgrounds are 3 each in Allies and Contacts. Contacts seems especially fitting here. I confess that I miss characters having Pack Totem as a background from Rite of Passage. Also, I sort of expected him to have a Mentor of some sort, just from the fact that he was apparently forced into his current role, and you'd think he'd have some sort of handler or something. <br /> <br /> Rage, Gnosis, and Willpower are all at their default values (1, 1, and 4, respectively). <br /> <br /> Overall, this is a fairly solid concept. I wish it had actually be given a name instead of just stringing together two traits, yes. And the Attributes feel really broken, yes. And the family thing doesn't make a lot of sense, yes. But I think all of those can be easily overlooked, fixed, or ignored. <br /> I also wish I knew more about how this guy ended up in the Tribe he did, as well as how he ended up in the Rat Fink camp. (I've never been really wild about that name; I think &quot;Muck Rakers&quot; or some variation on that might've been better.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-07T22:12:16-08:00","id":1525191,"title":"","content":"I think the Rat Fink is a fairly solid template, but I understand your dislike of the name being &quot;Auspice Camp&quot;. Your suggestion of &quot;The Invisible Man&quot; would be better. Tribebooks were expected to fill out a lot of details first mentioned in the original Players Guide so it makes sense to use them to explore the various camps. But it could lead to a lot of unoriginal templates. As you mentioned before, showing 10 templates instead of 5 could have showcased more originality. I don't think the &quot;camps&quot; collectively comprised the majority of each tribe so I would have liked templates that made no mention of them as well.<br /> <br /> Character sheet wise, I think it is fairly solid, but agree with all of your improvements.<br /> <br /> Of all the Bone Gnawer templates, this is my favorite. One thing I really like about it is that it is not necessary for this character to change form unless absolutely needed in combat. As an ST, I see players make all sorts of unnecessary changes to form simply because they can. They change form not only when it is not necessary to do so, but when it could endanger the Veil. I find it extremely annoying. But as written, this character likely rarely changes unless it makes sense to do so. I understand the appeal of playing a werewolf is to change form. I would just like it to make sense when players decide to do so. This is a solid concept given the parameters of the setting and this character idea.<br /> <br /> I think this would be a great character concept for an urban based chronicle. <br /> <br /> My one big complaint of the tribebook is that it seems to discount rural Bone Gnawers despite introducing the Hill Folk camp. Too often the tribe seems to be &quot;unemployed bums in the city&quot; as opposed to &quot;runts of the Garou Nation&quot; which I think is more appropriate. Historically the tribe's kinfolk is probably more &quot;oppressed peasants&quot; than &quot;urban homeless&quot;, but that is not what the tribebook evokes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-07T22:56:50-08:00","id":1525192,"title":"","content":"One of my big petpeeves with the Gnawers is the whole &quot;must be homeless&quot; creed. While Nosferatu made sense (Masquerade break AND poor hours), your typical Fianna and Get of Fenris ahroun is as much a moocher as a Gnawer one.<br /> <br /> Luckily W20 eased things a bit, which means the focus can be on the &quot;chooses to live in the dredges of humanity because no one else will.&quot; They are the 'runts' of the Nation, but they are still garou and they are still allowed to have the full stat spreads that others are.<br /> <br /> <br /> Other than that, I'm glad nWoD got rid of Appearance as a stat for the reasons above.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-08T02:41:36-08:00","id":1525199,"title":"","content":"The attribute-spread on that char-sheet is certainly excessive...<br /> <br /> Actually, I think the Nosferatu could be the reason they gave the character App 1. In this book's write-up of the Rat-Finks Camp it focuses on their connection to the Nosferatu. So maybe whoever came up with the template wanted this character to be this kind of pseudo-Nosferatu.<br /> <br /> But the concept is pretty good and the Rat Fink Camp being all about information-gathering also fits the Tribe. What I especially like is that the concept is easy to pick up and understand the vibe this is going for. It's easy to build additional detail around it to make it fit whatever the Chronicle's setting is.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-08T17:31:04-08:00","id":1525227,"title":"","content":"Yeah, this was back when &quot;You like X and I like X so we should totally hang out together!&quot; was very much a thing. <br /> <br /> As a creative aside, anyone have any ideas as to what Rat Fink Galliards and Ahrouns might be like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-08T17:35:15-08:00","id":1525228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525227#post1525227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, this was back when &quot;You like X and I like X so we should totally hang out together!&quot; was very much a thing.<br /> <br /> As a creative aside, anyone have any ideas as to what Rat Fink Galliards and Ahrouns might be like?</div> </div> </div> </div>A bookkeeper and legbreaker, respectively?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-08T18:34:37-08:00","id":1525229,"title":"","content":"<b>Rust Shaman </b>(Homid Theurge)<br /> <br /> This one is fairly interesting. Someone who was apparently touched by the spirits of the city almost from birth and instinctively aware of the animist nature of the World of Darkness. Their First Change started while in a subway station and they fled deeper into the city's underground, eventually to the sewers. There they apparently met Rat herself (or at least an avatar) and was shown secret keys to the city, and now serves as her prophet. Now they wander the city, telling others what the streets of destiny hold for them. <br /> <br /> I use they because, even thought the artwork is of a male, there's not really anything in the write up to indicate gender and this could just as easily work as a female (or any sort of non-binary, as that does have traditional associations with shamanism in some cultures).<br /> <br /> The character is described as seeming somewhat out of it to others, but this is because they are constantly aware of the spiritual aspect of the world. They also engage, in a seemingly OCD manner, in constant drumming and other rituals directed toward the various city spirits of taxi cabs, fire hydrants, pay phones (again, the 90s), and the like. They also regularly talk to said spirits, something that probably looks like schizophrenia to humans but is probably fairly normal to most Garou by the time they hit Rank 2. <br /> <br /> Equipment is a massive key ring full of random keys that may or may not be important, and a handful of random paper detritus. I feel like maybe they should have a staff of some sort. Having it be a Fetish would be optional, but I just think it would be ascetically cool for a modern urban prophet. <br /> <br /> The image is of an almost stereotypical early 90s homeless man. He appears fairly older than normal for a starting PC, being partially bald and having a long beard that feels like it's probably grey. He has an interesting necklace with some assorted junk hanging from it. As with a noticeable amount of Timbrook's artwork, it's a little different to guess his race, and arguments could be made for multiple directions. Overall, it's a pretty decent image. Though I can't help but wonder what this might've looked like if presented as a 20-something female. <br /> <br /> He's not part of any Camp. That actually makes him the only one of these five who isn't associated with one. Again, we come back to the whole &quot;I wish there'd been 10 instead of 5&quot; thing. <br /> <br /> For Attributes, Physicals are secondary, with 1/3/4. Sam Chupp seems to have some sort of weird fixation on giving Bone Gnawers attribute ratings of 1. (And you haven't seen anything yet; just wait for the Ahroun.) Socials are tertiary with 3/2/1. Against, I don't know what the deal is with Bone Gnawers having 1s in Appearance. I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27535_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27535\" data-vbnamecard=\"27535\">Knightingale</a> may be correct and it's some kind of Nosferatu-lite thing. Mental is primary with 4/2/4.<br /> The Mental spread is fine. I think the other two would be better being flipped. Have Physicals as all 2s, and Socials as either 3/3/2 or 4/2/2. This keeps his Charisma high for his prophet role and but doesn't conflate his disheveled clothing and possible lack of regular hygiene for actual physical ugliness. <br /> <br /> For Abilities, Talents are primary, with 3 each in Alertness and Primal Urge, 2 each in Dodge, Empathy, and Streetwise, and 1 in Expression. <br /> Skills are tertiary, with 3 in Stealth and 2 in Survival. <br /> Knowledge is secondary with one extra dot from freebies, for a 4 in Rituals, and 3 each in Enigmas and Occult. <br /> For the most part, this is fine. However, I question the lack of Performance given how the write up specifically mentions his drumming. I'd also sort of expect his Streetwise to be a little higher. <br /> <br /> Backgrounds are 4 in Rites and 1 in Allies. It's not specified who the Ally is. It could be some sort of spirit, maybe. <br /> I sort of feel like he could benefit from some Contacts or else more dots in Allies. I think this would fit in with the mention of his equipment including a bunch of business cards, notes, and other stuff, where they could represent people he's actually assisted through his role as a prophet and now help him on occasion with information or other favors. <br /> He has one unspent freebie point, and I wonder if it was supposed to be spent on Fetish. The book has a new level one Fetish, The Lost Keyring, that matches the description of the keyring in his equipment, and would seem appropriate for this character. <br /> <br /> With Gifts, I really think that Persuasion would be more useful for this character than Smell of Man. <br /> <br /> His Rage is the default 2. Gnosis is a whopping 7. This is where the vast bulk of his freebies went. Willpower is the default 4. <br /> I'm sort of torn here. On the one hand, having such a massive level of spiritual attunement certainly fits the character. But on the other, this seems perhaps a little excessive. I really do feel that at least some of those points could've been better spent on addition Ability or Background dots. <br /> <br /> Overall, this is a really interesting character. I enjoy how it plays into the animistic nature of the setting, as well as how certain behaviors which make total sense in one context (urban shamanism) seem nonsensical or off-putting in another (modern rational materialism). I like the idea of a Homid who has been aware of the spiritual aspect of the world for their entire life long before the Change. <br /> <br /> I will however point out the obvious: This is also essentially a Dreamspeaker Mage reskinned as a werewolf. Not that this is necessarily bad. I think it's also an interesting potential Mage character. (I'm also almost 100% certain that it, as well as the Trashheap totem in this book, are primarily responsible for the inspiration of the narrator of the revised Dreamspeakers book.) <br /> <br /> So, I like this one. It's a slightly offbeat idea that actually makes a lot of sense in context of the game and the Tribe, and certainly not something I would have thought of on my own back in 1994. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-08T18:37:15-08:00","id":1525230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525228#post1525228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A bookkeeper and legbreaker, respectively?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Possible. <br /> <br /> I think you could do something interesting with an Ahroun who works primarily as an &quot;extractor&quot; whose skillset is aimed at pulling the Camp's various moles - be they Garou or especially Kinfolk - out of danger when their cover is blown.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-08T19:52:50-08:00","id":1525231,"title":"","content":"I think the Rust Shaman is another solid concept with a so-so character sheet, possibly showing the limitations of the standard Storyteller System character creation mechanics. A lot of the high stats seem to exist simply because the writer needed to dump points into something that makes sense. The high ranks in Enigmas, Occult, and Rituals all make sense to a degree, but seem excessive. I would have preferred the Knowledges branch to receive the least dots and make Skills the secondary and add one point or more in Animal Ken, Performance, and Repair. It's very strange to see a character without any offensive combat skills - no Brawl, no Melee, no Firearms. At least one point in Brawl and one point in Melee (to hit someone with a tool, drumstick, club, bottle or something) would make it better. It would also be interesting to know what Rites this character knows, but I guess that is to be left to the player.<br /> <br /> We also seem to have a pattern of making Appearance the dump stat for Bone Gnawers. I understand the tribe isn't glamorous, but really?<br /> <br /> This scene from Repo Man reminds me of the rust shaman.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vRJ5cCP0ZPE\" data-code=\"vRJ5cCP0ZPE\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/vRJ5cCP0ZPE/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> We're now at the high point of the templates of this sourcebook as the following ones all have major issues in my opinion, but I'll refrain until you get to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T00:01:06-08:00","id":1525237,"title":"","content":"Overall I got an idea why Bone Gnawers templates have Appearance 1. During my games this stat not only describe how your character looks like but also the general &quot;aura&quot; which surrounds it. So:<br /> <br /> As for Ragabash: he is a janitor. He is usually surrounded by the smell of cleaning chemicals and rotten food (you know, &quot;fruit friday&quot; and so on). If he quits his post as a janitor, cleans up and shaves himself he could easily improve his Appearance. Also, being skinny (hence Strenght and Stamina 1), he is totally unimpressive. Just think of that: could you call Mike Myers or Rick Moranis totally unattractive? And now think about Brian Thompson. He has a very brutal, almost primitive, face. It is his statuesque body that makes him attractive. I knew a few guys that were totally average in their &quot;male form&quot;. But if they put some make-up and fake boobs (for Halloween or during the LARPs they used to play a women) and they were picked up by guys on the street.<br /> <br /> The same is for Urban Shaman: he's homeless. They are usually disheveled and smell bad. If he shaves his beard and cleans himself he also could become more attractive. As for his fetish maybe he found (or got it during his meeting with Totem) The Lost Keyring. He just didn't attuned it.<br /> <br /> As for this concept as a female look at the Urban Primitive concept from Glass Walkers tribebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T04:41:09-08:00","id":1525243,"title":"","content":"The Rust Shaman is something I wish more Bone Gnawer templates would have gone with; The animism of the city. Because animism isn't just nature and trees, it is everything around you and the things others throw away. The older the object, the more spiritual resonance it has. And the Rust Shaman perfectly shows this.<br /> <br /> As for the Dreamspeaker similarity? Honestly, it is just that both have the same source of 'power' as it were.<br /> <br /> I think the App 1 issue comes from these being the first-ever Gnawers statted. So the thinking of &quot;Oh, these guys are the Nossie of the garou&quot; would stick for a bit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525237#post1525237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Overall I got an idea why Bone Gnawers templates have Appearance 1. During my games this stat not only describe how your character looks like but also the general &quot;aura&quot; which surrounds it. So:</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember that that is your houserule and not something the devs had in mind when they made this template. As much as your way explains things away, it isn't the source of the issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T08:20:08-08:00","id":1525249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525243#post1525243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember that that is your houserule and not something the devs had in mind when they made this template. As much as your way explains things away, it isn't the source of the issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it isn't<br /> <br /> &quot;Appearance<br /> <br /> The trait describes your general appereance in terms of your attractiveness and force of presence. You do not need necessarily beauty to have a high Appearance you only need looks that somehow attracts others to you. Appereance is not just your static beauty, it's the appeal of the way you move and talk, your animation expressiveness. It's the measure of how interesting and attractive you seem to others&quot;<br /> <br /> W:tA 1st edition corebook.<br /> <br /> So it's not only your face but the impression you make BEFORE you open your mouth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 11-09-2023, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T09:18:48-08:00","id":1525252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525249#post1525249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, it isn't<br /> <br /> &quot;Appearance<br /> <br /> The trait describes your general appereance in terms of your attractiveness and force of presence. You do not need necessarily beauty to have a high Appearance you only need looks that somehow attracts others to you. Appereance is not just your static beauty, it's the appeal of the way you move and talk, your animation expressiveness. It's the measure of how interesting and attractive you seem to others&quot;<br /> <br /> W:tA 1st edition corebook.<br /> <br /> So it's not only your face but the impression you make BEFORE you open your mouth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but look at the dots;<br /> <br /> <i>1 dot. You tend to attract the hostility of others.<br /> <br /> 2 dots. You are easily ignored for you fit well in a crowd.</i><br /> <br /> So, basically app 1 is a detriment to the Ratfink, not a benefit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T09:30:49-08:00","id":1525254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525252#post1525252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah but look at the dots;<br /> <br /> <i>1 dot. You tend to attract the hostility of others.<br /> <br /> 2 dots. You are easily ignored for you fit well in a crowd.</i><br /> <br /> So, basically app 1 is a detriment to the Ratfink, not a benefit.</div> </div> </div> </div>That I can agree. But still I think that aggresion comes in many forms. And Ragabashes often take beating (again, in many forms) to diffuse the situation. So App 1 here can be useful: first of all, I think it's highly unlikely that hostility of Pentex employees would take a physical version. I think that it would be rather verbal abuse. And second, it can be an advantage: A hostile one is prone to anger and can make a mistake (such as leaving black operation papers in the caffeteria).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T09:35:35-08:00","id":1525256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525254#post1525254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That I can agree. But still I think that aggresion comes in many forms. And Ragabashes often take beating (again, in many forms) to diffuse the situation. So App 1 here can be useful: first of all, I think it's highly unlikely that hostility of Pentex employees would take a physical version. I think that it would be rather verbal abuse. And second, it can be an advantage: A hostile one is prone to anger and can make a mistake (such as leaving black operation papers in the caffeteria).</div> </div> </div> </div>But the whole point of Ratfink's plan is to be invisible. Even if you hate someone, you remember them and when someone is suspected you'd recall them being particularly unpleasant. Someone who relies on being unseen is not served by that, because they rely on going under the radar. Which is App 2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T10:29:54-08:00","id":1525259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525256#post1525256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But the whole point of Ratfink's plan is to be invisible. Even if you hate someone, you remember them and when someone is suspected you'd recall them being particularly unpleasant. Someone who relies on being unseen is not served by that, because they rely on going under the radar. Which is App 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok. On the other hand, based on my own experience, I rarely remember people who pissed me off, regardless the way they did it. And I've got a good memory for faces. I would recognize them when I see them, but not the names etc. So still I'd go &quot;by the book&quot;. App 1 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T10:38:34-08:00","id":1525262,"title":"","content":"The reason I mentioned it is not just because these two templates have Appearance 1. Of the remaining three, two more have Appearance 1 and the other is Appearance 2. The Rust Shaman definitely has a reason why the character is Appearance 1. The others don't. There's no real reason for such low traits across the board except &quot;Um, they're Bone Gnawers so who cares.&quot;<br /> <br /> This is not a major issue and can be easily fixed, but I find it annoying. In my experience players rarely want their characters to have App 1 unless that is part of their specific character concept. They at least default to App 2 and may increase from there. Because Attributes are so expensive to increase with XP, I find most players choosing to increase Abilities instead. So getting the Attributes &quot;right&quot; for their character at creation is generally important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T15:01:20-08:00","id":1525272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525259#post1525259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok. On the other hand, based on my own experience, I rarely remember people who pissed me off, regardless the way they did it. And I've got a good memory for faces. I would recognize them when I see them, but not the names etc. So still I'd go &quot;by the book&quot;. App 1 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not about who pisses you off, it is that the character stands out in some way. To use a very clumsy example, an app 1 kid is the one that bullies zero in on. App 2 kid just disappears in the mass,","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T15:42:10-08:00","id":1525276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525272#post1525272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not about who pisses you off, it is that the character stands out in some way. To use a very clumsy example, an app 1 kid is the one that bullies zero in on. App 2 kid just disappears in the mass,</div> </div> </div> </div>If only they were playing Adventure! or Exalted 3rd edition...<br /> <br /> (But then the Nossie players might quibble over having to put Appearance dots into being as horrifying as the Nosferatu are supposed to be...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T19:31:13-08:00","id":1525283,"title":"","content":"<b>Vigilante Wolf </b>(Lupus Philodox)<br /> <br /> Animal abuse is one of my button issues, so that will probably color my reaction to this one. <br /> <br /> This is also another of those write ups that appears to be longer than average.<br /> <br /> This one isn't really gender specified either. They were born to what I presume was feral stray with a high percentage of wolf blood. The runt of the litter, they were the only one spared when their mother and pack mates were all horribly abused and murdered by some group of humans. &quot;Street punks&quot; who did it just for amusement. Naturally, this left a lot of psychic scars and emotional baggage. <br /> They managed to survive, partially thanks to help from more empathic and humane humans, all of whom seemed to carry a distinctive scent that marked them. Obviously, this is meant to imply Bone Gnawers and/or their Kinfolk. Eventually they grew up powerful enough to dominate and command most of the other stray dogs in the area. <br /> Then the First Change happened and they learned that humans tend to abuse other humans as well before finally being able to fight back against his abusers. Now they're a roaming urban vigilante who is loosely associated with The Hood camp. <br /> <br /> Equipment is a trench coat and fedora, a light pistol, hand cuffs, and matches. The coat is mentioned in the write up as being dedicated so they don't lose it when shifting. I confess that this leaves me with the image of a person walking around the city streets naked under a trench coat, which honestly sounds more like a flasher than a vigilante. But with the fedora, I'm guessing at least some of the inspiration behind this character came from the 1990 film <i>Darkman</i>. Not that that's a bad thing.<br /> <br /> The image is of a somewhat ragged and scruffy looking Crinos with blood on their hands. There's nothing really outstanding about it one way or another. It fits the character and does have a nice savage quality to it, I think. <br /> <br /> For Attributes, Physicals are primary, with a 3/4/3 spread. Socials are tertiary with 3/2/1. Mental is secondary, with 4/2/2.<br /> I'm a little torn on the Socials. One the one hand, I can see the character as perhaps having various scars and the like from their very rough upbringing (and also the Darkman influence), and a certain degree of Manipulation is needed for good Intimidation rolls. On the other hand, I could just as easily see them as looking fairly normal and having a low Manipulation to represent how straightforward and blunt they are. I guess this is one of those six vs half a dozen things. <br /> <br /> For Abilities, Talents are primary with two extra dots from freebies. 3 each in Alertness and Dodge, 2 each in Brawl, Intimidation, Primal Urge, and Streetwise, and 1 in Athletics. <br /> Skills are secondary with two extra dots from freebies (again). 3 each in Stealth and Survival, 2 each in Animal Ken and Firearms, and 1 in Leadership.<br /> Knowledge is tertiary with two extra dots from freebies (yet again). 3 in Investigation, 2 in Enigmas, and 1 each in Law and Linguistics. <br /> By and large, I think these are fine. I don't really think they need the Firearms skill. Law is also perhaps a little iffy. I think I'd probably take those two Firearms dots and put one into Leadership and the other into either Brawl or Streetwise. The one from Law I'd be tempted to use for Backgrounds instead.<br /> <br /> Said Backgrounds are 3 in Allies and 2 in Contacts. From the write up, I think the Contacts are mainly the Barking Chain. At least some of the Allies might be the stray street dogs they still command the loyalty of. This is part of why I think a slight boost to Leadership might be useful. This also reminds me that I wish the WoD games had at some point talked about the idea of having animal allies, be they wolf packs, incredibly well trained horses, or whatever. If I'd decided to spend those freebies on Backgrounds instead of Abilities, I might've gone with more levels in Contacts, or possibly Pack Totem. A one dot Mentor who helps the character better understand human society might also be useful. <br /> <br /> Rage and Gnosis are the default levels of 3 and 5, respectively. Willpower has been raised to 7 with freebies.<br /> <br /> I mostly like this character. It's not perfect, but I can't exactly put my finger on what it's flaw is. It does have a fairly strong backstory and motivation. I think there's a case this might work better as an Ahroun, but at the same time I think the way the write up shows how they've experienced both abuse and kindness at the hands of humans works with the Half-Moon ideas about balance and justice. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T21:06:13-08:00","id":1525287,"title":"","content":"That wouldn't be the only Philodox non-homid to end up as a vigilante with a trench coat and a fedora, incidentally (though more on that when we get down to the letter S).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T21:38:40-08:00","id":1525290,"title":"","content":"I like this template in a lot of ways with one big exception. It is very hard to see this character as an actual lupus - meaning a wolf. Its description of its life as an animal points more towards being a dog. There is no problem with Bone Gnawers having lupus members. But why would a wolf pack be living in a city? Does it make sense that some kinds would actually mess with a wolf pack? Or that the wolf mother could not have seriously injured or scared this group of kids/teens who messed with her cubs? &quot;Street punks&quot; won't normally screw around with an actual wolf pack or den. None of this seems like it is talking about wild wolves (who somehow found themselves in a city for some reason). It naturally reads like they are talking about dogs.<br /> <br /> I remember there being a LOT of confusion about the nature of the Bone Gnawers in the nineties. A LOT of players had the impression that Bone Gnawers were basically dogs, not wolves. It doesn't help that page 29 of the tribebook actually shows a picture of a dog. (Even in the 1e corebook there are images of Bone Gnawers that seem much more like dogs than wolves, though this might simply be because of the lower quality of art in that sourcebook.) Even terminology like &quot;the Barking Chain&quot;, which this template references, creates the impression of dogs as opposed to wolves. Wolves don't really bark. Everyone says that wolves howl, but dogs bark. I understand the term may be poetic, but combined with other things, it creates a lot of confusion.<br /> <br /> I don't see the lupus of the Bone Gnawer being urban based. They are probably one of the tribes that are most wolf-starved. If you are going to assign a camp to lupus, the Hillfolk are more natural. The Bone Gnawer as described are VERY homid based, so there actually is not a lot for the lupus breed to go by. The tribebook just ignores the issue rather than engage it. It's major weakness that is not sufficiently addressed even in the Revised version.<br /> <br /> Outside of this issue, the template suffers from not explaining exactly how a lupus gets Allies and Contacts. I think it is perfectly fine for a lupus to have human Allies and Contacts, but the template description must address how the lupus crossed this divide. You may only need two sentences or so, but it should be explained. It doesn't. It just assumes you have them.<br /> <br /> Lastly, and I may be unfair about this, it irritates me to read this:<br /> <br /> &quot;You do not threaten the Veil. You wear a black trenchcoat that is Dedicated to you.&quot;<br /> <br /> Great, that must be all you need. Black trenchcoats solves everything.<br /> <br /> For the tribe and auspice, this is a solid template. But I have major problems for it as a lupus breed character.<br /> <br /> Again, this template has an Appearance of 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-09T22:52:55-08:00","id":1525291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525290#post1525290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this template in a lot of ways with one big exception. It is very hard to see this character as an actual lupus - meaning a wolf. Its description of its life as an animal points more towards being a dog. There is no problem with Bone Gnawers having lupus members. But why would a wolf pack be living in a city? Does it make sense that some kinds would actually mess with a wolf pack? Or that the wolf mother could not have seriously injured or scared this group of kids/teens who messed with her cubs? &quot;Street punks&quot; won't normally screw around with an actual wolf pack or den. None of this seems like it is talking about wild wolves (who somehow found themselves in a city for some reason). It naturally reads like they are talking about dogs.</div> </div> </div> </div>This might be my more fantastical take on WoD, but I actually like this. Because in our world, city/town scavenging wolves are mostly Arabian and Egyptian. Not North American as this fellow is.<br /> <br /> But WoD is not our world in the sense that there are semi-sentient wolf kin running about nevermind fully sentient lupus garou. There are two (or four if we count Furies and Coggies) tribes of werewolves regularly found in the city. So I can totally see high content wolfdog kin being a thing in the cities. You got smarter than normal wolves, who already are smart and you get wolves trying to find easier time where the Trash is.<br /> <br /> Basically, it shows the setting is not just in character bios, it actually affects how the world IS.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-10T03:20:06-08:00","id":1525304,"title":"","content":"When the text talked about how the character was engaging with his newfound friends' hospitality, I assumed the character had already gone through their First Change with the way it talked about &quot;dominating the streets&quot;. Was a bit surprised that the First Change only happened after that. And then you get this rushed transition of the character finding out that humans are bad which then goes right over to &quot;Concept&quot; where now it's described how the character cares about carrying out justice... Well, that was quick! Seemed like just a moment ago, the character was merely an angry &quot;dog&quot; in the city.<br /> <br /> Also, if he has a &quot;Dedicated black coat&quot;, he should start out with the Rite. Or these dots Allies and Contacts could've been reduced as well to give him dots in Mentor to reflect who taught him to be this adapt in his Homid-form and within the city.<br /> <br /> I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> that here it might have been better to switch the Breeds between the upcoming Galliard and this one. It just seems like the whole Lupus-bit is there in the backstory but the moment the writer got to Concept and Roleplaying-Hints, the wolf-born element got dropped in favor of this Hood-Camp-based vigilante that cares about justice. <br /> <br /> Appearance 1 again as well... Looking through the Tribebook, the only way I could imagine it linking up with the idea of this Tribe is that besides being inspired by Nosferatu, the low Appearance could be representative of the Bone Gnawers' general low social status. Somehow the Bone Gnawers' low status is so inherent to them, like they're &quot;lowborn&quot; in a very literal sense and so this is reflected in their Appearance. Not really a fan of this idea personally but that's the only way I could make sense of it being this &quot;must-do&quot; that was applied repeatedly in the templates here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-10T11:35:22-08:00","id":1525318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525291#post1525291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But WoD is not our world in the sense that there are semi-sentient wolf kin running about nevermind fully sentient lupus garou. There are two (or four if we count Furies and Coggies) tribes of werewolves regularly found in the city. So I can totally see high content wolfdog kin being a thing in the cities. You got smarter than normal wolves, who already are smart and you get wolves trying to find easier time where the Trash is.</div> </div> </div> </div>If this is actually something that is an element of the game setting, it is such a departure from the real world that it really needs to be documented and explained explicitly somewhere (preferably a major book that won't be overlooked - like in the corebook or players guide, not wait many years for something like Book of the City (which doesn't describe anything like that). What is the extent of them? Are they found in all major cities? Only cities that have urban caerns or a large population of Urrah? Is it something unique to the Bone Gnawers, or do the Glass Walkers (and perhaps even other tribes) have them as well? Is this only a kinfolk animal thing, or are there other such scavenging wolf packs. Is this well known among humans, or is it somehow kept secret and unknown except for urban legends and the like? <br /> <br /> Should we consider them some kind of fictional subspecies of canis lupus that are perhaps smaller, more slender, and have more doglike or coyote-like features?<br /> <br /> What exactly do these carnivores eat in the city? Wolves need to eat a lot of meat - about 5-15 lbs per day - and there are no large hoofed animals that make up 90% of the wilderness wolf diet. Cities don't even have a lot of small mammals like rabbits, beavers, raccoons, or large fish like salmon. Yeah, some of those animals are around in the city, but not enough to support an ongoing population of wolves. Eating rodents and birds won't be enough. So are they eating people's pets like urban coyotes often do? Really going after food waste in garbage cans (if you think raccoons are bad)? Scavenging off (or perhaps hunting/killing) people living in the street? US cities typically don't have a large greenbelt or wilderness nearby that such wolves could live off of and then go back and forth to the city. It's just a lot of suburbs. A good ST can figure out answers for these in a way to make sense (maybe the Bone Gnawers move them back and forth, monitor them so they know when to provide aid, have their members regularly provide food (either real or through the Cooking Gift or by a Fetish), have kinfolk run restaurants or collect in common building so they can dump a lot of food waste, etc., but some thought needs to go into it to help us suspend our disbelief.<br /> <br /> Not only would this be a prominent setting element for the Werewolf game, it has other impacts as well. Some kind of wild scavenging wolf packs in cities would interest a LOT of vampires who have Animalism. How does that impact the Garou in return?<br /> <br /> I am not necessarily against this idea. As you explained, there is various lore in the game that can support the concept. And the idea of wolflike urban predators has a good presentation in the book and movie Wolfen which was Whitley Strieber's more &quot;scientific&quot; take on the werewolf myth. So it's firmly in theme. I think it can add to the game. If an ST wants to make it a thing in her chronicle and does a good job of presenting this, I am not against it. I could easily enjoy provided it is kept limited and doesn't force other changes like a domino.<br /> <br /> But the actual setting materials don't present us with this. We're not given enough as STs and PCs to assume it exists. Instead, we have to create head canon in order to justify things like this. I don't think the setting actually intends it. It isn't necessarily against it either, but I don't think the creators actually considered this. So when we have things like this, it needs more explanation. Again, no reason not to make sufficient changes to allow it, but to pull it off, an ST will need to put some thought into it. If people want to talk about, it could be its own thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-10T12:10:13-08:00","id":1525321,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3046_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3046\" data-vbnamecard=\"3046\">Black Fox</a> Yeah, obviously it is a MASSIVE change from irl world and needs more meat on its bones. I personally enjoy it because it showcases the changing breeds don't live in a vacuum as it were.<br /> <br /> To get back to the canon, maybe some writers went a BIT far with &quot;WoD is darker than our world&quot;, because this is not the last time trash scavenging wolves appear. Red Talon revised has one template with the character being a urban trash eating wolf. I get the feeling there was not really much thought put into this outsider &quot;Well the setting is dark so why not actually dangerous street wolves?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-11T03:01:01-08:00","id":1525341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525290#post1525290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this template in a lot of ways with one big exception. It is very hard to see this character as an actual lupus - meaning a wolf. Its description of its life as an animal points more towards being a dog. There is no problem with Bone Gnawers having lupus members. But why would a wolf pack be living in a city? Does it make sense that some kinds would actually mess with a wolf pack? Or that the wolf mother could not have seriously injured or scared this group of kids/teens who messed with her cubs? &quot;Street punks&quot; won't normally screw around with an actual wolf pack or den. None of this seems like it is talking about wild wolves (who somehow found themselves in a city for some reason). It naturally reads like they are talking about dogs.<br /> <br /> I remember there being a LOT of confusion about the nature of the Bone Gnawers in the nineties. A LOT of players had the impression that Bone Gnawers were basically dogs, not wolves. It doesn't help that page 29 of the tribebook actually shows a picture of a dog. (Even in the 1e corebook there are images of Bone Gnawers that seem much more like dogs than wolves, though this might simply be because of the lower quality of art in that sourcebook.) Even terminology like &quot;the Barking Chain&quot;, which this template references, creates the impression of dogs as opposed to wolves. Wolves don't really bark. Everyone says that wolves howl, but dogs bark. I understand the term may be poetic, but combined with other things, it creates a lot of confusion.<br /> <br /> I don't see the lupus of the Bone Gnawer being urban based. They are probably one of the tribes that are most wolf-starved. If you are going to assign a camp to lupus, the Hillfolk are more natural. The Bone Gnawer as described are VERY homid based, so there actually is not a lot for the lupus breed to go by. The tribebook just ignores the issue rather than engage it. It's major weakness that is not sufficiently addressed even in the Revised version.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my country many times wolves were seen on the city streets, eating trash, or in the smaller settlements, attacking herd, dogs and cats. We also have Kamyk (Stone in english), which was found on the side of the road after being hit by a car. He lost one of his front paws and still was able to escape from the animal shelter. For a few months, despite being hunted by the people from the shelter, he was living on the city streets, as he was without the pack and being unable to hunt. Many people wished him good luck and fed him (it was a holiday resort and he became kind of a tourist attraction). After a few months unfortunately he was caught and brought back to the shelter. There he has an enormous, 0.5 ha. big hunting territory, with better defences than the previous one. And still, the first thing he tried to do was trying to escape. So wolf living in the city for me it's totally acceptable. In my city, population about 700 k, it's normal to see boars, foxes, or deers on the streets. Sometimes even moose and, since few days, a lynx. And still, it's not Alaska but middle Europe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-11T10:19:33-08:00","id":1525347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525341#post1525341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So wolf living in the city for me it's totally acceptable. In my city, population about 700 k, it's normal to see boars, foxes, or deers on the streets. Sometimes even moose and, since few days, a lynx. And still, it's not Alaska but middle Europe.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that is understandable. When your city is within the range of certain wild animals it is natural to see some of them some of the time enter suburban or urban areas. There are still plenty of areas in Europe where wolves still dwell in the mountains and forests. Even in Los Angeles there are occasional reports of coyotes, mountain lions, and bears because those animals still live in the nearby mountains. Many cities in the US now report coyotes because they have spread so far. Your area still has wolves in the nearby countryside. So it is normal and easy for an ST to justify it in your city.<br /> <br /> I think that is a different scenario than what I am talking about. In the US the wolf is only extant in Alaska, the northern Rockies, and the northern Great Lakes area plus a few other isolated places. So if there are wolf packs scavenging in most major US cities (or say the British Isles, much of France, Australia, and other countries where they've been extirpated), they simply cannot wander in from the nearby wilderness. A pack of wild wolves in the city limits of New York City, Chicago, Washington, Dallas, London, Paris, etc. would not be a normal occurrence. It would be very unusual. Especially if they are now hunting exclusively in the urban environment and not the rare wolf wandering in and out from the wilderness. So if the Bone Gnawers - and perhaps other tribes that dwell in the city - have a stock of urban based lupus kinfolk that regularly scavenge there, it takes a lot more to explain. It changes the world. At the very least the ST needs to describe to the players how the setting departs from reality because players won't be expecting that based on their understanding of the city. The ST needs to do some world building and think through the scope and ramifications.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-11T10:33:15-08:00","id":1525348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525291#post1525291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, it shows the setting is not just in character bios, it actually affects how the world IS.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel this is a very dangerous road to go down as it assumes forethought and a broader design to these things. Like so many things White Wolf made these were done quickly and without much forethought.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-11T12:27:22-08:00","id":1525356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525347#post1525347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that is a different scenario than what I am talking about. In the US the wolf is only extant in Alaska, the northern Rockies, and the northern Great Lakes area plus a few other isolated places. So if there are wolf packs scavenging in most major US cities (or say the British Isles, much of France, Australia, and other countries where they've been extirpated), they simply cannot wander in from the nearby wilderness. A pack of wild wolves in the city limits of New York City, Chicago, Washington, Dallas, London, Paris, etc. would not be a normal occurrence. It would be very unusual. Especially if they are now hunting exclusively in the urban environment and not the rare wolf wandering in and out from the wilderness. So if the Bone Gnawers - and perhaps other tribes that dwell in the city - have a stock of urban based lupus kinfolk that regularly scavenge there, it takes a lot more to explain. It changes the world. At the very least the ST needs to describe to the players how the setting departs from reality because players won't be expecting that based on their understanding of the city. The ST needs to do some world building and think through the scope and ramifications.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>But the thing is that you've made an assumption that templates were created having North America in mind. I know that places of birth/live of the templates appeared later (for example in Stargazers tribebook; the first ones were in Ways of the Wolf but they were still in US) but that doesn't mean that they were all created for US setting. Even more: I find it funny that you don't assume the sex of the templates if it isn't depicted or shown in the description but you assume their place of birth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-11T19:44:06-08:00","id":1525363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525356#post1525356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the thing is that you've made an assumption that templates were created having North America in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was an American company using American authors selling to an American audience at the time. Early White Wolf material clearly defaulted to the US. We can safely assume the templates were indeed meant for North America although obviously some supplements were explicitly based in foreign countries, and these templates themselves - in a broad point of view - could be customized to fit different settings. While the World of Darkness did quickly obtain a large international audience and eventually a more global outlook in their material, I think it's quite silly to think the writers were not assuming a default for North American expectations.<br /> <br /> Even if it weren't, the situation this template described when it was not just a stray wolf wandering in from a nearby wilderness area that could match other regions in the world, but that entire packs of wolves seemed to be living in a specifically urban ecosystem which is not something that exists in reality, but is clearly fictional.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-12T01:26:22-08:00","id":1525368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525363#post1525363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was an American company using American authors selling to an American audience at the time. Early White Wolf material clearly defaulted to the US. We can safely assume the templates were indeed meant for North America although obviously some supplements were explicitly based in foreign countries, and these templates themselves - in a broad point of view - could be customized to fit different settings. While the World of Darkness did quickly obtain a large international audience and eventually a more global outlook in their material, I think it's quite silly to think the writers were not assuming a default for North American expectations.<br /> <br /> Even if it weren't, the situation this template described when it was not just a stray wolf wandering in from a nearby wilderness area that could match other regions in the world, but that entire packs of wolves seemed to be living in a specifically urban ecosystem which is not something that exists in reality, but is clearly fictional.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand Bone Gnawers tribebook was published shortly after Rage across Russia. And you know the stereotype about it: that wolves and bears live freely on the city streets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-15T19:59:31-08:00","id":1525495,"title":"","content":"Apologies but I have been a bit under the weather the past week. I should have the Galliard tomorrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-15T21:54:15-08:00","id":1525498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525495#post1525495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apologies but I have been a bit under the weather the past week. I should have the Galliard tomorrow.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's fine <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> . The cold has been going around at my work as well. Lucky for me, the worst I've had so far was a mild case of the sniffles. Hope you get better soon <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-16T10:57:29-08:00","id":1525525,"title":"","content":"<b>Hillfolk Hitchhiker</b> (Metis Galliard)<br /> <br /> Because, of course, the example character of the Breed born from spiritual incest is from a culture frequently stereotyped for inbreeding. In hindsight, I'm rather grateful that Ethan Skemp was actually from said culture so that most of that sort of thing went away under his tenure as developer. <br /> <br /> And, again, one whose name includes which Camp their from. At least this one has a little more than just &quot;Auspice + Camp&quot; like our first one. <br /> <br /> So, the character is the offspring of a pair of migrant workers. And yes, these turn out to be their real parents and not just Kinfolk who took them in. I'm not exactly sure how a pair of Garou live as migrant workers, let alone while having a Metis cub with them. But they also spent Falls and Winters with Kinfolk in the city. (This part actually makes a bit of sense, as during the boom period of WW2, a lot of Appalachian people moved to nearby cities for work. Baltimore, for example, has an entire area that has long been referred to as &quot;Billytown&quot;.) Eventually, they - the Kinfolk apparently, as the writing isn't all that clear - revealed they were werewolves and taught them how to change form. Apparently they took all of this in without even blinking. I wish I could be that blas\u00e9 about things. <br /> <br /> So, the Prelude is entirely about being Hillfolk. And now for the Concept section, which is about the Auspice and Hitchhiker parts. So they love mountain people music, and learned to play fiddle, harp, and harmonica, and also like to howl in the high mountain places. That's nice. I mean, I like the idea. But I'm left wondering why? I mean, besides the painfully obvious answer of &quot;because they're Galliard and that's what Galliards do.&quot; They now roam the roads, listening to the music of everyone they encounter and sharing their own music. <br /> <br /> They're very friendly and good natured. Their Metis deformity is Loose Teeth. Equipment is coveralls (I think they mean overalls), white T-shirt, harmonica, roadmaps, three cans of cheap beer (that's pretty random), backpack, and hiking boots. <br /> <br /> For Attributes, Physicals are tertiary, with 1/2/3. ::Sigh:: Again with the 1s.<br /> Socials are primary, with 4/4/2. I'm quite frankly shocked that Appearance isn't 1. And I'm sure that no one will be shocked to learn that the Ahroun character does have a 1 in Appearance. So out of these five templates, the only one with an Appearance above 1 is the Metis character. That's just sad. <br /> Mental is secondary, with 1/4/3. Again, another 1. And I'm not sure how such a character gets buy with such a low level of Perception. And then there's the Intelligence, which is the highest of the five. I get the idea of such a character being very intelligent, especially when it comes to remembering music, folklore, and the like, but I'm not sure this level is necessary. <br /> Honestly, I feel all of these need to be balanced out a little better. Socials are fine, but I think Physicals should be straight 2s across the board and Mental should be either 2/3/3 or 3/2/3.<br /> <br /> For Abilities, Talents are primary, with 3 each in Alertness, Athletics, and Empathy, 2 in Dodge, and 1 each in Brawl and Primal Urge. <br /> Skills are secondary, with 3 each in Performance and Survival, and 1 each in Animal Ken, Drive, and Stealth. <br /> Knowledge is tertiary, with 1 each in Enigmas, Investigation, Law, Linguistics, and Politics. <br /> Overall, these are fine. However, I'm not entirely sure why the character has Law. (Politics I can accept as a Grapes of Wrath/Tom Joad reference.) I think that dot might make more sense in Linguistics. I might also move one of those Athletic dots to Expression or possibly Dodge.<br /> <br /> Backgrounds are 5 dots in Allies. I guess I can see that. Although you'd think this might be spread among Allies and Contacts. <br /> <br /> Rage is 5. Gnosis is 4. Willpower is 6. <br /> <br /> That point of Rage, point of Gnosis, and two points of WP are the only five freebie points spent. There are ten more that haven't been used. It's been a while since I've seen missing freebies at this level. <br /> I'd probably spend at least six of them on Abilities (one each in Performance, Expression or Subterfuge, and Firearms or Melee). <br /> <br /> Overall, this isn't a terrible character. The screw up with the freebies is almost inexcusable, and I can't understand the obsession with the 1 ratings in Attributes. But the general concept is OK. However, I feel this would've been a lot better as a Homid rather than a Metis. A character who grew up in the Appalachian mountains with a love of music and culture, who now wanders around collecting the music and folklore of other poor and working class groups as a Songcatcher. (If you're unfamiliar with the work of Sharyn McCrumb, her novels set among the Appalachians and drawing on local folklore and music are very good.)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-16T11:44:09-08:00","id":1525528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525525#post1525525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But they also spent Falls and Winters with Kinfolk in the city. (This part actually makes a bit of sense, as during the boom period of WW2, a lot of Appalachian people moved to nearby cities for work. Baltimore, for example, has an entire area that has long been referred to as &quot;Billytown&quot;.) Eventually, they - the Kinfolk apparently, as the writing isn't all that clear - revealed they were werewolves and taught them how to change form. Apparently they took all of this in without even blinking. I wish I could be that blas\u00e9 about things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did the writers forget that a metis cub is not in fact a disabled human child but a tiny crinos? XD<br /> <br /> But yeah, agreed on the homid part. This character has little to do with being garou born and a lot to do with being from Appalachia.<br /> <br /> The loose teeth deformity is just,wow.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-16T11:54:27-08:00","id":1525531,"title":"","content":"A hitchhiker concept is a good one, but there are all sorts of issues with how it is written.<br /> <br /> First, the metis background just doesn't work. Wouldn't she be in crinos form growing up? Early WtA often had metis newborns change to a homid or lupus form, but that was always mentioned. Not addressing it really goes against the metis concept. Second, there is no indication her parents ever did the things we expect them to do as Garou. There doesn't seem to be mysterious disappearances as they go off and fight the Wyrm. Nothing that indicates her parents may essentially be a two person anruth pack going from caern to caern. Or are we to assume they are essentially AWOL from the Garou Nation? If they are, then that should be addressed. Furthermore, since they are Garou why does the template character need to learn about the Garou and how to change from him kin in the city? Wouldn't her Garou parents be doing that? The one advantage metis characters have over other breeds is that they grew up in Garou culture and know things much better than homids and lupus. Why remove that from this character?<br /> <br /> This seems like something written for a homid and then quickly rewritten to make it metis without the writer bothering to think things through. Homid breed would probably make more sense, but metis can work - it just needs to be properly explained and addressed.<br /> <br /> Second, I agree that her harmonica, three points of Performance, and listening to music everywhere she travels seems tacked on to make the concept a Galliard. A better approach might have been her collecting stories and rumors from the different areas she visits. She can compile news, stories, and folklore, figuring out stuff concerning the Wyrm while doing so. That would give her hitchhiking some background and be of value. These early Galliard templates all seem to fall back to Galliard = musician. There needs to be more variety for this auspice. If you do need to go down the musical route once again, put something in that better establishes it for the character like how her parents and her constantly used music to occupy their time when they travelled.<br /> <br /> Third, Allies 5 doesn't work for me. There's no indication in the description that she is building strong relationships with people who are now strongly inclined to help her out. Being &quot;friendly&quot; just isn't enough. This would work better either as Contacts or an extended Kinfolk network. Kinfolk 5 would net her an impressive 50 Kinfolk who could provide a lot of support for a hitchhiking Garou. Especially in terms of people willing to pick her up and drive her to the next stop (some could be truckers who could be on a long haul), as a Garou with Rage 5 should be affecting 63% of people with the Curse. Not many people would want to pick up an unknown hitchhiker that would cause them to fear they are picking up some dangerous person. Unless you justify it by using Kinfolk, the hitchhiking concept would work better for a Ragabash. But like with many concepts, the Curse just gets ignored so this will be a common complaint. If the writers even bothered to address the Curse and mention how it affected the concept and addressed it, I think these templates would have done a lot to help STs and PCs integrate that concept into their chronicles in a useful way.<br /> <br /> The Metis deformity is weird to me. It's one of the example deformities provided in the first Players Guide, but it only comes into play if you use bite as a weapon. There's nothing really symbolic or impactful in terms of the character concept which is unusual. Unless the writer intended it to be a commentary on poor dental health for a hillbilly. I do like the idea of a metis deformity that is not readily apparent. There should be more of those. Unfortunately, the 2e corebook and 1e Players Guide do not have many examples so we're limited here at finding a replacement that would make sense for this tribebook. Maybe silver sensitivity instead. But there is nothing inherently wrong with Loose Teeth. It just seems like another afterthought though.<br /> <br /> As you mentioned, this is the only concept with an Appearance greater than 1. Though given that she's supposed to be an incredibly friendly hitchhiker who makes lots of friends, an even higher Appearance could be justified. Nothing wrong with just a 2 though. But in line with the other templates, it's still part of the pattern that Bone Gnawers must not be attractive.<br /> <br /> While I want to like this template, I think there's too many problems with it. The basic concept is fine and has lots of potential, but I would alter her background and much of her character sheet. In addition, there is a lot of white space left on the character description page. This could have been used to flesh out the character concept more and address these issues. And what kind of migrant work her parents did would be good to know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-16T12:21:39-08:00","id":1525532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525531#post1525531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, there is no indication her parents ever did the things we expect them to do as Garou. There doesn't seem to be mysterious disappearances as they go off and fight the Wyrm. Nothing that indicates her parents may essentially be a two person anruth pack going from caern to caern. Or are we to assume they are essentially AWOL from the Garou Nation? If they are, then that should be addressed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in one early WtA short story, there is a female Silver Fang lupus living in a zoo. Not kinfolk, a lupus. And she basically chills there and has pups. So in early WtA, being AWOL from the Nation seems to be pretty normal.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-16T12:31:15-08:00","id":1525533,"title":"","content":"I forgot to mention that I kept referring to the character as &quot;they&quot; because the write up didn't really indicate gender and the image, which I also forgot to talk about, could be read as male or female. <br /> <br /> Said image being a very skinny young individual in overalls, t-shirt, boots, and straw hat, playing a harmonica. The character also seems to have unusually large hands compared to the rest of their body. <br /> <br /> And yes, I think this character would be a lot better as a Homid who is sort of an amateur folklorist, with the music an aspect of that but not the whole, expanding it to include oral history, superstitions, urban legends, folk tales, and the like. This would require moving a few points around to give them some Occult ability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-16T13:09:49-08:00","id":1525535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525532#post1525532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in early WtA, being AWOL from the Nation seems to be pretty normal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's fine. No problem with characters being like that, especially given how in early editions the Garou Nation had much more internal discontent and societal breakdown that later. Eventually the revised tribebook outright states much of the tribe is Rabble that doesn't do anything. So Bone Gnawer drops outs don't need much explanation. But if that is the case, some mention of it should be made. Because if a player is given this character, one of her first questions will be &quot;What's up with Mom and Dad?&quot; Maybe they just dropped out of the Nation after they decided to have their metis baby and say, &quot;To hell with it, our only concern is our child now.&quot; Or any other number of reasons. But then the character needs a reason why she decided to go to it - even if it is simply curiosity, an exhortation by one of her kinfolk, or a defining event.<br /> <br /> There's some good grist there to really provide a good hook for a player. By being lazy and not thinking things through, it creates a much weaker template.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-17T15:20:25-08:00","id":1525572,"title":"","content":"<b>Frankweiler Knight</b> (Homid Ahroun)<br /> <br /> And, once again, the Camp + Vague Descriptor naming convention. <br /> <br /> So, the Frankweilers are a Camp who tend to lurk about and make their territories in various urban museums, libraries, churches, theaters, and other places of culture. If you've ever wondered, the name comes from a book by E L Konigsburg called <i>From the Mixed-Up Files of Mrs. Basil E. Frankweiler</i>. Someone must have been a fan of the book as a kid to have used it here. I'm not sure why though, as the titular Mrs. Frankweiler is one of NYC's wealthy elite, while the two kids who live in the Metropolitan Museum of Art are named Kincaid. Also, the book came out in 1967, so I'm wondering what this Camp would've been called before that. <br /> <br /> Anyway ...<br /> <br /> He was born backstage at a theater during a production of Hamlet, and grew up in and around that world. At least until Child Protective Services took him away and put him in a foster home. Apparently he was bullied to some degree, and at age 13 freaked out, underwent the First Change, and killed several of the other kids in the home. This may be the darkest First Change out of the ones we've looked at so far. <br /> He was found by local Bone Gnawers, and now lives on the run (I presume wanted for multiple murders), spending his time hiding in various theaters and museums. He likes to fool around with antique armor and weapons and speaks in a mix of Shakespearian English and modern American. I honestly can help but imagine this character coming across a bit like Thor in the Marvel Comics (back in the old pre-MCU days). <br /> <br /> Equipment is antique silken clothing stolen from a museum, a book of Shakespeare plays, a broadsword, and a big black cloak. <br /> <br /> The image is of a man, maybe early 20s, dressed like he's costumed for a Shakespearian play. He looks fairly handsome (this will be important in a moment), and may be meant to be African American. <br /> <br /> For Attributes, Physicals are primary, with a 4/5/1 spread. And again with the 1 dot attributes. Honestly, when I see a character with a 1 in Stamina, I expect them to have some sort of health issue. <br /> Socials are secondary, with 5/2/1. Good grief. Remember what I said about the image? This guy looks like a fairly handsome young actor. <br /> And finally Mental is tertiary, with ... 2/1/3. Oh FFS. <br /> I think this may be the only time I've seen a character with three attributes at 1. This is just ridiculous. A wannabe Shakespearian actor turned knight, who has the stamina of an asthmatic octogenarian, the appearance of Quasimodo, and the brains of Forrest Gump. <br /> <br /> For Abilities, Talents are secondary, with 2 each in Alertness, Dodge, and Empathy, and 1 each in Intimidation, Primal Urge, and Streetwise. <br /> Skills are primary, with 3 each in Etiquette, Melee, Performance, and Stealth, and 1 in Leadership. <br /> Knowledge is tertiary, with 3 in Linguistics, and 1 each in Enigmas and Medicine. <br /> Some of these abilities are fine. I'm sort of surprised he doesn't have anything in Athletics or Expression. Streetwise also feels kind of low for a guy who effectively squats in whatever urban cultural center he can find.<br /> <br /> Backgrounds are 2 in Allies and 3 in Contacts. These seem fine, but I wish I had some sort of information on who or what these represent. <br /> I will also note that, aside from the Theurge having the Rites background, Allies and Contacts are the only backgrounds any of these characters have. I realize that the tribe is barred from having Past Life, Pure Breed, and Resources, but no one has Kinfolk, Fetish, Mentor, or Totem? <br /> <br /> Rage is 7, Gnosis is 3 and Willpower is 6. These eight freebies are the only ones spent. There are seven unspent points here. <br /> <br /> Conceptually, this isn't a bad character. The write up is fairly decent and he seems like a potentially interesting person to play. However, the stats are mostly a broken mess.<br /> The Attributes need to be balanced out to get rid of the 1s. I think 3/4/3, 4/2/2, and 2/2/2 would work fine.<br /> I really don't think he needs the extra Gnosis, and the eleven freebie points could've gone a long way toward boosting his some of his abilities. A Mentor might also be useful. <br /> <br /> And so that's the Bone Gnawers. Overall, these are some fairly decent ideas, but they tend to fall down a little (sometimes a lot) in execution. I've no idea what the deal is with the low Appearance traits, beyond the suggestion that someone decided they were the Werewolf equivalent to Nosferatu. <br /> The weird limiting of Backgrounds to only three of them is also a mystery. <br /> <br /> Next will be Children of Gaia.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-17T15:29:24-08:00","id":1525573,"title":"","content":"The only reasoning I could find for low Attributes would be rough living and nutritional and health care deficits, but Garou health and the Cooking Gift should probably keep at least some of that at bay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-17T20:16:21-08:00","id":1525578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525572#post1525572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this may be the only time I've seen a character with three attributes at 1. This is just ridiculous. A wannabe Shakespearian actor turned knight, who has the stamina of an asthmatic octogenarian, the appearance of Quasimodo, and the brains of Forrest Gump.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good summary of the character and why I hate it.\u200b This is my least favorite template of the book. In fact, I think it stinks. I don't even like the concept. I find it bizarre as written.<br /> <br /> If you were going to write an Ahroun template for the Frankweiler camp, I would have imagined someone like a bouncer at a theatre, or perhaps a security guard type concept (either officially, or perhaps in secret). Not some person who acts like a &quot;Shakespearean Warlord&quot;. The template, in my opinion, doesn't even actually fit the description of the Frankweiler camp. It's just that &quot;Hey, the theatre is kind of associated with the Frankweiler camp&quot; and then no further actual thoughts.<br /> <br /> I honestly think the writer couldn't come up with an intriguing Ahroun concept and just threw some ideas together that superficially seemed to fit so that another camp was theoretically represented.<br /> <br /> Who actually would want to play this? Not only for all the terrible character sheet mistakes. With a strong concept, a player can easily adjust a character sheet to work. The character seems like a doofus with way too many problems.<br /> <br /> There are individual parts that could be salvaged for a legitimate concept. Make the character some kind of street theatre person and make the auspice Ragabash and amp up his acting skills (that he can use in other ways). Concentrate on his love of books, plays, and theatres, and make him a Galliard teaching culture to others. Make him a protector of the local library who scares away gang activity so kids and teens have a safe place to learn and help them move out of the ghetto. But as written, I find it terrible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525572#post1525572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rage is 7, Gnosis is 3 and Willpower is 6.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having Rage greater than Willpower is always bad. Per the rules, the Beast Within is active and the Garou losing die or dice on social rolls. So this is even worse than just the Curse.<br /> <br /> The character sheet's Backgrounds, as you mentioned, are terrible. They always seem to be an afterthought as opposed to something to be developed in the template description.<br /> <br /> I think the Templates for this sourcebook started really strong, and then progressively got worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-17T21:24:14-08:00","id":1525580,"title":"","content":"I think if you asked me to do a Bone Gnawer Ahroun template, the first thing that would come to mind would be this local urban legend, a monster that comes out of the darkness to protect the local homeless and street people from threats both human and supernatural. Something that drew a bit on the 80s tv series Beauty and The Beast and this story I remember Henry Rollins relating in one of his spoken word bits about a local homeless guy who had both of his arms smashed and broken by a gang of rich LA high school kids with baseball bats. And I realize that this is essentially the Vigilante Wolf character from this book, which I think would probably work better as a Metis Ahroun. <br /> <br /> I really like the idea of the Frankweiler camp, and while I think this is at least the start of a potentially cool idea, it needs some work and I'm not sure it is the best for an example of the Camp or the Auspice. (I do think you could have done something interesting with a Theurge grailseeker type inspired by Robin Williams's character in The Fisher King.) <br /> <br /> When it comes to Camps, I always want to know how each Auspice would express itself as part of that group, as well as what place each Breed would have there. What role would Galliards and Ahroun play in the Rat Finks? Why might a Lupus decide to be a Frankweiler? That sort of thing. <br /> <br /> I think an interesting idea for a Philodox would be a lawyer who lives and works out of his old and worn out car, doing a lot of pro bono work to help the local community (including its homeless and various shelters, churches, clinics, etc.). They could have ties to the Rat Finks, Hood, and Frankweilers, and eventually end up as a member of whichever group the player wanted.<br /> <br /> Also, I confess that I am mildly disappointed that we don't have anything that riffs on the junkyard dog archetype, with a Lupus who hangs around an urban scrapyard, perhaps as a protector of a Caern or some spirit there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-17T22:50:17-08:00","id":1525581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525580#post1525580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I confess that I am mildly disappointed that we don't have anything that riffs on the junkyard dog archetype, with a Lupus who hangs around an urban scrapyard, perhaps as a protector of a Caern or some spirit there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Junkyard Dog would be a great template concept for the Bone Gnawers. Maybe something like an urban legend of a terrible spectral dog that haunts an area. Sometimes you want to go with the classics.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-18T02:58:20-08:00","id":1525584,"title":"","content":"I wonder how much the sheet team and the art commission team talked to each other, given the app 1s. I at least would first ask the app stat if I were to do template art.<br /> <br /> I truly think they had Nosferatu in mind when they statted these guys, not focusing on the fact that homeless does not mean ugly.<br /> <br /> I like the Vigilante Wolf and the Rust Shaman most, they both seem like Bone Gnawer concepts. Ratfink is fine, but could also be a kinfolk. The other two are baffling and ill-statted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-18T04:47:14-08:00","id":1525588,"title":"","content":"With the insistence on App 1, I think the idea of Bone Gnawers being of lower status is just taken way too far. In that it really is thought of as comparable to the Nosferatu-curse. It's App 1 because somehow just from looking at the Bone Gnawer, them being &quot;lesser&quot; just is apparent. But it has to be this mysterious, supernatural thing that somehow was applied here because both in writing and the art, it isn't like these Bone Gnawers characters were treated like they're all these Nosferatu-esque hideos monsters. There's nothing or very little to make you go &quot;Oh yeah, that character has App 1.&quot;. The reasoning for App 1 (with one exception being 2) in all thee cases can really only be tied back to them all being Bone Gnawers. But then you already got the Tribal Weakness reflecting the lower status. It's really unnecessary to add this unmentioned need for App 1 as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-18T06:44:57-08:00","id":1525591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525584#post1525584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder how much the sheet team and the art commission team talked to each other, given the app 1s. I at least would first ask the app stat if I were to do template art.</div> </div> </div> </div>Typically, at least by the revised era, template and who's who entries would start with [Art Notes] (brackets would indicate that said text was for the Developer and not part of the actual book material, in this case to be passed on to the Art Developer who would give them to the assigned artist) giving at least a basic description of what the writer was hoping for. <br /> <br /> Sometimes you get certain oddities, such as when Sean Riley didn't think to specify that Kleon Winston, a character who had originally appeared in Rage Across New York, was African American, and so you ended up having the image of him in the revised tribebook be a white guy. <br /> <br /> Then you have the case of Christopher Shy's revised period work, where it seemed he just mostly did whatever the heck he felt like regardless of any art notes. The massive amount of facial tattoos in Vampire's Children of the Night, for example, as well as the Assamite sorcerer Al Ashrad having to retroactively be made the only member of his clan to be pale white and not darken with age because Shy turned in a piece that was effectively an albino. And then his overly cyberpunk photoshopped work for revised Mage, which resulted in a lot of the chapter opening fiction and even some of the signature characters having to be rewritten. (There was some speculation, comparing his work with what Leif Jones did for the Tradition write ups, that the Verbena signature character may have originally been meant to be African American.)<br /> <br /> On the other end of the spectrum, you have someone like Ron Spenser, whose work would sometimes be so detailed that I swear he must have read the entire manuscript before doing his work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-18T08:09:26-08:00","id":1525592,"title":"","content":"And still in 1994 with <b>Children of Gaia</b>. This was written by Daniel Greenberg with Heather Curatola. Greenberg was the writer for Vampire's original Malkavian clan book, which doesn't exactly fill me with hope here. (I think he was Vampire Developer Andrew Greenberg's brother, and apparently did most of his freelancing while a college student.) Curatola is also known as Heather Heckel after marrying fellow White Wolf author Harry Heckel. Template art is again by Josh Timbrook.<br /> <br /> This was, IIRC, when you first saw some of the Middle Eastern aspects of the tribe in an effort to flesh them out from more than just &quot;the Baby Boomer era Hippy werewolves&quot; that they started as. Unfortunately, a lot of it is still tied up in a lot of that era's more New Age-y grasp of various Eastern philosophies and religions, as well as paganism and various social causes. The Tribe's Camps are especially thin, most having only one or two paragraph in-character write ups that don't really give you much beyond the most basic idea. The one exception is the Aethera Inamorata, a Camp primarily based on how wonderful sex is, that gets at least half a page. (Inamorata is an old Latin term for a person's female lover. Aethera refers to aether/air. Apparently the literal translation is &quot;Aether in love&quot;. I presume it is meant to refer to something similar to the Sons of Ether's concept, with it being some sort of spiritual force permeating anything to do with love and sex.) <br /> <br /> And, naturally, every single one of these templates is a member of a Camp. Even if they don't make any mention of why they are a member or how they are supposed to express that Camp's (very vague) ideals. <br /> <br /> <b>Wise Fool</b> (Lupus Ragabash)<br /> <br /> Apparently the offspring of another Lupus Garou, which is presented as being a rarity. They were raised by the Tribe and learned how to be tolerant and understanding of other Tribes and Breeds. Their First Change was very non-traumatic. <br /> Conceptually, they focus on using laughter and humor as a way to distract other Garou from their conflicts, concerns, and pains. This includes being perfectly willing to make themselves the butt of jokes when necessary. <br /> They make friends very easily, are charming and loyal, eager to help others, and extremely patient. <br /> <br /> Equipment includes juggling balls, a cloak of many colors, marbles, bits of string, a chew toy, and a kite. The balls, cloak, and chew toy I can get behind. Maybe even the kite and marbles. Bits of string seem trivial. Like telling me that a character's equipment includes 63 cents in pocket change. I also feel like said cloak should be a fetish of some sort. <br /> <br /> The image is of a Garou in Crinos form, with said cloak , their hair (such as it is) pulled back into what looks like they're hoping to grow out into a man bun at some point, and juggling a pair of balls. I honestly kind of hate it. Mainly because it looks like a Garou trying to pretend to be a furry. There is none of the sense of Rage or danger I expect from the Garou war form, even taking the Tribe's weakness into account. <br /> <br /> As I mentioned, all of these characters have a Camp listed, and this one's is the Aethera Inamorata. I have no clue as to why. Nothing about the character's write up mentions anything about sex or using it as a method of spiritual healing. Nor about helping arrange liaisons and marriages between Garou and Kinfolk. About the closest you get is the character's focus on laugher as an expression of love, perhaps. I don't think this character needs to be part of a Camp. But if you were to force me to put them in one, I think The Patient Deed would have made more sense. <br /> <br /> For Attributes, Physicals are tertiary with an extra dot from freebies, for a 2/3/2 spread. Socials are primary with 4/3/3. Mental is secondary with 2/2/4. <br /> These seem perfectly fine. I do appreciate some attention being paid to Manipulation, with some acknowledgement that the character is manipulating others on a certain level. I might even go so far do say that a 4/4/2 spread for Socials wouldn't have been out of place here. <br /> <br /> For Abilities, Talents are primary with an extra dot from freebies. They have 3 each in Alertness, Athletics, and Empathy, a 2 in Primal Urge, and 1 each in Brawl, Dodge, and Streetwise. <br /> Skills are secondary with a 3 in Performance, 2 each in Leadership and Survival, and 1 each in Animal Ken and Stealth. <br /> Knowledge is tertiary, with 3 in Enigmas and 2 in Medicine. <br /> So, Medicine is one of the restricted abilities for Lupus. While I can sort of understand why this character might have learned such an ability, it should've been bought with freebies. I think those points would work better in Investigation and/or Rituals, and both would fit certain aspects of the character (both the Ragabash Auspice and the character's interest in learning about others for the former; their having grown up entirely among Garou for the former). <br /> I think that dot of Streetwise might do better as Subterfuge, owing to what I mentioned earlier about the character being manipulative to a certain degree. I do appreciate them having Leadership. It's a nice change of pace for a Ragabash after a lot of the 1st ed material. I think they might also benefit slightly from having some degree of Expression. <br /> <br /> Backgrounds are 5 dots in Allies. I find this disappointing, especially after Bone Gnawers overused that background. Like I said before, I think the cloak mentioned under equipment might've made the interesting basis for a Fetish of some sort. And given the mention of the character's mother being Garou (as well as saying this was rare), Pure Breed would also seem like a fitting Background here. Also Mentor given how the character has effectively been raised by Garou all their life. <br /> <br /> This is the first character to have spent freebies (seven of them) on a fourth Gift. I'm not entirely sure why they need the extra Ragabash gift (they have both Blur of the Milky Eye and Open Seal). Neither feels overly necessary for the character concept, even if I can see how both might be useful in play. <br /> <br /> Rage is 2. Gnosis is 5. Willpower is 4. I don't think that extra dot of Rage is necessary. If anything, it might work against the character concept. <br /> <br /> I really feel those eight freebie points could've been better spent on Abilities and Backgrounds. Maybe also a slight WP boost. <br /> <br /> So, I do not hate this character. I'm not entirely certain that I like it either, but part of that may be because of the artwork. Overall, I think this concept works fairly well with the Tribe, and for certain aspects of the Auspice. (It certainly moves closer to Questioner of the Ways than some of the earlier generic trickster or gutter punk concepts.) I'm not really sure why the character is a Lupus, even if that Breed perhaps works a bit better for this than the other two might. (Lupus are probably more likely to open up to another Lupus, and social prejudice against Metis might end up working against it.) And I see no reason why it has to be part of a Camp, let alone the one selected. So, this is probably a better start that I might have feared given the Tribe's reputation and stereotypes, especially in the early days.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-18T09:27:12-08:00","id":1525594,"title":"","content":"It's a weak template, but without anything too objectionable. The name is Wise Fool, but something like Wisecracker, Class Clown, or Company Joker would probably be better as the entire concept is about his ability to make others laugh. It seems heavily based on the idea that pack omegas clown around and help disperse any stress or tension within the pack, but without emphasizing the omega part.<br /> <br /> The problem is someone making the rest of the pack (or sept) laugh is more like a personality quirk you add to a character, not the basis of one. What exactly does this character bring to the pack during play? What kind of things does the character do? Is he an infiltrator and uses his sense of humor to gain trust? Is he really oriented into Garou society and going to embed himself into the sept and going towards a leadership position within the Garou? Is it his athletic skills that are going to come into play like an acrobatic burglar (if so he needs more Stealth)? As is, the character just seems to be the type that really needs to be given direction by the other PCs and told what to do. It's a weak hook.<br /> <br /> As written, it seems to be that his ability to make people laugh and always helping others is what gets him Allies, and his 5 dots of Allies is the key. He's the guy who knows a guy that can help them. But I don't think this aspect really works. Simply because people like you doesn't mean they are going to stick their neck out for you, which is what Allies means. This character had to have done something important for each of these Allies, and we're not given any idea of what that could be. It's also very strange for a lupus to have so many Allies. Certainly not impossible, but it means a very human society centered lupus. Maybe it's wilderness centered humans - park rangers, veterinarians, rescue shelters, and other people he might have met and helped by volunteering in a lot of groups doing things for animals and the wilderness. Some groups are desperate for volunteers, and a hard working wisecracker type that makes things fun would help retain and attract more volunteers. That and being dependable might make some people willing to help that person out, especially if it is for things closely related to their own activity. But there's nothing in the description that would lead one to this direction.<br /> <br /> It's a consistent problem with these Templates to give the character Allies but not \u200bprovide any description of how they were obtained or what kind of things they should do. I understand many Players will want to customize these characters, but there needs to be a bridge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525592#post1525592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I mentioned, all of these characters have a Camp listed, and this one's is the Aethera Inamorata. I have no clue as to why. Nothing about the character's write up mentions anything about sex or using it as a method of spiritual healing.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is a throwaway line about how he felt the First Change to be &quot;curiously arousing experience&quot;. I think that's the extent of it. Unless we're supposed to read something into how he makes all those friends and allies. I agree that there's no real connection to the camp at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525592#post1525592\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they might also benefit slightly from having some degree of Expression.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would make the Expression the go to Ability to represent someone who can constantly wisecrack and make people laugh so I agree it should be improved from its zero ranks.<br /> <br /> All together it's a very BLEH template. Nothing that would make me want to play a Children of Gaia Ragabash. There are certainly some interesting ideas in the sourcebook, but as written in the material, the CoG are probably my least favorite tribe with a lot of baggage. It's why I ended up going with a &quot;Protect the Innocent and Unspoiled&quot; angle more aligned with folklore and legend around unicorns for the tribe in my chronicles, rather than the idea that &quot;It's all about Love, especially the sexual kind&quot; that the tribebooks default to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rjlSiASsUIs\" data-code=\"rjlSiASsUIs\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/rjlSiASsUIs/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-18T11:08:43-08:00","id":1525601,"title":"","content":"Out of all the tribes, the Coggies suffer the most with their initial concept of peacemakers/hippies. As I stated before, they are still written as the upper middle class youths with no other flavours. The best description for the tribe I've seen comes from the tribebook of another tribe entirely.<br /> <br /> And Wise Fool shows this, by being an interesting idea hampered by the lack of thinking about the stats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-18T11:29:53-08:00","id":1525602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525601#post1525601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The best description for the tribe I've seen comes from the tribebook of another tribe entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which one, out of curiosity?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-18T11:36:43-08:00","id":1525604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525602#post1525602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which one, out of curiosity?</div> </div> </div> </div>Silent Strider's Revised, essentially painting the Coggies as using their peaceful ways to shame other garou and slowly convince the Nation that there is no need of tribes. I always liked that, because it gives a very cool dark twist on the tribe. They are trying to ensure future garou souls all end up as Coggies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-18T14:53:36-08:00","id":1525607,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think they work better when you focus on them as one of the Leadership Tribes of the Garou Nation (along with the Silver Fangs and Shadow Lords, and how Middle Brother was in the Pure Lands). At some point, I sort of rewrote setting history a little for my Werewolf the Dark Ages games so that the whole Silver Crown thing happened in the early 12th century, and now there is sort of a three way civil war happening in the aftermath between Falcon Banner loyalists to the Silver Fangs, the revolutionary Army of Thunder led by the Shadow Lords, and the Children of Gaia's Unicorn Crusade that is allegedly fighting for peaceful coexistence but several of its leaders are really wanting to take over the Garou Nation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-18T16:19:13-08:00","id":1525610,"title":"","content":"<b>Supernatural Investigator</b> (Homid Theurge)<br /> <br /> So, this guy grew up with a real fascination - obsession even - with stories about otherworldly creatures and supernatural beings. Especially movies about vampires and other creatures which implied that said beings weren't necessarily evil and could even be the good guys. (Too bad this predates the Buffy tv show; this guy would've been a super-fan of that.) Apparently his First Change happened while he was laying in bed reading by moonlight. And I thought the Bone Gnawer Hitchhiker's First Change was pretty chill. Yeesh. <br /> He started &quot;nocturnal missions&quot; out into the supernatural world to meet all the creatures he used to read about. Exactly when he was found by other Garou, did his Rite of Passage, and joined the Children of Gaia is not mentioned at all. <br /> And then things take a turn for the cringe. <br /> <br /> Apparently he met a bunch of &quot;highly moral&quot; vampires, naturally of Clan Gangrel. I am going to pretend that these vampires are Edge and Christian of the WWE (points if you get the joke there) because that will make me laugh rather than cry at this next bit. They introduced him to a bunch of other vampires, and they're totally helping him look for this legendary vampire who supposedly transcended vampirism. I guess this means Saulot, in which case all the stuff that eventually came about in Vampire's metaplot just makes that even funnier. <br /> <br /> He's also met fairies, mages, ghosts, demons and lots of other stuff. And he's decided that the ones that are selfish are Wyrm oriented, while the ones who actually care about others are for Gaia. I can't exactly fault that sort of reasoning, but I have this suspicion that non-selfish vampires are perhaps a bit scarce. Demons even more so. So the fact that this guy seems to think that a lot of vampires are A-OK and have a lot to teach the Garou makes me question his level of awareness. <br /> <br /> Yes, this entire book has this weird fixation on vampires as being an antithesis of life and Gaia while at the same time being super important because some of them can reach Golconda and that's something Garou need to learn from. And I think the main reason this character exists is because of that. <br /> <br /> Anyway, he's apparently building alliances with all of these other supernatural beings to help the Garou. <br /> <br /> ::Sigh::<br /> <br /> For equipment, he's got a cell phone, a trench coat (of course he does, but I'll get to that in a minute), a pistol, a miniature infrared camera, a pocket tape recorder, and a laptop. <br /> <br /> The image is of a guy in a trench coat with what looks like a cigarette in his mouth and his hands in his pockets. The face looks like some mash up of Fox Mulder of the X-Files and John Constantine from DC/Vertigo's Hellblazer. His eyes look rather odd, like maybe he's high or something. It's obvious that Mulder and Constantine are the primary inspirations behind this character. <br /> <br /> He's a member of the Patient Deed camp. I only know this because it's on the character sheet. There's nothing at all in the write up about it. Or even about his Tribe. <br /> <br /> For Attributes, Physicals are tertiary with 2/2/2. Socials are primary with 4/3/3. Mental is secondary with an additional dot from freebies for 3s across the board. <br /> While I realize that this guy seems to be a friendly &quot;get out there and meet people&quot; sort of person, I feel like he'd be better served with Socials and Mental being switched. <br /> <br /> For Abilities, Talents are primary, with 3 each in Empathy and Streetwise, 2 each in Alertness and Brawl, and 1 each in Intimidation, Primal Urge, and Subterfuge. <br /> Skills are tertiary, with a 2 in Firearms and 1 each in Drive, Melee, and Stealth. <br /> Knowledge is secondary with one extra dot from freebies, with a 4 in Enigmas, a 3 in Occult, and 1 each in Politics and Rituals. (And yes, he is missing a dot in Knowledges, as at least two freebies were spent on that fourth dot in Enigmas.)<br /> I will point out that we have a Supernatural Investigator who has no points in Investigation. I'd say that maybe a more proper name might be Supernatural Diplomat, but he has such low Politics and Subterfuge, and no Etiquette. <br /> <br /> Backgrounds are 3 in Allies (I presume his Gangrel buddies), and 2 in Rites. I am just going to guess he has Rites because he's a Theurge and they all have to have that just because they are Theurges. <br /> You would think that with as many different supernatural creatures this guy has met, he might at least have some Contacts. But no. <br /> <br /> Rage is 2. Gnosis is a whopping 5 (that's where the bulk of his freebies went). Willpower is 4. <br /> <br /> I really don't care for this one. It's not the alleged concept. A paranormal investigator is a potentially cool idea for a Theurge. Perhaps better suited to the Uktena or maybe Silent Striders (especially if focused on ghosts), but still good. But this really isn't that. He's essentially a werewolf who hangs out with vampires. Honestly, between that and the totally lack of any mention of his Tribe in the write up, I feel like I'm reading something that should be in the Ronin chapter of WoD: Outcasts. This feels like something that started with the whole X-Files &quot;I want to believe&quot; idea (which isn't a bad idea) and quickly veered off the rails with the Vampire crossover stuff and turned into a very weak and toothless attempt at Hellblazer. <br /> I think the character freebies are largely wasted on such a high Gnosis score, especially considering how lacking his Abilities are in certain areas. <br /> So this one is just broken, both conceptually and mechanically. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-18T16:26:26-08:00","id":1525611,"title":"","content":"<b>Supernatural Investigator</b> (Homid Theurge)<br /> <br /> So, this guy grew up with a real fascination - obsession even - with stories about otherworldly creatures and supernatural beings. Especially movies about vampires and other creatures which implied that said beings weren't necessarily evil and could even be the good guys. Apparently his First Change happened while he was laying in bed reading by moonlight. And I thought the Hitchhiker's First Change was pretty chill.<br /> He started &quot;nocturnal missions&quot; out into the supernatural world to meet all the creatures he used to read about. Exactly when he was found by other Garou, did his Rite of Passage, and joined the Children of Gaia is not mentioned at all.<br /> And then things take a turn for the cringe.<br /> <br /> Apparently he met a bunch of &quot;highly moral&quot; vampires, naturally of Clan Gangrel. I am going to pretend that these vampires are Edge and Christian of the WWE (points if you get the joke there) because that will make me laugh rather than cry at this next bit. They introduced him to a bunch of other vampires, and they're totally helping him look for this legendary vampire who supposedly transcended vampirism. I guess this means Saulot, in which case all the stuff that eventually came about in Vampire's metaplot just makes that even funnier.<br /> <br /> He's also met fey, mages, ghosts, demons and lots of other stuff. And he's decided that the ones that are selfish are Wyrm oriented, while the ones who actually care about others are for Gaia. I can't exactly fault that sort of reasoning, but I have this suspicion that non-selfish vampires are perhaps a bit scarce. Demons even more so. So the fact that this guy seems to think that a lot of vampires are cool and have a lot to teach the Garou makes me question his level of awareness.<br /> <br /> Yes, this entire book has a rather odd take on vampires, being bad but also Garou need to learn about Golconda or something. <br /> <br /> Anyway, he's apparently building alliances with all of these other supernatural beings to help the Garou.<br /> <br /> For equipment, he's got a cell phone, a trench coat (of course he does, but I'll get to that in a minute), a pistol, a miniature infrared camera, a pocket tape recorder, and a laptop.<br /> <br /> The image is of a guy in a trench coat with what looks like a cigarette in his mouth and his hands in his pockets. The face looks like some mash up of Fox Mulder of the X-Files and John Constantine from DC/Vertigo's Hellblazer. His eyes look rather odd. It's obvious that Mulder and Constantine are the primary inspirations behind this character.<br /> <br /> He's a member of the Patient Deed camp. I only know this because it's on the character sheet. There's nothing at all in the write up about it. Or even about his Tribe.<br /> <br /> For Attributes, Physicals are tertiary with 2/2/2. Socials are primary with 4/3/3. Mental is secondary with an additional dot from freebies for 3s across the board.<br /> While I realize that this guy seems to be a friendly &quot;get out there and meet people&quot; sort of person, I feel like he'd be better served with Socials and Mental being switched.<br /> <br /> For Abilities, Talents are primary, with 3 each in Empathy and Streetwise, 2 each in Alertness and Brawl, and 1 each in Intimidation, Primal Urge, and Subterfuge.<br /> Skills are tertiary, with a 2 in Firearms and 1 each in Drive, Melee, and Stealth.<br /> Knowledge is secondary with one extra dot from freebies, with a 4 in Enigmas, a 3 in Occult, and 1 each in Politics and Rituals. (And yes, he is missing a dot in Knowledges, as at least two freebies were spent on that fourth dot in Enigmas.)<br /> I will point out that we have a Supernatural Investigator who has no points in Investigation. I'd say that maybe a more proper name might be Supernatural Diplomat, but he has such low Politics and Subterfuge, and no Etiquette.<br /> <br /> Backgrounds are 3 in Allies (I presume his Gangrel buddies), and 2 in Rites. I am just going to guess he has Rites because he's a Theurge and they all have to have that just because they are Theurges.<br /> You would think that with as many different supernatural creatures this guy has met, he might at least have some Contacts. But no.<br /> <br /> Rage is 2. Gnosis is a whopping 5 (that's where the bulk of his freebies went). Willpower is 4.<br /> <br /> I really don't care for this one. It's not the alleged concept. A paranormal investigator is a potentially cool idea for a Theurge. Perhaps better suited to the Uktena or maybe Silent Striders (especially if focused on ghosts), but still good. But this really isn't that. He's essentially a werewolf who hangs out with vampires. Honestly, between that and the totally lack of any mention of his Tribe in the write up, I feel like I'm reading something that should be in the Ronin chapter of WoD: Outcasts. This feels like something that started with the whole X-Files &quot;I want to believe&quot; idea (which isn't a bad idea) and quickly veered off the rails with the Vampire crossover stuff and turned into a very weak and toothless attempt at Hellblazer.<br /> I think the character freebies are largely wasted on such a high Gnosis score, especially considering how lacking his Abilities are in certain areas.<br /> So this one is just broken, both conceptually and mechanically.<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-18T16:27:42-08:00","id":1525612,"title":"","content":"OK, I've tried twice to post the next one, but it keeps getting flagged. I am quite frankly sick of this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-18T16:33:31-08:00","id":1525613,"title":"","content":"<b>Supernatural Investigator</b> (Homid Theurge)<br /> <br /> So, this guy grew up with a real fascination - obsession even - with stories about otherworldly creatures and supernatural beings. Especially movies about vampires and other creatures which implied that said beings weren't necessarily evil and could even be the good guys. (Too bad this predates the Buffy tv show; this guy would've been a super-fan of that.) Apparently his First Change happened while he was laying in bed reading by moonlight. And I thought the Bone Gnawer Hitchhiker's First Change was pretty chill. Yeesh.<br /> He started &quot;nocturnal missions&quot; out into the supernatural world to meet all the creatures he used to read about. Exactly when he was found by other Garou, did his Rite of Passage, and joined the Children of Gaia is not mentioned at all.<br /> And then things take a turn for the cringe.<br /> <br /> Apparently he met a bunch of &quot;highly moral&quot; vampires, naturally of Clan Gangrel. I am going to pretend that these vampires are Edge and Christian of the WWE (points if you get the joke there) because that will make me laugh rather than cry at this next bit. They introduced him to a bunch of other vampires, and they're totally helping him look for this legendary vampire who supposedly transcended vampirism. I guess this means Saulot, in which case all the stuff that eventually came about in Vampire's metaplot just makes that even funnier.<br /> <br /> He's also met fairies, mages, ghosts, demons and lots of other stuff. And he's decided that the ones that are selfish are Wyrm oriented, while the ones who actually care about others are for Gaia. I can't exactly fault that sort of reasoning, but I have this suspicion that non-selfish vampires are perhaps a bit scarce. Demons even more so. So the fact that this guy seems to think that a lot of vampires are A-OK and have a lot to teach the Garou makes me question his level of awareness.<br /> <br /> Yes, this entire book has this weird fixation on vampires as being an antithesis of life and Gaia while at the same time being super important because some of them can reach Golconda and that's something Garou need to learn from. And I think the main reason this character exists is because of that.<br /> <br /> Anyway, he's apparently building alliances with all of these other supernatural beings to help the Garou.<br /> <br /> ::Sigh::<br /> <br /> For equipment, he's got a cell phone, a trench coat (of course he does, but I'll get to that in a minute), a pistol, a miniature infrared camera, a pocket tape recorder, and a laptop.<br /> <br /> The image is of a guy in a trench coat with what looks like a cigarette in his mouth and his hands in his pockets. The face looks like some mash up of Fox Mulder of the X-Files and John Constantine from DC/Vertigo's Hellblazer. His eyes look rather odd, like maybe he's high or something. It's obvious that Mulder and Constantine are the primary inspirations behind this character.<br /> <br /> He's a member of the Patient Deed camp. I only know this because it's on the character sheet. There's nothing at all in the write up about it. Or even about his Tribe.<br /> <br /> For Attributes, Physicals are tertiary with 2/2/2. Socials are primary with 4/3/3. Mental is secondary with an additional dot from freebies for 3s across the board.<br /> While I realize that this guy seems to be a friendly &quot;get out there and meet people&quot; sort of person, I feel like he'd be better served with Socials and Mental being switched.<br /> <br /> For Abilities, Talents are primary, with 3 each in Empathy and Streetwise, 2 each in Alertness and Brawl, and 1 each in Intimidation, Primal Urge, and Subterfuge.<br /> Skills are tertiary, with a 2 in Firearms and 1 each in Drive, Melee, and Stealth.<br /> Knowledge is secondary with one extra dot from freebies, with a 4 in Enigmas, a 3 in Occult, and 1 each in Politics and Rituals. (And yes, he is missing a dot in Knowledges, as at least two freebies were spent on that fourth dot in Enigmas.)<br /> I will point out that we have a Supernatural Investigator who has no points in Investigation. I'd say that maybe a more proper name might be Supernatural Diplomat, but he has such low Politics and Subterfuge, and no Etiquette.<br /> <br /> Backgrounds are 3 in Allies (I presume his Gangrel buddies), and 2 in Rites. I am just going to guess he has Rites because he's a Theurge and they all have to have that just because they are Theurges.<br /> You would think that with as many different supernatural creatures this guy has met, he might at least have some Contacts. But no.<br /> <br /> Rage is 2. Gnosis is a whopping 5 (that's where the bulk of his freebies went). Willpower is 4.<br /> <br /> I really don't care for this one. It's not the alleged concept. A paranormal investigator is a potentially cool idea for a Theurge. Perhaps better suited to the Uktena or maybe Silent Striders (especially if focused on ghosts), but still good. But this really isn't that. He's essentially a werewolf who hangs out with vampires. Honestly, between that and the totally lack of any mention of his Tribe in the write up, I feel like I'm reading something that should be in the Ronin chapter of WoD: Outcasts. This feels like something that started with the whole X-Files &quot;I want to believe&quot; idea (which isn't a bad idea) and quickly veered off the rails with the Vampire crossover stuff and turned into a very weak and toothless attempt at Hellblazer.<br /> I think the character freebies are largely wasted on such a high Gnosis score, especially considering how lacking his Abilities are in certain areas.<br /> So this one is just broken, both conceptually and mechanically.<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-19T09:13:48-08:00","id":1525638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525607#post1525607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I think they work better when you focus on them as one of the Leadership Tribes of the Garou Nation (along with the Silver Fangs and Shadow Lords, and how Middle Brother was in the Pure Lands). At some point, I sort of rewrote setting history a little for my Werewolf the Dark Ages games so that the whole Silver Crown thing happened in the early 12th century, and now there is sort of a three way civil war happening in the aftermath between Falcon Banner loyalists to the Silver Fangs, the revolutionary Army of Thunder led by the Shadow Lords, and the Children of Gaia's Unicorn Crusade that is allegedly fighting for peaceful coexistence but several of its leaders are really wanting to take over the Garou Nation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, agreed.<br /> <br /> The 'weakness' that canon gives is utterly insulting. Even if Coggies Revised is an awful book in general, the way it portrays the tribe as wilting flowers who cannot deal with conflict is insulting. Nevermind that the Coggies ONLY have this loser energy in Europe. Anywhere IRL humanitarian aid goes? Coggies are apparently fine with conflict there.<br /> <br /> For me, it also doesn't allow the tribe to be dark on their own which is needed for a balanced tribal concept. Coggies are best foes when they try to do good, but in a way that is harmful. I.e. forcing a peace treaty, trying to overtake a sept through slow overtaking of positions/supporting garou souls to be reborn as Coggies/adopting and brainwashing many garou born and such.<br /> <br /> And this isn't even touching the tribal homelands and culture issues from there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-22T03:12:40-08:00","id":1525778,"title":"","content":"So, does anyone have any thoughts on the Black Furies, Bone Gnawers, or Children of Gaia they'd like to share while I am waiting for post approval? Template ideas, thoughts about Camps, artwork or characters you really liked, etc.?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-22T04:04:48-08:00","id":1525784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525778#post1525778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, does anyone have any thoughts on the Black Furies, Bone Gnawers, or Children of Gaia they'd like to share while I am waiting for post approval? Template ideas, thoughts about Camps, artwork or characters you really liked, etc.?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're all 'colorful' Tribes, so templates/characters that look like direct antitheses but somehow circle back to reflecting the Tribe in spirit (heh heh) would be nice. A gruff father of rather dated beliefs, who nevertheless genuinely loves his wife and daughters. A silver spoon who doesn't actually have much wealth to call their own, most being tied to various charities and civic infrastructure. A violent brute who breaks bodies without remorse, but only when the peace of their Sept is hurt, and spends most of their time in zen meditation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-22T06:45:17-08:00","id":1525790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525778#post1525778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, does anyone have any thoughts on the Black Furies, Bone Gnawers, or Children of Gaia they'd like to share while I am waiting for post approval? Template ideas, thoughts about Camps, artwork or characters you really liked, etc.?</div> </div> </div> </div>With my friends we used to run our games in a &quot;perfect world&quot; where septs cooperate and &quot;trade&quot; the cubs according to their needs. So we formed two &quot;perfect packs&quot;<br /> <br /> 1. A rock band<br /> <br /> As the master of improvisation Ragabash played lead guitar<br /> As &quot;the gloomy one&quot; Theurge played bass guitar<br /> As &quot;the balanced one&quot; Philodox was a drummer<br /> Gaillard played rhythm guitar<br /> And Ahroun, having biggest lungs, was on vocals<br /> <br /> 2. A fire team<br /> <br /> Ragabash - recon/stealth kill specjalist<br /> Theurge - medic<br /> Philodox - leader<br /> Gaillard - communication specialist <br /> Ahroun - heavy weapons/demolitions expert<br /> <br /> The tribes were varied (and actually I believe they could be from any tribe, maybe except Red Talons). We started it as a joke but it worked pretty well. The third idea was for &quot;furry X-men&quot; but we never tried that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-22T10:38:23-08:00","id":1525799,"title":"","content":"Antagonists templates for all three tribes;<br /> <br /> Black Furies: The Traditionalist- Many people have tried to co-opt womanhood and this Fury has had enough. A theurge or a philodox, they try to erase all the progress made by the younger generation. Seeing it all as insulting.<br /> <br /> Bone Gnawers: The Serial Killer- A ragabash sociopath who is barely a member of the Rabble, using their gifts to kill rich people are squat in their houses. Doesn't care for the Nation and has ignored most spiritual lessons entirely. Aka, doesn't know/care what the Wyrm is.<br /> <br /> Children of Gaia: The Fundamentalist- All must join the Children of Gaia. All must give up their hateful ways. This philodox spends most of their time manipulating the sept leadership to their preferred direction. Seen as weak by most, their honeyed words still shape the sept subtly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-22T11:28:30-08:00","id":1525802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525799#post1525799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Antagonists templates for all three tribes;<br /> <br /> Black Furies: The Traditionalist- Many people have tried to co-opt womanhood and this Fury has had enough. A theurge or a philodox, they try to erase all the progress made by the younger generation. Seeing it all as insulting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, but why? And how? AFAIK Most Black Furies don't want to destroy/dominate males (except maybe GoF). They'd rather see themselves as equal to men. If younger generations slowly achieve this particular template will stand against what the BF want to reach. Frankly I don't feel it. I've got an impression that you wanted to create a rich character and get an emotional roleplaying moment but I still don't see it. Maybe I missed something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525799#post1525799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bone Gnawers: The Serial Killer- A ragabash sociopath who is barely a member of the Rabble, using their gifts to kill rich people are squat in their houses. Doesn't care for the Nation and has ignored most spiritual lessons entirely. Aka, doesn't know/care what the Wyrm is.</div> </div> </div> </div>IMHO this one is better. Still I got a feeling that it's quite thin. First of all what is the modus operandi? How this character chooses its victims and why? I would rather see it as a Robin Hood like character who first give the resources of the victims to the poor but slowly gets addicted to the money. Plus if you throw away its knowledge about the Wyrm you will propably get a newly changed cub and not a Bone Gnawer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525799#post1525799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Children of Gaia: The Fundamentalist- All must join the Children of Gaia. All must give up their hateful ways. This philodox spends most of their time manipulating the sept leadership to their preferred direction. Seen as weak by most, their honeyed words still shape the sept subtly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this one is the best. There's only one question: how far it could go to achieve what it wants.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-22T21:53:29-08:00","id":1525822,"title":"","content":"I also used CoG who, being a mediocre warrior, chose to fight another way. She looked for songs about environment or human rights and sold mixtapes with them. Anyone who remember Serial Killer from &quot;Hackers&quot; will know what I'm talking about. For an additional fee she could also make those tapes using particular genre (her metal/punk compilations were very popular around Gets). And she sent the money she earned that way to Greenpeace, WWF and Amnesty International. We had a very much fun replaying her trial (something like Metallica vs. Napster).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-22T22:18:55-08:00","id":1525823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <d