er":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-23T08:57:07-08:00","id":1525843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525830#post1525830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm still seeing my posts as unapproved; Are you able to see them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was last night, but it doesn't show up to me as of this post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-23T11:31:25-08:00","id":1525855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525831#post1525831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I am personally agnostic on the issue, I would deeply appreciate not having this usually very heated discussion in the thread while already having difficulties with the board algorithms. Thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny thing. People could be offended (or are protected from being offended) by a fictional character. Looks like Mizuki's Children of Gaia is alive <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-23T12:48:54-08:00","id":1525859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525778#post1525778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, does anyone have any thoughts on the Black Furies, Bone Gnawers, or Children of Gaia they'd like to share while I am waiting for post approval? Template ideas, thoughts about Camps, artwork or characters you really liked, etc.?</div> </div> </div> </div>Black Furies: Love the idea of the Tribe. Looking at gender through a mystical, primordial lens and taking inspiration from ancient practices is a great concept. I love the idea of the Tribe and what it stands for. On the other hand, the moment you try to bring it into present-day inevitably people will start talking about present-day-perspectives on gender (and maybe even start arguing about it). But historically gender is just such a more expansive subject, just reducing it to present-day-culture-wars takes away from an all-female-Tribe that's been there for millennia. Instead of expanding horizons on what gender means by looking at history and mysticism, things are just gonna trapped in the minutiae of present-day-debates. Great Tribe for when you know the people who sit at your table, bad Tribe for sidetracking things because gender is certainly quite the discussion topic. But I think the damage is done. Hell, we know that they killed the &quot;all-female&quot;-thing in W5 because one of the developers thought of the BF as &quot;the feminist Tribe&quot;. Just sad that what the Tribe is and could be developed into often really just gets reduced to &quot;the Feminist Tribe&quot;. Gender is a fascinating subject from a historical perspective especially since the WtA-framework allows for quite the grand landscape of various ideas/concepts over the millennia.<br /> <br /> Bone Gnawers: The focus for that Tribe shouldn't be pseudo-Nosferatu of the Garou-Nation focused on information-gathering but adaptability and survival. They are the Tribe who manages and organizes Garou-presences in the unlikeliest places you'd expect. Where the Glass Walkers manage to survive in the city because they're getting close to the Weaver, Bone Gnawers are all about surviving despite the odds. The places where no Garou wants to be, the struggles that won't earn you Renown as Garou conceive it and the battles that don't directly fight the Wyrm but indirectly do - that's where the Bone Gnawers are. They mingle, they adapt and they survive.<br /> <br /> Children of Gaia: I don't like the idea of reducing them to &quot;peace-loving hippies&quot;. Rather than human references, the focus should be on what they represent in the Garou-Nation. The way I portrayed them in my games is that this is the Tribe that has no traditions - but beliefs instead. And they preach those beliefs. It's a Tribe more concerned with &quot;mindset&quot; than &quot;legacy&quot; when it comes to its members. They are the Tribe about what other Tribes think and/or do. Not just in the sense of approve/disapprove but they actively try to influence things. Whereas the Silver Fangs are all just arrogant assholes \u00e0 la &quot;nobless oblige&quot;, the Children of Gaia have a vision of what the Garou-Nation should be like (with Children of Gaia hardliners saying it <i>has to be</i> like that) and they're gonna make sure it turns into that. They say they don't want to be in charge but they have a lot of... opinions about who should do what and when in a Sept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-23T17:32:21-08:00","id":1525869,"title":"","content":"I will mention that when it comes to Children of Gaia Ahroun, my biggest influence in how I view them come from two bits that Larry Hama wrote for Marvel's GI Joe comic in the 80s. One was the Arashikage ninja clan's philosophy that the only rational reason for mastering violence was to abolish it (effectively in one's life and heart, with the idea that once enough people have achieved that, it will carry over into society at large). The other was Snake-Eyes' description of Storm Shadow as a tightly wound killing machine who desperately needs the discipline of martial arts to keep his own worst impulses in check. <br /> If you had asked me to do templates for the revised CoG book, the Ahroun would have been a Homid who has spent much of their pre-Change life training in Akido and other arts as a means to keep their latent Rage under control and continue to use it for that purpose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-24T12:59:03-08:00","id":1525884,"title":"","content":"And the Theurge now seems to be visible, on the preceding page.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-24T17:38:58-08:00","id":1525893,"title":"","content":"I actually like this Template a lot more than you. It's probably my favorite of the CoG templates. But it is crossover heavy and can lead to a lot of eye rolling. It's also a bit too hard on the nose and would have benefitted from less direct involvement with other games. But crossover was a good thing to be pursued during this time period of the WoD and not something that was frowned upon. So some adjustments would need to be done if translating this to newer versions that have a different outlook on this like moral vampires, Golconda, potential relations between Garou and vampires, etc. Despite that I think the core concept is OK. The character sheet is relatively OK except for the obvious mistakes these templates always make (why does a Supernmatural Investigator have zero points in Investigation?). The flavor text needs updating to whatever is appropriate for that player's chronicle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525613#post1525613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's a member of the Patient Deed camp. I only know this because it's on the character sheet. There's nothing at all in the write up about it. Or even about his Tribe.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a major problem for all templates in this tribebook. Very little explanation for a character's inclusion in the camp. You can often tease out an explanation why, but this is something that should be stated outright.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525613#post1525613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And then things take a turn for the cringe.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of what is written in the Template should be the description of this character after many, many years of investigation. It's not one of a brand new Cliath on the start of his path. And I think that's a major problem of it. Way too much is frontloaded for a Cliath. As an established PC or NPC of many years, he might have had this level of success.<br /> <br /> It would have been better for the template to explain he's encountered more typical Wyrm tainted vampires as well, but he met one highly moral vampire and learned there is a vampire myth about restoring one's humanity or even mortality. And he decided to help his new friend and in the process learned there are more vampires like her as well. If he can confirm it is true that vampires can be redeemed, then it may be possible to expand that knowledge to other Wyrm creatures, and that would result in a major victory for Gaia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525613#post1525613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the fact that this guy seems to think that a lot of vampires are A-OK and have a lot to teach the Garou makes me question his level of awareness.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>One possible explanation is by the text saying &quot;highly moral vampires of Clan Gangrel&quot; is that Gangrel are less likely to detect as the Wyrm. Gangrel are supposed to be only detected as if they had three higher Humanity (I think) than what they actually have. Can't remember where that rule originated though. I think it may be scattered in several books. So that would make one think the Gangrel are much more morally superior than they are. A lot of White Wolf writers would write in-character text in a way that one must read it critically. So it is had at times to determine if something is bad writing or revealing a lack of knowledge by a character.<br /> <br /> It would be better if there was some sentence of him destroying a Wyrm ridden vampire so that the text acknowledges that the character is aware of the danger they represent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525613#post1525613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, he's apparently building alliances with all of these other supernatural beings to help the Garou.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>While the most wording is spent on vampires, I think his explorations with other supernatural creatures are actually the heart of this character. He'd be much more successful working with mages, faeries, even ghosts, and unusual spirits than vampires. But again, this is really something that this starting character could work towards, not have it be a starting point.<br /> <br /> If I was an ST this is where I'd actually concentrate for the character. I'd allow him to know <i>one</i> vampire as part of his background (maybe something like the Babe in the Woods or Lupine Impersonator in the Gangrel clanbook templates) and have a few leads on other kinds of creatures he could begin to encounter (information on a haunted house, a wise wilderness hermit of either the Dreamspeaker or Verbena traditions that is not obviously magical, a Stag spirit that knows where some faeries are located).<br /> <br /> However, as a crossover heavy character concept, a lot is going to depend on how much lore the ST has of the other gamelines and how much effort the ST wants to expend on that. Given five different STs, this concept will have five very different experiences. Some STs will basically sandbag this kind of character because she does not want to spend the time and effort to master the lore of the other game lines (or create her own as replacement), and that is an acceptable decision for the ST.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525613#post1525613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't care for this one. It's not the alleged concept. A paranormal investigator is a potentially cool idea for a Theurge. Perhaps better suited to the Uktena or maybe Silent Striders (especially if focused on ghosts), but still good. But this really isn't that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the difference is that the character wants to not just investigate the paranormal (like those other tribes would), but sees the possibility of redemption and alliance to serve Gaia. So your comment on &quot;diplomat&quot; is correct. But that (and the Abilities needed for it) can be something for the character to grow into.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525613#post1525613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's essentially a werewolf who hangs out with vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>This may be our biggest point of contention because I see the template as being much more than this, but I understand why you might think that given how much wording is given over to vampires compared to other creatures. I think that may be because at this point in time, a lot more Vampire material had been published than any other game line. I don't think Changeling was even published yet, Wraith had just been published and lacked additional sourcebooks, and Mage only had a few books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525613#post1525613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So this one is just broken, both conceptually and mechanically.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> The bad character sheet mechanics is unfortunately typical. By all means criticize, but I try to divorce the bad character sheet (which will often need to be redone regardless of concept, but some more than others) from the actual template concept.<br /> <br /> I know you say the core concept is OK so I think the real issue is the actual character description in the template which I agree needs a much better rewrite. Despite that I come away a lot more positive than you despite sharing most of your complaints.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-24T18:24:37-08:00","id":1525894,"title":"","content":"To clarify, I think this starts as a potentially good idea, but quickly seems to lose the plot. I think the two biggest problems with the write up are,<br /> one: that it goes directly from first change to hanging out with vampires, with nothing in between about adjusting to the world of Werewolf, joining a Tribe, or the rest; and<br /> two: it spends so much time talking not just about vampires, but about Vampire the Masquerade. <br /> I think if it had spent that paragraph about Gangrel talking about why he was a Child of Gaia and then the following one saying that he had managed to have peaceful and even productive encounters with faeries, witches, immortals, and even a vampire that did not appear to be Wyrm-tainted (who told him the legend about a possible redemption/cure), then this would be a very solid character that was let down by a poor set of traits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-24T18:33:33-08:00","id":1525895,"title":"","content":"Also, not the last character that ended up looking like Fox Mulder; one of the sample characters of Project Twilight is basically just someone telling the artist, &quot;Draw Agent Mulder from the X-Files. Yes, really.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-25T13:01:44-08:00","id":1525918,"title":"","content":"<b>Anodyne</b> (Metis Philodox)<br /> <br /> So, anodyne is an archaic term for painkillers, as well as a synonym for inoffensive. (Also, oddly, the name of the Stargazer signature character who first appeared in Rage Across New York, which was also written by Daniel Greenberg. I guess he just really likes that word for some reason.) Apparently this concept is supposed to evoke both meanings, as both a healer and as someone who tries to work as a mediator by not giving any offense to others. Which isn't all that bad of an idea. <br /> <br /> Their parents tried to drown them after they were born, but they were saved and given to the Children of Gaia. The tribe is the only family they've ever known, and they claim not to care who their real parents were. If that's true, they're remarkably well adjusted. <br /> They showed &quot;special gifts&quot; and are marked by the Tribal Totem. There really is no further development of the former and the latter is their Metis deformity, Unicorn Horn. And that's about as much as we get about that. But they are a skilled healer, both physically as well as emotionally/spiritually. <br /> <br /> They try to act as a bridge between various forces and factions. As a Philodox, between passion and wisdom; as a Child of Gaia, between the tribes; and as a Metis between Homid and Lupus. The first two I can get behind. The third is maybe a little iffy, but I can understand the idea of having an outsider's perspective who isn't attached to either species. <br /> <br /> The roleplaying hints describe them as being confident and authoritative, which is an interesting change from how Metis are typically presented. They also try to lead and teach by example, and aren't just all talk in their ideals. <br /> <br /> As mentioned, the Metis deformity is Unicorn Horn. I honestly never really cared that much for this particular deformity, which was first presented in this book. I sort of feel like it was invented entirely for this character and is sort of a &quot;I'm special&quot; cop out for the usual breed weakness. The write up doesn't even mention any mechanics about how it impacts the character. Among other things, you'd at least think it was a major potential Veil breach. <br /> <br /> Equipment is a walking staff, bandages, and a first aid kit. <br /> <br /> The image appears to be human female, but as a certain androgynous quality to it that could be interpreted as gender fluid or some other non-binary. They are exceedingly thin and lithe. They appear to be wearing the bandages mentions in the equipment. Also a heck of a lot of jewelry. They almost look like they belong in a sword &amp; sorcery/sword &amp; sandals fantasy story. Plus the very blatant horn growing out of their forehead. It's not a bad image, even if the horn is kind of distracting. But like I said, it looks like they belong in a fantasy game rather than a modern &quot;urban fantasy&quot; horror game. Unless maybe they're part of some sort of weird isolated New Age cult. <br /> <br /> They're listed as part of the Demeter's Daughters Camp. They're basically focused on trying to restore humanity's connection to the natural world. It fits the character more or less, but I wish the write up had worked this in somewhere. <br /> <br /> For Attributes, Physicals are secondary with one extra dot from freebies, for 2/3/4. Socials are tertiary and all at 2. Mental is primary with 3/4/3.<br /> I'm having a hard time making sense of this. The character is written as a healers and diplomat, someone who tries to build bridges between disparate factions. And yet their Social traits are all at 2. I feel like Socials should be secondary or primary, perhaps at 3/3/2 or 4/4/2. Physical should probably be tertiary here. <br /> <br /> For Abilities, Talents are primary with one extra dot from freebies. Brawl (?!), Empathy, and Primal Urge are 3 each. Alertness is 2, and then 1 each in Athletics, Dodge, and Intimidation. <br /> Skills are tertiary, with 2 each in Melee and Leadership, and 1 in Survival. <br /> Knowledge is secondary, with 3 each in Enigmas and Rituals, 2 in Medicine, and 1 in Law.<br /> These feel really wonky. The high level of Brawl especially. There's nothing in the write up to really explain this. The Medicine knowledge also feels slightly low given what a focus they have on healing. And as a bridge builder, nothing in Politics. <br /> <br /> Backgrounds are 2 in Mentor and 3 in Past Life. It's nice to see something other than Allies or Contacts after so long. I feel like this is a character that could benefit from a Fetish, especially something that would hide that horn from humans.<br /> <br /> Rage is 3, Gnosis is 3, and Willpower is 5. <br /> <br /> Seven freebies were spent on an extra Gift, which I don't think is really necessary. I think those points would be better spent on Abilities or Backgrounds. <br /> <br /> This is an interesting character. I don't exactly love it, but it seems a fairly solid and original idea. However, the character sheet is questionable in several areas. And I find the breed deformity kind of odd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-25T13:54:51-08:00","id":1525927,"title":"","content":"This concept is half-way there to an interesting one, I think. Being a Metis and then having a peculiar deformity like a Unicorn horn while being in the CoG-Tribe. Being peaceful and focused on healing while also being willing to act violently. Being scorned by Garou-society, let alone being the offspring of Garou-parents who tried to kill them. The concept revolving around the character being an anodyne for others. There's a lot of stuff to work with here.<br /> <br /> The character-sheet gave me a bit of a whiplash. I certainly didn't picture that sort of char-sheet while reading the description. The Backgrounds aren't explained at all, for example.<br /> <br /> I think the aspect I would hone in on far more is the deformity. A Metis with a Unicorn-horn in the CoG and what this exactly means is an interesting idea. Is the Metis truly blessed by the Unicorn? Does the Unicorn expect this character to do something?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-25T14:42:03-08:00","id":1525934,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the write up for the deformity in the tribebook gives absolutely no mechanics about how it works. Can it be used as a weapon? How do humans or wolves react to it? What happens if it breaks? Do spirits - especially Unicorn's brood - react to it in any way? Does it improve Social interactions with Children of Gaia? Does it glow when you use Gifts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-26T00:04:26-08:00","id":1525955,"title":"","content":"This is a fairly &quot;meh&quot; template, but the character has grown on me over the years.<br /> <br /> Outside of the Metis deformity, I think the template is OK, but uninteresting. The character is all about healing - appropriate for a Unicorn based character. She has the Gift of Mother's Touch, and appropriate ranks in Medicine (for physical healing) and Empathy (for psychological healing). I don't know how interesting this would be for a PC, but as an NPC it is perfectly viable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525918#post1525918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Also, oddly, the name of the Stargazer signature character who first appeared in Rage Across New York, which was also written by Daniel Greenberg. I guess he just really likes that word for some reason.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not sure what you mean by this. The only Stargazer in Rage Across New York is Antonine Teardrop. Antonine is not the same as Anodyne, but there are similarities in its sound. I think you are misremembering here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525918#post1525918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their parents tried to drown them after they were born, but they were saved and given to the Children of Gaia.</div> </div> </div> </div>As the Metis deformity is a &quot;unicorn horn&quot;, the most likely reason is that at least one parent is in fact a Child of Gaia. While it is not impossible (given ST interpretation) that a Metis born from a different tribe would have a deformity that illustrates so much from a singular tribe, my instincts is that such &quot;tells&quot; should reflect a tribal origin. If I were the ST, I would make at least one parent (likely the mother) be from CoG who saved her daughter from the father's wrath/despair. The mother, in fact, would be the character's Mentor. But the child would not know she is her mother, in a similar way that some children know their mother as their &quot;older sister&quot; when their mom was a teen mother whose parents wanted to protect their daughter from the stigma and burden of an only mother while providing for their grandchild. I'd leave it to the player to figure it out for themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525918#post1525918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The roleplaying hints describe them as being confident and authoritative, which is an interesting change from how Metis are typically presented.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one aspect that really interests me. A confidant, decisive Metis is not expected, but I think the concept sells it. She would be an interesting character is handled properly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525918#post1525918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The write up doesn't even mention any mechanics about how it impacts the character. Among other things, you'd at least think it was a major potential Veil breach.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the one issue that really bothers me. As depicted in the art, this is a very big issue in regards to the Veil so it must be addressed. Does the character try to avoid any interaction with the outside world other than Garou society and targeted missions? Should we assume the art does not truthfully depicted the horn accurately, and that it is much smaller and can be hidden by appropriate clothing? Or that the horn has been cut off so that it can be so hidden (and perhaps taking a Renown hit)? There may be other options, but whatever tract is chosen, the template should address it.<br /> <br /> This would be important for the character, and by ignoring this obvious issue, the template description is a big disservice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525918#post1525918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is an interesting character. I don't exactly love it, but it seems a fairly solid and original idea. However, the character sheet is questionable in several areas</div> </div> </div> </div>When I first saw the template so long ago, I disliked it intently. But it has since grown on me as I've seen the potential and came up with reasons to excuse or deal with its obvious faults.<br /> <br /> Unicorn as healer is an obvious hook given the legendry ties between a unicorn's horn and its healing properties, and that is what this template is about. The unicorn horn is an emblem of healing, and therefore lots about this character fits. But it is insufficiently developed or explained.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-26T05:43:09-08:00","id":1525959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525611#post1525611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am going to pretend that these vampires are Edge and Christian of the WWE (points if you get the joke there) because that will make me laugh rather than cry at this next bit.<br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. And, as Edge returned to WWE some time ago (sadly, he left when his contract expired) he should have embraced one of young wrestler as his succesor. Maybe this will also bring El Diablo Verde out of the shadows of XWF. Kudos to you if you get the joke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-26T08:28:19-08:00","id":1525962,"title":"","content":"The horn deformity is most likely same as the horns deformity.<br /> <br /> I admit I've had some wild mixes of deformities over the years to fit a theme. But yeah, the horn IS a pretty big breach of the veil.<br /> <br /> And I'm am more and more certain the WRITING team is not talking to the statting team, either. This character is socials first if there ever was one.<br /> <br /> I've played similar characters and I honestly feel this could have been done better in the sheet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-27T12:58:15-08:00","id":1526016,"title":"","content":"It seems like delayed posts have been able to go through but I figured I\u2019d still share some ideas I\u2019ve got floating around re the tribes covered so far, maybe it\u2019ll be helpful for some folks.<br /> <br /> \u2022Black Furies: I covered a good chunk of my thoughts on them and interesting ways they could be used earlier in this thread. To sum things up briefly I think that the idea of them being avengers for violations of primordial and ancient laws is a solid avenue as well as the idea of them representing schools of thought and mysticism which were more active prior to what might be deemed the usurpation of the patriarch, a motif that may be particularly useful because a bunch of irl occultists and anthropologist types alike have written a lot on that notion so there\u2019s plenty of inspirational material out there.<br /> <br /> \u2022Bone Gnawers: I think one can use the Bone Gnawers in a lot of ways. As the tribe of outcasts they can be used to represent everything from the weakest links culled by other tribes or proto-tribes who were destroyed before they could fully metastasize; perhaps you could flesh this angle out to have them also take on a dispossession theme to add to their rivalry with the Silent Striders. I agree with others who have said that the urban Gnawers are over-represented in tribal material and that the rural and itinerant (Bone Gnawer circuses?) sections of the tribe need more coverage. I do like the idea that the Bone Gnawers represent the largest tribe of Gaian Garou in the Final Nights, although the ranks of the Rabble make up a sizable chunk of that. A lot of Gnawers probably do live as Ghost Wolves, struggling to carve out chunks of privacy to live their own lives, away from the Nation. Rat I think would go along with those who choose to go that route, just as much as those who do stick around to fight. I\u2019ve always liked the image of the Bone Gnawers as the Nation\u2019s equivalent of the down-trodden and cynical plebs/peasants. Rallying young high-tribe Garou to flock to the war banner has always been relatively easy (it\u2019s usually harder to let their tribal/Sept elders sign off on it), but rallying the large numbers of Bone Gnawers is relatively difficult. A lot of them don\u2019t see any reason to join your own struggle without a good reason - even the active Warriors of the tribe have their own goals that they\u2019d rather pursue. The age-old bargain is to offer the Gnawers territory, resources, patronage, protection, etc. in exchange for service - but they\u2019ve been short-changed before and hard to persuade. As the Final Nights go on, fewer and fewer of Rat\u2019s Children answer the war calls of even the most lucrative war packs. As a patron Rat is all about Survival - Rat is also a little crazy but what\u2019s that between friends. Bone Gnawers often have their hands full dealing with the local Ratkin problems and the other scavenger and down-low types that go over-looked by other Garou. Something ironic about the Bone Gnawers is that they\u2019re probably the most likely Garou to become involved in dealing with something causing problems for the average person - the Sept might not care about the fomor-run tainted gas station but the Gnawers who live nearby might. I think that Ragabadh is meant to be an archetypal Bone Gnawer auspice so I imagine all types of BG jokesters, clowns, trouble-shooters, investigators, etc. BG Theurges - Urban Shamans, Country Witch-Doctors, Dirtbag Pill Mixer (their batch will blow your mind right open). BG Philodox - Beleaguered parents/elders/siblings, community leader types, friendly deputies, itinerant folk judge. BG Galliard a Underground musician, newspaper/magazine hoarding info guru, folk preacher. BG Ahroun - Vigilante, Junkyard Dog, Enforcer, bounty hunter, etc.<br /> <br /> \u2022Children of Gaia: I\u2019m fond of a lot of the additions and flourishes which Black Fox and No One of Consequence has added to this tribe. The idea of the tribe being concerned with protecting a universal purity and being guardians with a universal-ifying ideal clicked for me. I like the stuff with them being a competing leadership tribe. That said I do think there should still be a place for the hippies, the human-whisperers, and the moon-eyed mystics amongst them but those can all probably be camps or traditions amongst a variety of camps and traditions. I can easily imagine an interesting dynamic with competing camps who interpret Unicorn\u2019s call for purity as a policing mandate which covers all Garou (perhaps all Gaians/life in general\u2026) on one extreme and full new-age libertarian style camps on the other extreme calling for a peaceful reconciliation of all life back within the universal communion of the Mother. White Wolf tended to associate the Children of Gaia with hippies and new age stuff but tbh I do think interesting stuff could be done by fleshing out potential ties they may have with Christianity and Islam (as well as other sorts of universalist confessional type systems). I think the image of the Coggie peace keeper has been around for so long that I don\u2019t want to lose it entirely from Werewolf but it would be nice to flesh out other interpretations Garou could come up for to match Unicorn\u2019s mandate of Purity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T17:36:05-08:00","id":1526094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525955#post1525955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not sure what you mean by this. The only Stargazer in Rage Across New York is Antonine Teardrop. Antonine is not the same as Anodyne, but there are similarities in its sound. I think you are misremembering here.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, it's worse than that. I actually went and looked it up while writing the post, and even reading it here and now, my brain keeps trying to insist that his name is Anodyne. I can't figure it out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1525962#post1525962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I'm am more and more certain the WRITING team is not talking to the statting team, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> It will almost always being the same person writing both the write up and the character sheet. The only exception I've ever been aware of is when the revised Vampire and Mage books included MET/LARP character sheets, where some of the writers weren't familiar with MET rules and so someone who worked on MET did the conversions for those.<br /> <br /> However, someone (I want to say from layout or editing) has to covert the written text into a character sheet image. So it's always possible there may be errors in the conversion process or in the final making of the image.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1526016#post1526016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Bone Gnawer circuses?)\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>It occurs to me that you could do an interesting Bone Gnawer Metis background of being raised by Kinfolk among one of those small boardwalk carnivals as part of their exhibition of natural oddities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1526016#post1526016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">White Wolf tended to associate the Children of Gaia with hippies and new age stuff but tbh I do think interesting stuff could be done by fleshing out potential ties they may have with Christianity and Islam (as well as other sorts of universalist confessional type systems).</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> I'm honestly kind of surprised that more wasn't written about the Children of Gaia and the Bah\u00e1'\u00ed faith. The original tribe book has a number of potentially interesting historical seeds involving Sufism, Hinduism, and certain Chinese ethical philosophies (Mohism seems especially fitting), but sadly they've never really been followed up on very much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-01T16:57:57-08:00","id":1526214,"title":"","content":"<b>Umbral Traveler </b>(Homid Galliard)<br /> <br /> Born to prominent Kinfolk and prophesied for greatness, with an innate spirituality even as a child. During their Rite of Passage, they apparently fell into the Umbra, encountered an avatar of Unicorn, and was taken to the Children of Gaia tribal homeland realm. <br /> Now they search the Umbral (perhaps obsessively), looking for tales, stories, and interesting encounters to share with other Garou in hopes of providing inspiration, hope, and unity. They're very earnest and honest, aware of the potential dangers of the Umbra but their optimism (and possibly obsession) overrides any sense of fear. <br /> <br /> Equipment is an Uzi, a flak jacket, flash light, grappling hook, stun gun, rappelling equipment, and a Fetish, a Memory Ribbon from the Atrocity Realm (it prevents possession and raises the difficulty of all frenzies by two). It's a fairly interesting fetish, originally appearing in Umbra: The Velvet Shadow. Although it might be more useful to one of the other characters (the Supernatural Investigator or Anodyne perhaps). I'm a little torn on the rest of the equipment. For some reason, I've never exactly viewed Garou as needing to outfit for a major expedition when going into the Umbra. The Uzi seems especially odd. But maybe I'm wrong.<br /> <br /> The image is of a somewhat young and androgynous looking individual with an Uzi and a really bulky jacket. You can see the flashlight as well, and a backpack with bedroll. They seem vaguely Native American. Overall, not a bad image. But I'm not really sure how well it gets across the idea of someone who is eagerly scouring the Umbra for sources of hope and inspiration. I think you could almost swap this out with the image of the Philodox missionary in Black Furies and no one would really bat an eye. <br /> <br /> The character is a member of the Servants of the Unicorn camp. Which is to say that they're just a regular run of the mill Child of Gaia, because that's all that &quot;camp&quot; is: Tribe members who aren't part of any of the other Camps. Which is honestly a terrible idea for a &quot;camp&quot;. <br /> <br /> For Attributes, Physicals are tertiary, all at 2. Socials are primary, with 3/4/3. Mental is secondary with 3/2/3. <br /> These aren't really bad, but it sort of feels like this character should have slightly better physicals, at least with Stamina. Also they feel more like a Charisma type character than a Manipulation one. <br /> <br /> For Abilities, Talents are secondary with three extra dots from freebies. Alertness and Empathy are 3 each. Brawl and Primal Urge are both 2, and Dodge and Expression are 1s. <br /> Skills are primary, with 3 each in Etiquette, Leadership, and Performance, and 2 each in Stealth and Survival. <br /> Knowledge is tertiary with two extra dots from freebies, with 3 in Enigmas, 2 in Rituals, and 1 each in Investigation and Occult. <br /> I find these a little wonky. We again see Galliards defaulting to Performance, and in the case of this character, I feel Expression would be a lot more fitting for what they do. Athletics would also be useful for their travel and exploration. I'll also point out that even though the character has an Uzi in their equipment list and image, they've no Firearms skill. <br /> <br /> Backgrounds are a 4 in Fetish (for the Memory Ribbon) and a 1 in Past Life. This is odd. Like I mentioned, while I like the Fetish, I'm not really sure this character needs it. And given how they're the offspring of prominent Kinfolk and prophesied for greatness, you would expect them to have some amount of Pure Breed, and perhaps Kinfolk as well. <br /> <br /> Rage is the default 4, Gnosis has been boosted to 3, and Rage to 5. <br /> <br /> Generally speaking, I like this character. It's a good concept, and I especially like the idea of a Galliard whose focus is finding things to inspire and help others (and also not having anything to do with music). However, this seems to fall into the same issue of the others of having a weak character sheet that could use some work. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-01T18:04:00-08:00","id":1526216,"title":"","content":"An uzi, with no Firearms. Their deed name is doubtlessly Spray-and-Pray.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-01T18:07:58-08:00","id":1526217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1526216#post1526216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An uzi, with no Firearms. Their deed name is doubtlessly Spray-and-Pray.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just hope they have a packmate who has enough dots in Firearms to be able to reload, clean, and if necessary unjam it for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-01T19:06:21-08:00","id":1526218,"title":"","content":"The idea is sound, but I don't think the character description really sold it. I think my main problem is what kind of stories is this character collecting and telling? Is this just something that won't truly be explored? Is the ST expected to provide some details and backgrounds of these stories? Is the player up to the challenge at creating these stories and getting ST approval?<br /> <br /> If the player wants to put in a lot of this effort and use their interest in folk tales and myth or just plain creative writing, this could be a very strong character. Otherwise it puts a lot of burden on the ST to come up with interesting and relevant stories, and in my experience the ST has better things to do than set aside that amount of prep time to help out one PC. And if a certain amount of effort is not put into this concept, then it just becomes the PC asking the ST if she can roll Performance in order to inspire other Garou or convince them or whatever. It just becomes an entertainer with a different flavor which would be disappointing.<br /> <br /> There also seems to be a couple of concepts mixed together. Umbral traveler, story collector, and chosen one are all different things. It's not bad to combine different aspects and create something more interesting, but this seems more like random stuff cobbled together than a solid blending of all of them.<br /> <br /> I want to like this, but it just feels flat to me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1526214#post1526214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The character is a member of the Servants of the Unicorn camp. Which is to say that they're just a regular run of the mill Child of Gaia, because that's all that &quot;camp&quot; is: Tribe members who aren't part of any of the other Camps. Which is honestly a terrible idea for a &quot;camp&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to the tribebook description, the Servants of the Unicorns are the mediators between the other tribes who attempt to heal old grudges and bring the tribes together. So the camp does have a mission. Of course you may think that is the default of the Children of Gaia anyway. They do make up the majority of the tribe and therefore are the default, but they technically do have a mission other than be themselves.<br /> <br /> Like always, the character sheet doesn't reflect the character description well as you mentioned. It's just a big problem with all the templates in multiple game lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-01T20:44:48-08:00","id":1526222,"title":"","content":"Yeah, my description of the character is fairly brief because a lot of what is there (especially in the first paragraph) tends towards the fluff side of things. I think this is a really good core of an idea, but would certainly benefit from some stronger focus on the reason for them going into the Umbra, and some fleshing out of what they are trying to bring back. If I were trying to rewrite it, I would probably cut about two-thirds of the equipment and use that word count to explain their mission more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-02T04:23:16-08:00","id":1526224,"title":"","content":"Another one of the &quot;How to slot this into a pack&quot; characters. This character is very much a solo type and sadly I have never seen a game set in the umbra over the physical.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-02T10:48:48-08:00","id":1526236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1526224#post1526224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another one of the &quot;How to slot this into a pack&quot; characters. This character is very much a solo type and sadly I have never seen a game set in the umbra over the physical.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. Even skimming through the other 1st ed tribe books, I could really only find two others - the Fianna Theurge and Uktena Ahroun - that I could really see this character forming an umbral exploration focused pack with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-02T11:55:31-08:00","id":1526242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1526224#post1526224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">sadly I have never seen a game set in the umbra over the physical.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is just a lot easier to run a game set in the physical world because everyone understands how it works. In order to run the umbra, an ST really needs to concentrate and figure out a lot of things. Even though the corebook and the Umbra sourcebooks have a lot of information, it still takes a lot of effort to figure out how to RUN a game set there. It's one to read about Moon Bridges and Moon Paths and Domains and the various Umbral Realms, but there's a lot of stuff that still needs detailing - how should the transition from Penumbra to a Domain be portrayed, when should spirits be encountered and how many, what kind of airts and spirit pathways should be around.<br /> <br /> Not to mention the concepts in the Umbra are so expansive at some point it just makes it more intimidating. Running things in the Penumbra is very different than an expedition to a Near Realm or entering the Dream Zone.<br /> <br /> It can be intimidating if an ST wants to get it &quot;right&quot; or do it justice. And for those STs that don't care, the umbra is just a shortcut for players entering and leaving the physical world, or at best a location for a specific plot point that the ST can railroad the players to and fro.<br /> <br /> It's a lot of work as the ST has to create an entire new setting.<br /> <br /> It's unfortunate that none of the Rage sourcebooks ever decided to include some descriptions of the local Penumbra, Domains, etc. It would have gone a long way to show players how these concepts are supposed to be done in play.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-03T16:12:44-08:00","id":1526301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1526242#post1526242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not to mention the concepts in the Umbra are so expansive at some point it just makes it more intimidating. Running things in the Penumbra is very different than an expedition to a Near Realm or entering the Dream Zone.</div> </div> </div> </div>In hindsight, I lament that Umbra revised didn't have a ST chapter that was at least twice as large and included sections about running each realm/region and how they differ.<br /> <br /> Also perhaps mildly surprised that no one has tried making guides to the individual realms as a STV project.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-03T23:52:24-08:00","id":1526311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1526301#post1526301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In hindsight, I lament that Umbra revised didn't have a ST chapter that was at least twice as large and included sections about running each realm/region and how they differ.<br /> <br /> Also perhaps mildly surprised that no one has tried making guides to the individual realms as a STV project.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Umbra 20th does all that. But Umbra Revised had even MORE on the realms than 20 version from what I recall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-05T17:21:58-08:00","id":1526380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1526242#post1526242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's unfortunate that none of the Rage sourcebooks ever decided to include some descriptions of the local Penumbra, Domains, etc. It would have gone a long way to show players how these concepts are supposed to be done in play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rage Accross Egypt had all that. It was probably the best Rage Across book they ever made. Sadly we got no more.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-08T16:54:37-08:00","id":1526538,"title":"","content":"<b>Spirit Warrior</b> (Homid Ahroun)<br /> <br /> So, this character's father was a great Child of Gaia Kinfolk who worked in poverty stricken areas of a despairing city. Doing what exactly is not said. I feel like this should be at least mildly important. Was the father an inner city preacher? A lawyer doing pro bono work for those in need? A doctor running a clinic? He was murdered by &quot;Wyrm forces&quot;. Again, this is really vague, and feels like it should be important enough to be detailed. Murdered by corrupt land developers? A junkie desperate for money? Vampires? <br /> Anyway, this shattered the character's sense of security and safety. Suddenly the world became a much darker and more frightening place, one full of drive by shootings, domestic abuse, and foreign wars. The only way to stop the violence seemed to be with more violence. So they prayed for Gaia for power, and she answered with the First Change. They killed a gang that had been rampaging through the neighborhood &quot;as an offering to Gaia&quot; and was then found by the tribe. <br /> <br /> They are still haunted by their father's assassination and tend to fixate on protecting those they view as innocent and helpless. Those tribes who don't &quot;accept the love of Gaia and worth of humanity&quot; need to be gotten rid of. <br /> <br /> Roleplaying hints are to rage against injustice and create the peace fo Gaia by any means necessary, including the elimination of political opponents. &quot;Kill for Peace. Peace through War.&quot; The ends justify the means (apparently no matter how many people they have to murder). <br /> <br /> Equipment is a pistol, knife, motorcycle, leather jacket, knives (I guess one just isn't enough when you are killing for peace), handcuffs, and a crowbar. <br /> <br /> The image is almost generic Glabro form. Massively muscled, fangs, snarling face, wearing just what seems to be a tank top and athletic shorts, with two of those peaceful knives. I presume the image is meant to be male, but given it is Glabro, one could interpret it as a fairly athletic female. It's also kind of impossible to tell race or ethnicity, but it could be interpreted as African American or Hispanic. <br /> <br /> The character is part of the Imminent Strike camp. Which much like the Patient Deed is less a camp than a political stance. Given how extreme the character is, I'm kind of surprised they aren't part of the One Tree. <br /> <br /> For Attributes, Physicals are primary with one extra dot from freebies, for a 4/4/3 spread. Socials are tertiary with 3/1/2. Mental is secondary with 2/2/4. These are mostly OK, given that the character seems to exist solely to kill and scream how how important it is that they kill. <br /> <br /> For Abilities, Talents are primary with four extra dots from freebies. Brawl is 4, naturally. (The only other character in this book with a 4 is the Supernatural Investigator with Enigmas.) Alertness and Streetwise are 3 each, with 2 each in Dodge, Intimidation, and Primal Urge, and 1 in Athletics. <br /> Skills are secondary, with a 3 in Melee, a 2 in Drive and Leadership, and 1 in Firearms and Stealth. <br /> Knowledge is tertiary, with 2 in Investigation, and 1 each in Enigmas, Law, and Occult. <br /> So, again, the character is here to fight and kill, and occasionally justify their killing or lead others in killing.<br /> (Given their backstory, I feel this missed an opportunity to do something mildly interesting by lifting a page from Batman and having the character completely shun firearms because they associate them with their parent's death.)<br /> <br /> For Backgrounds, we have 2 each in Contacts and Pure Breed, and 1 in Kinfolk. I presume the Kinfolk are other members of their father's side of the family, if not siblings. Not sure what the Contacts are. Maybe people from the old neighborhood?<br /> <br /> Rage is the default 5. Gnosis has been raised to 2 for some reason. Willpower is the default 4. I feel like those two points used for Gnosis could've been better spent on Willpower or possibly some Backgrounds. Maybe a Mentor to keep this character in check. <br /> <br /> I have mixed feelings about this character. One the one hand, I can certainly see the place for tribe members who take the Children of Gaia's self righteous idealism to extremes. And this character is that traditional idealistic sociopath who is going to build their idea of utopia on a giant pile of bodies. But at the same time, I just don't think it's a great representation of the Tribe or the Auspice, especially compared with some of the martial arts stuff I mention above and various philosophies like Morihei Ueshiba's The Art of Peace or Dan Miller's The Way of the Peaceful Warrior. So, it's not terrible, even if it is kind of one note, but I think there are a number of better ideas that could've been used here. <br /> <br /> And that's it for Children of Gaia. Overall, I think these were better than I remembered, but still not great. A lot of them suffer from poorly thought out character sheets. <br /> <br /> Next will be Fianna.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-09T07:01:21-08:00","id":1526554,"title":"","content":"As an artist, I got to say this is the UGLIEST glabro art I've seen. It has plains of empty space and the arms are oddly shaped.<br /> <br /> But to the character, as much as the Revised CoG Ahroun template of artistic dancer lupus gets mocked, it at least still tried to offer a more nuanced character. Because the spirit warrior is painfully one-note and wouldn't have much to do in play outside combat.<br /> <br /> Also, I think having a Coggie see aggression and take it to mean the world is violent and trying softer methods is pointless wouldn't get them picked by Unicorn if I was the ST. Because a more Coggie way to see the situation would be to track down the source of the shooters' pain and heal it or failing that, end them. If you are going for a tribe of compassion and healing, it cannot falter in face of violence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-09T10:20:43-08:00","id":1526558,"title":"","content":"This is my least favorite template of this tribebook. Somehow the character goes from rage and killing minions of the Wyrm to protect the innocent to anger at any Garou who won't &quot;cooperate&quot; with the other tribes. It seems like the writer was struggling with how to portray a Children of Gaia Ahroun and didn't know where to go. So we end up with some kind of psychopath who kills for &quot;peace&quot;. I understand wanting a CoG concept that goes against type, but this is not a success at doing that.<br /> <br /> Some kind of deranged killer who serves Unicorn because that's his people is a concept that can be interesting for an NPC I guess, but I think it's terrible for a PC. There's nothing for a player to do with this except snarl and KILL KILL KILL.<br /> <br /> In terms of mechanics, it is mostly OK though very limited. The high ranks of Streetwise indicate this is a concept mainly for a city based chronicle. Once again we have a character whose Willpower is less than his Rage, so the character will have penalties because of the Beast Within. Maybe that explains the character being a psycho, but it's a terrible design choice for a new player. Who wants all these penalties?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1526538#post1526538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, this character's father was a great Child of Gaia Kinfolk who worked in poverty stricken areas of a despairing city. Doing what exactly is not said. I feel like this should be at least mildly important. Was the father an inner city preacher? A lawyer doing pro bono work for those in need? A doctor running a clinic? He was murdered by &quot;Wyrm forces&quot;. Again, this is really vague, and feels like it should be important enough to be detailed. Murdered by corrupt land developers? A junkie desperate for money? Vampires?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am actually OK with this because I don't think the specifics matter so much for this concept, and this is something that can be easily customized by the player.<br /> <br /> Overall this is a terrible template. With a few exceptions, I think the character sheet is OK, just a trifle boring. But the character description is a complete mess. I just find it unappealing. It doesn't showcase being an Ahroun or a Children of Gaia well. Nothing about it makes me feel inspired. There's a few elements I feel are worthy of being explored, but they would each require a completely new write up in order to do them justice.<br /> <br /> All of the Children of Gaia tribebook templates are fairly weak and disappointing. White Wolf always seemed to know what they wanted to do with a tribe as a whole, but always struggled at an individual character level with how to portray them. Some of these templates have one or two features that are very strong and appealing, but the writer didn't know how to connect the dots and make a compelling rank one cliath that a player can pick up and run with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-09T11:03:28-08:00","id":1526561,"title":"","content":"I have this image in my head of this character being in a pack with the Bone Gnawer Vigilante Wolf and any future similar types as this gang of urban murder hobos who are constantly trying to out edge lord each other over who has the most tragic backstory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T02:22:54-08:00","id":1526587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1526561#post1526561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have this image in my head of this character being in a pack with the Bone Gnawer Vigilante Wolf and any future similar types as this gang of urban murder hobos who are constantly trying to out edge lord each other over who has the most tragic backstory.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tried this approach once. But I got a feeling that packs created like this had less social tensions. Now I rather create packs based on some area on which the cubs are born (either for my ST characters or PC packs, during the latter I encourage my players to create characters with different skills and ideals and sometimes they crash with other PCs during their lives) and then form a pack. Using this method I would propably get a pack formed by 2 Black Furies, Theurge and Gaillard (I'm talking about templates that you described), a Bone Gnawer Ragabash and CoG Ahroun. If I later let a pack like that meet Rite of Passage characters both packs would most likely split: Fury Gaillard would try form a band with Janet, BF Theurge would ask Snarl at Fleas to go with her away of the city and form a pack with wolves (not necessarily as alpha male and female which would propably end with them parking ways) and the rest would return to their normal lives; Curtis to being an ordinary teenager, Linda as pro bono lawyer and Ragabash and Ahroun templates forming a team, with Ragabash trying to convince Ahroun to concentrate his efforts on corporations with him as a scout. Whisperer, being left alone, would join BSD or join the Bone Gnawer and CoG. This would also add some roleplaying layer with them trying to convince the spirits and the septs that this approach is the right one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T02:28:59-08:00","id":1526588,"title":"","content":"I think No One of Consequence meant the edgy pack thing as a joke how dysfunctional and childishly edgy it would be.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T18:38:30-08:00","id":1526891,"title":"","content":"And now to late 1994 with <b>Fianna</b>. The book was written by Harry Heckel, and has a mildly notorious flaw of being focused very heavily on Ireland (especially Northern Ireland) and all but ignoring most other places with Celtic heritage. (Seriously, in the geographic section, Boston gets its own section that's the same size as the one for the rest of the US and larger than the ones for England or the rest of Continental Europe.) Overall, the book is very &quot;Oirish&quot; (see the TVTropes website's entry for Oirland). The worst part of this is the heavy focus on the Troubles (the long running religious/ethnic/nationalist conflict from the late 60s to the late 90s), including their Camps largely being presented as being totally focused on which modern nation they derive from (Ireland, Wales, Britain, Continental Europe). <br /> <br /> The art for the templates appears to be by Tony Diterlizzi. Overall, it's good work. However, he ended up being a major artist for Changeling, and you can certainly see the reason for that, as a lot of these have a look that feels more like Fae than Garou. I generally like his work, but I'm not sure it's the best fit for Werewolf. <br /> <br /> And we start off with ... (damn it)<br /> <br /> <b>Roving Ragabash</b> (Homid Ragabash)<br /> <br /> Back to the Camp + Auspice naming convention, as this is a member of the Whispering Rovers Camp. The Rovers were the &quot;Continental&quot; Fianna, meaning mainly French, but at the same time were heavily patterned after Irish Travelers/&quot;Walking People&quot; and essentially presented as Fianna versions of the The Rom (see Clanbook Gangrel). <br /> <br /> The character was orphaned at a young age and bounced around between different guardians until reaching an age where she could access their rather substantial inheritance. She immediately started spending the money on world travel without much of any real goal in life. Then came the First Change and being found by a young man with &quot;bright green eyes&quot; (because sure, why not?) who explained the Fianna, and overnight they changed from &quot;a little girl with too much money to a woman with goals and a reason for living.&quot; No idea if the guy was a werewolf or just Kinfolk. Anyway, now she pretty much does the same stuff she was doing before, traveling a lot and enjoying herself, but also using her money to fund her pack. About the only real change seems to be a better appreciation for how short life can be in light of having to fight the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> As far as role playing hints, we're told that she knows a lot of trivia, and usually just enough to get herself in trouble (which can be fun). She cares a lot about her pack mates, has had a lot of acquaintances but few friends, and enjoys spending money on people she cares about. <br /> <br /> Equipment is a cell phone (still essentially for upper class people in the early 90s), yacht, credit cards galore, and lots of clothes. <br /> <br /> The image is ... a man. Yeah, the write up is explicitly a woman, and the art is very much not. It's a generally normal looking guy in fairly upscale clothing. Also with pointy ears (the Changeling thing). On its own, it's a perfectly fine image, just perhaps more fitting for a Sidhe than a Fianna. But I can't help but wonder if it was inadvertently swapped with the Theurge one that follows it. <br /> <br /> As I said, the character is a Whispering Rover. Exactly why is not touched on in any form, save that they like to travel. And I presume are probably meant to be from France or something. <br /> <br /> For Attributes, Physicals are secondary, with 2/3/3. Socials are tertiary with an extra dot from freebies, for 3/2/2. Mental is primary, with 3/3/4. <br /> This seems backwards. While I can see an argument for Social vs Mental being primary, Social shouldn't be tertiary for this character. Just speaking for myself, I would have gone with 2/2/2 for Physical, 4/3/3 for Social and 3/2/3 for Mental. <br /> <br /> For Abilities, Talents are primary, with a 3 in Alertness, 2 each in Brawl, Dodge, and Streetwise, and 1 each in Athletics, Empathy, Intimidation, and Primal Urge. <br /> Skills are secondary, with 3 in Stealth, 2 in Survival, and 1 each in Drive, Etiquette, Melee, and Repair. <br /> Knowledge is tertiary with 3 in Linguistics and 1 each in Enigmas and Rituals. <br /> These feel a little all over the place, without much focus, and a few feel more like they were picked just to be useful in a standard Werewolf campaign. I would've expected higher ratings in Etiquette, and perhaps Expression as well. Also maybe something like Investigation or Law. <br /> <br /> Backgrounds is a 5 in Resources. This fits with the character and is kind of a nice change from the typical range of mostly broke werewolves we've seen so far. However, I think a few freebies spent on some Contacts or even a dot of Pure Breed wouldn't have been out of the question. <br /> <br /> They have an extra Gift, which eats up seven of sad freebies, all of which I feel could've been better spent on Abilities and Backgrounds.<br /> <br /> Rage is the default 1. Gnosis is raised to 2 and Willpower raised to 4. <br /> <br /> So, generally speaking, I like this character. Globetrotting Wealthy Heiress is a fun and fairly different idea for a Fianna character. The stats could be a bit better, but conceptually, it's pretty good. However, I have no clue why this character is a Ragabash. There's absolutely nothing here that says &quot;Questioner of the Ways&quot; or even &quot;Trickster&quot;. I think this would've worked a lot better as a Galliard, someone who expresses &quot;Lover of the Ways&quot; through a love of adventure and various cultures, of discovering new places and things, and of the bonds they build with their traveling companions. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-15T20:00:17-08:00","id":1526893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1526891#post1526891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And now to late 1994 with <b>Fianna</b>. The book was written by Harry Heckel, and has a mildly notorious flaw of being focused very heavily on Ireland (especially Northern Ireland) and all but ignoring most other places with Celtic heritage.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's definitely a big flaw. And besides the issue of limiting the Fianna to Ireland only and leaving out the other Celts, there's also the issue of neglecting Stag as the totem in general and imagining what the tribe would be like for non-Celts like lupus breed, or even homids prior to the emergence of the Celtic peoples. This unfortunately makes the book more about magical Irish people than a group of werewolves in cultic devotion to the Prince of the Forest.<br /> <br /> There's no problem with exploiting certain things about Irish culture. The tribe's capital is based in Ireland after all. And there are interesting things like the historical and folkloric fianna having a lot of wolf/outlaw imagery and poetry and tying that into the Garou. But it's unnecessarily limiting. This is a major problem with all the tribebooks. It's easy to understand why the initial writers heavily explored the human culture of a tribe's homid members - it's an obvious source to steal from when developing the tribes, but it was clearly a mistake. The Revised tribebooks would do a lot to expand away from too heavily specific human cultures, but overall they too neglected the aspect that all tribes would predate known human cultures and in origin would be just as lupus influenced as homid.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1526891#post1526891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back to the Camp + Auspice naming convention, as this is a member of the Whispering Rovers Camp.</div> </div> </div> </div>A major problem is that there's nothing about the character description that ties this to the Whispering Rovers. The description is actually about a rich jetsetting Garou homid, which is not what the camp is about. There's nothing tying this character to either the old continental Celts or that she's part of some wandering group of vagabonds. She's a rich heiress who likes to travel. Not the same thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1526891#post1526891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The image is ... a man. Yeah, the write up is explicitly a woman, and the art is very much not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's weird for the description to clearly describe a woman yet the picture be a man. This is just bad editing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1526891#post1526891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, generally speaking, I like this character. Globetrotting Wealthy Heiress is a fun and fairly different idea for a Fianna character. The stats could be a bit better, but conceptually, it's pretty good.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. It's not a traditional concept, but I think it works and could be a lot of fun to play. Despite some issues with how the template is written, I think the concept is great.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1526891#post1526891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, I have no clue why this character is a Ragabash. There's absolutely nothing here that says &quot;Questioner of the Ways&quot; or even &quot;Trickster&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's very little work done tying this into either the auspice or the tribe. This character could easily be transplanted to almost any tribe, and multiple auspices could fit. However, the Ragabash auspice works. As written, the template is a lot about having fun which is a trait heavily associated with the Ragabash. And someone jetsetting around the world is clearly not a traditional Garou or Fianna, so being a Ragabash lets her avoid a lot of possible Renown hits.<br /> <br /> While I agree it is nice to see extended development of the auspice and really explore the auspice, characters are much more than their auspice. They can embrace that role or reject it. Of all the auspices, the Ragabash has the most freedom to advance in rank however they choose so they are very open to developing in many ways. And the low Rage enables the Ragabash to fit in with humans which a Galliard would have trouble with.<br /> <br /> Other than randomly assigning this template to the Whispering Rovers, the lack of a real tie to the Fianna is more of a problem for me than the auspice. Not a deal breaker for the concept. Just as earlier said, you can use this for almost any tribe as written.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-16T00:06:45-08:00","id":1526904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1523773-wir-pre-made-werewolf-character-templates?p=1526893#post1526893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it's weird for the description to clearly describe a woman yet the picture be a man. This is just bad editing</div> </div> </div> </div>I added once a merit for 2 points called androgynous. Basically it was invented for female characters who can &quot;become&quot; a man or a man which can easily masquerade as a female. Of course it demanded some preparations but generally it allows you to imitate other sex as long as you don't fail a subterfuge test or roleplay. I got this idea when one of my buddies went to a store to buy some beer and returned with nothing because he forgot his I.D. It was during Halloween. Some time later people decided to make him a costume so girls put some make-up on him, placed two cue balls to the bra and so on. He went to the same store again and was served without any problem. Moreso some guys tried to pick him up and even brought the beer back for him because &quot;it's a shame that we guys let this beauty go alone and carry a case of beer&quot;. And I personally knew 2 guys with features delicate enough to do so. If I ever use this character I would use this merit again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 12-23-2023, 04:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-25T16:57:30-08:00","id":1527444,"title":"","content":"And, finally, continuing. (Had a lot going on the past week+ with work and Christmas prep.) <br /> <br /> <b>Fey Struck Garou </b>(Homid Theurge)<br /> <br /> I'm a little meh on calling a template &quot;Garou&quot;. It feels a bit non-descriptive. I feel like there are so many other words you could use here. Poet. Mystic. Dreamer. Just something that actually tells me more about the character. I mean, I know its a werewolf already. Tell me something more. <br /> <br /> So, apparently as a child this character encountered the Fey. Or at least thinks they did. And became a bit obsessed about the whole thing. Exactly what they did about this obsession isn't exactly clear. Study fairy legends? Constantly investigate strange and mysterious places? No idea. Eventually they stumbled across werewolves, and learned that they were one. <br /> <br /> They're described as a perpetual dreamer, someone who doesn't really want to grow up, and who notices odd things. But also they don't really pay attention to other people, people wrapped up in their own obsession. And tend to presume &quot;faerie&quot; explanations for things regardless if it's true or not. They've visited the Arcadian Gateway realm and want to go back, and believe that the power of the Fey will give the tribe the power to defeat the Wyrm and Weaver and save Gaia. <br /> <br /> Equipment is a four leaf clover, a map of local ley lines, and a well worn copy of A Midsummer Night's Dream. <br /> <br /> The image is, again because of the artist's style being so heavily associated with Changeling, looking more of a character from that game rather than one from Werewolf. But it is a very nice image. A very tall and petite female, in what might be taken as a cross between Victorian-esque clothing and mid-90s club wear. It's a cool look, but again, feels maybe a little more Changeling (or even Mage Hollow One) than Werewolf. <br /> <br /> The character is part of the Tuatha de Fionn camp. Apparently just because of the fey connection. <br /> <br /> For Attributes, Physicals are tertiary with one extra dot from freebies, for a 2/3/2 spread. Socials are (apparently) primary, but are missing a dot, for a 3/2/4 spread. That leaves Mental as secondary, with 3/3/2.<br /> <br /> I've no idea where that missing dot might've meant to go. Maybe Charisma, but there's not much in the description to indicate the character is especially charismatic. Or manipulative. And the high Appearance also feels kind of random. Like they just didn't know what else to do or perhaps that the art came in and they just decided the character was now a super attractive female. <br /> I feel like, as is, this character might benefit from having Mental as primary, with a high Perception to reflect the idea that they notice (odd) things that others frequently don't, and maybe high Wits in the tradition of certain types of folklore characters. <br /> <br /> For Abilities, Talents are secondary with two extra dots from freebies. Expression is 3. Alertness and Empathy are 2 each. And 1 each in Athletics, Brawl, Dodge, and Primal Urge.<br /> Skills are tertiary with a 2 in Stealth and 1 each in Animal Ken, Performance, and Survival. <br /> Knowledge is primary with one extra dot from freebies. Enigmas is 4, and Linguistics, Occult, and Rituals are 3 each. Then there's a single dot in Investigation. <br /> While I can understand the focus on the Knowledges, I feel like the rest is maybe a little unfocused. While this would fit a sort of aimless dreamer (which is what the rather sparse character description leaves the impression of), it feels like something is missing. <br /> <br /> Backgrounds are 3 in Past Life and 2 in Rituals (with the rituals being written out individually). This seems fine, for the most part. Although I think this is a character that might benefit from a Mentor. Maybe also a Fetish tied to the Arcadia Gateway or some Contacts. <br /> <br /> Rage is the default 2, Gnosis is raised to 3 with freebies, and Willpower is the default 3. <br /> <br /> There just really isn't a lot here with this character. I get the idea of a character who (apparently) encountered the Fey at a young age and never really got over it, but beyond that, there just isn't much of anything beyond a sort of vague day dreamer. This just sort of feels like an obligatory Fey related character because the tribe is Celtic (Oirish) and so has to have ties to the Little People. It feels like you could do a lot more with a Fianna Seeker of the Ways. The previous wealthy world traveler would have worked here as someone constantly wandering the world looking for things to help the tribe and the Garou nation. <br /> <br /> Hopefully have the next one up in the next few days. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-25T19:50:26-08:00","id":1527449,"title":"","content":"I want to like the Fey Struck Garou template, but there's not much to it. So much of Werewolf concepts involving the fae depends on the Changeling game (which at time of the first Fianna tribebook might still have been advertised as just &quot;Faeire&quot;), and there is so little in the game that supports it. If I remember correctly, in the first Umbra sourcebook the Arcadia Gateway was supposed to actually lead to Arcadia which was very likely to incorporate a lot of Ars Magica lore. But the World of Darkness went into an entirely different direction and stranded a lot of Werewolf concepts like this which were to rely on it.<br /> <br /> So while a concept like this hints at a lot of crossover goodies, in reality it is just a dead end that would require a lot of creative work by the ST to turn into anything useful. There's just not enough support for a template like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-26T17:39:42-08:00","id":1527472,"title":"","content":"Yeah. There's just nothing really there besides &quot;I like faeries.&quot; <br /> <br /> I think this is one that might've been stronger if done as a different auspice. Maybe a Philodox that is a negotiator with the various Fey courts and groups they've encountered, or a Galliard who is a modern day bard focused on retelling stories of the Fey and trying to coax them back into the modern world.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-29T17:44:45-08:00","id":1527615,"title":"","content":"<b>Black Rose</b> (Metis Philodox)<br /> <br /> So, the black rose tends to be a symbol of mourning, mystery, loss, and elegance, as well as major changes like death and rebirth. <br /> <br /> This character is the child of a Fianna mother and a father of some other tribe. Apparently she was teased as a child that her father was a Bone Gnawer, but didn't care because she believed her parents loved each other. Her mother raised her and taught her the Litany and the Silver Record, and how to &quot;sing and howl&quot;. Her deformity is blindness, which &quot;haunts her everyday&quot; even though she's learned to compensate. <br /> <br /> She has a strong sense of self and where she comes from, as well as powerful Past Lives. (Keep this in mind; it will come up later.) Her blindness &quot;makes a fun joke&quot; as she can't see all the suffering of the world. She travels and sings like all Song Keepers (she's a member of that camp, but nothing is said about how or why she joined, or what else she does among them). She hopes to one day fall in love like her mother did. Her favorite story is Cuchulain and Emer, because naturally the Fianna are all about human Irish mythology and not any of the stories of the Garou. No word on what her favorite food or color is. <br /> <br /> Roleplaying hints are that she carries herself with pride to cover for her insecurity about being a blind Metis. She loves being a Song Keeper and finds a beauty poetry and songs that nothing can take away. <br /> <br /> We get a paragraph about her blindness and optional rules for using her sense of smell to compensate, which is interesting. <br /> <br /> Equipment is a flute and rose colored glasses. I presume the latter is supposed to be a joke of some sort. <br /> <br /> The image is, again, a very nice one. A young woman with long hair and little round glasses in a dress holding a musical instrument which I am not knowledgable enough about the properly identify. As I said, it's a very nice image, but much like the previous two, it really feels much more like it is an image of a Changeling character (or possibly even a vampire or a mage) rather than a werewolf. <br /> <br /> For Attributes, Physicals are tertiary, with a 1/3/2 spread. I'm not sure why this character should be so physically weak, baring some sort of lithe female musician stereotype. Socials are primary, with 4/3/3. Mental is secondary with an extra dot from freebies, for 3s across the board. <br /> <br /> With Abilities, Talents are tertiary with two extra dots from freebies. 3 in Primal Urge, 2 in Expression, and 1 each Brawl and Empathy. I'm just going to presume that actually Brawling requires someone to actually grapple with her. And I'm kind of surprised by the lack of Alertness. That feels like it would be an important part of compensating/coping with blindness. Really, I think the only reason Primal Urge is so high is because the bit about coping with deformity via her sense of smell involves Perception + Primal Urge rolls. Also, given the way the character is described, I'd sort of expect her Expression and Empathy to be a little higher.<br /> Skills are secondary, with a 3 in Performance and a wide spread of 1s in Animal Ken, Etiquette, Firearms (?), Leadership, Stealth, and Survival. OK, I'll ask the obvious question here: Why does a blind character have the Firearms skill? Maybe this is the world's subtlest reference to that scene with Ray Charles in the Blues Brothers movie. And a lot of these skills seem kind of random. I think a higher Etiquette and maybe also Leadership would benefit this character. <br /> This leaves Knowledge as primary. 3 each in Linguistics, Occult, and Rituals, and 2 each in Enigmas and Law. Honestly, this Law bit is about the first thing I've seen that fits the Auspice. <br /> <br /> For Backgrounds, she has 2 in Allies and 3 in Mentor (her mother). I do like that we get some info on who the Mentor is. I wish more templates did that. I also wish this template had done the same with Allies. <br /> I mentioned earlier than the character write up says she has a powerful Past Life. Except that she doesn't. None of that Background whatsoever. (Or Pure Breed, or Kinfolk, or anything else that might contribute to that strong sense of self and where she comes from.) <br /> <br /> Seven freebies have been spent on a fourth Gift. I really feel that those freebies could've been better spent on Backgrounds or Abilities. <br /> <br /> Rage and Gnosis are both the default 3. Willpower has been raised to 5 with freebies. <br /> For those keeping track, that means five freebies for Attributes, four for Abilities, seven for Gifts, and two for WP, for a total of eighteen. So, just from a numerical perspective, this template is broken. <br /> <br /> Much like the previous one, there just isn't a lot here. The character is blind and a singer/musician. And a romantic. And that's about it. There's nothing really here that conveys Keeper of the Ways. Not really even the low hanging fruit of a character born from breaking the Litany now ironically tasked with upholding it. Really, this character feels more like a Galliard/Lover of the Ways. Someone who dearly loves music and stories - especially love stories - and her family and wants to share that love with others. <br /> I think there's a lot that could have been done here, but just wasn't. At the very least, I think getting rid of the extra Gift and sorting out the Abilities would go a ways toward helping. Perhaps make Talents secondary or primary so that you have the dots to put in Alertness as well as Primal Urge, Empathy, and Expression (maybe even a little Subterfuge). <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-29T23:35:21-08:00","id":1527620,"title":"","content":"The Black Rose is actually my favorite template of the first Fianna tribebook. I have an inordinate fondness for it. She's definitely not a combat character, which is unusual for a Garou, but I feel is very much an early World of Darkness trend to open up roleplaying to other play styles. I don't think she makes a good PC. But she would be a great NPC as the ST could explore a lot of things which a PC likely wouldn't. I think very few players would ever want to roleplay a character who is blind, even given the lupus form's scent abilities.<br /> <br /> She's not a standard Philodox, but is very much in the keeping of the Fianna interpretation of &quot;Songkeeper&quot; which unfortunately is not adequately explained or distinguished from the Galliard. &quot;Songkeepers&quot; in fact are mentioned as a &quot;camp&quot; of the Galliards, and I wonder if this character in fact was originally intended for that auspice. I think she can be easily seen as Philodox as someone who PRESERVES the songs/traditions of the past. But the Fianna overall always seems a tribe heavily associated with Galliad concepts. This should be made explicit though in order to distinguish her from a Galliard. She's a very positive depiction of a Metis, and I think the template is stronger for that. So many other examples are just incredibly negative. It's a good distinction.<br /> <br /> The description mentions Past Lives (Ancestors), but the character sheet does not mention them. Further proof that these may have been given to two different people.<br /> <br /> Overall, I have a much more positive assessment of this template than <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> . I see a lot of potential here even with all the normal caveats that the mechanics should be improved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-29T23:52:01-08:00","id":1527621,"title":"","content":"There are aspects of this character that work and some which don't. One of them is how pretty she is and how she is a member of a camp. The Fianna are the worst tribe for garou born, even the 1st tribebook states that having a KIN in a pack would be better than a garou born. A cliath garou born would have no chance to join a camp or even look so dignified. The revised tribebook's Mule in Black does a much better job at depicting a garou born among the Fianna.<br /> <br /> One thing that DOES work is that she doesn't do her philodox duties, because no way would she be able to among the Fianna.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-30T08:21:38-08:00","id":1527628,"title":"","content":"I think this is a character that really would have benefited from the revised era Academics or the early Mage Culture ability. Or even maybe the History, Literature, and/or Anthropology ones from the Vampire player guides. It would have helped give this some better focus as a Keeper of history, tradition, and culture. <br /> <br /> I don't really object to non-combat characters. I think a highly Social character works perfectly fine with a tribe like the Fianna. I still have no idea why anyone decided that Firearms should be one of her two combat abilities. (I probably would have focused on Dodge, having that be tied to her lifelong adaption to her blindness.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-30T16:20:43-08:00","id":1527643,"title":"","content":"The description of firearms skill says it includes also the ability to repair them. So as it's hard for me to imagine this character actually firing the gun I can imagine it fixing them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-30T06:45:26-08:00","id":1529708,"title":"","content":"I just wanted to pop in and say that stumbling onto this thread* was a key reason for my registering with these forums: I\u2019d like to thank everyone who contributes for that and send my Best Wishes for your being able to continue it as time &amp; opportunity allows.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>*Believe it or not I was on a search for more information about the Pregenerated PCs for RITE OF PASSAGE (By the way, Whisper <u>is</u> a tricky character, but I like to think that a dot in Totem on any character sheet represents a desire and a willingness to be part of something better: this would suggest that the character regards the possibility of walking the Black Spiral with dread, rather than anticipation, even before being offered an infinitely preferable alternative in the form of his new pack).<br /> <br /> I like to think of them as the \u2018Friends of Bill\u2019 pack (Not least because it amuses me to imagine the artist-formerly-known-as-Whisper piping up \u201cI\u2019m Bill\u201d, possibly in chorus with Snaps-at-Fleas, when somebody poses the obvious question after the new pack pick their Totem - Bear, obviously - and their name)</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}